{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously","id":847552,"title":"Removing Touchstones (or at least downplaying them tremendously)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-14T22:38:31-07:00","id":847552,"title":"Removing Touchstones (or at least downplaying them tremendously)","content":"I've been running a game for a couple of months now, and I have been noticing that, well, touchstones just aren't a thing. Everyone picked a touchstone at creation, of course, and we talked a lot about who would be a given character's touchstone and why, but, there has been zero interaction whatsoever between any of the PCs and their touchstones, except for the PC who chose his dog and made him a retainer (I never liked that one from the start, honestly, felt like cheating to make it both useful and effective in game, and a non-human to boot) and the circumstances of what they've been doing would make it truly odd and obviously forced for their touchstones to come to them.<br /> <br /> It could be the circumstances of the game we are playing in particular. The first session covered the PC's very first night as vampires, for example, and only about a week of in-game time has passed over, I would estimate, 10-12 sessions, rather than having characters who have already established themselves as vampires for several years before the start of a game, and making liberal use of time elapses as it seems is the norm.<br /> <br /> Frankly, having seen it in play, now, I'm wondering how, exactly, a freshly awoken vampire's touchstones first develop, how long they have to form a bond before they start feeling the penalties, etc., but rather than make that stuff up, my group and I discussed it, and we'd just like to downplay touchstones significantly. I said that if the PCs actually make a real connection to an NPC such that it's obviously a touchstone, I will still allow <i>some </i>of the touchstone mechanics to apply. They can get willpower from defending them and their touchstones can ignore their Nosferatu penalties or talk them down from frenzy, but they don't get a +2/+3/-2 to detachment rolls regardless, and I am not going to charge merit dots or tie them to Humanity lines or anything, either. It'll basically be a lot more hand wavy, and less hard coded, &quot;You better have some touchstones or else!&quot;<br /> <br /> Which brings me to my main problem: the Ventrue clan bane. I have to admit, I was already unhappy with it. &quot;You lose 1 XP more than a member of another clan at the same humanity, until you're borderline unplayable at 1 humanity anyway&quot; just doesn't have the same, well, <i>anything</i>, that the other clans get. I actually liked the old Ventrue flaw and thought it to be the best one of the bunch, but here, in the new edition, they fix everything up, make all the flaws better (Mekhet went from the lamest, basically non-flaw, to the most interesting!), and kind of drop the ball on the previous best.<br /> <br /> My stop gap solution is simple: -1 to detachment rolls, and on a detachment roll dramatic failure, gain a 1st edition style derangement (in addition to the jaded condition and other effects).<br /> <br /> However, I was wondering a few things. First, does anyone have some other ideas for a good Ventrue flaw? I read quite a few threads complaining about it, but the majority of the fixes I saw also tied into the Touchstone system, which, obviously, is something I do not want. Is what I outlined above a decent flaw? I did -1 because I figured -2 would be too severe (the die pools basically range from 1-4 with maybe a few bonus or penalties based on circumstances), but there have been very few detachment rolls so far (is it me or is the 2nd edition chart ridiculously more forgiving?). The derangement is mostly for flavor and fun rather than balance--I figured it wouldn't ever come up unless someone purposefully wanted one or they were already fairly low humanity committing fairly terrible acts, probably with one or more Banes in play.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else ever done a Blood and Smoke/2nd edition game downplaying/removing touchstones like this? How did it work out? What did you have to adjust that, maybe, I'm not thinking of, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  typo 03-15-2016, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T00:06:42-07:00","id":847566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously#post847552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been running a game for a couple of months now, and I have been noticing that, well, touchstones just aren't a thing. Everyone picked a touchstone at creation, of course, and we talked a lot about who would be a given character's touchstone and why, but, there has been zero interaction whatsoever between any of the PCs and their touchstones, except for the PC who chose his dog and made him a retainer (I never liked that one from the start, honestly, felt like cheating to make it both useful and effective in game, and a non-human to boot) and the circumstances of what they've been doing would make it truly odd and obviously forced for their touchstones to come to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, my initial reaction here was &quot;So why are their Touchstones still attached?&quot;, but after reading further, it seems like the problem you're having is stemming more from the fact that, as you mention, your characters are all recently embraced neonates. I'll address those circumstances more specifically later in this post, but first I just wanted to comment on this point in a more general sense, outside the context of your game's unique concerns. Cause the thing is, even if your characters had all been around longer and were more entrenched in vampire society, Touchstones aren't going to fit naturally in the flow of what the characters will generally be getting up to. This is a feature, not a bug. The point of Touchstones is to give vampires an anchor to humanity (that's small-h &quot;the human race&quot;, not big-H stat on the character sheet). Keeping connected to a normal mortal, with a mortal life, and mortal problems is <i>hard</i> for a vampire. They really have to go out of their way to maintain a relationship with someone who, quite frankly, doesn't fit into their unlife. It would be far more convenient to just ignore them and go about your business doing vampire things without having to check in on your human friend every once in a while. But if you do that, you lose the one person in your life who still reminds you of what it means to be human, and as a result, it's much harder to keep a grip on Humanity (that's the capital H kind there). A vampire should always be torn between the needs of their Coterie and the needs of their Touchstones. And if they chose to prioritize the Coterie, those Touchstones should become detached. That's all part of the drama of Vampire the Requiem.<br /> <br /> Side-note: Yeah, I wouldn't have allowed a dog as a Touchstone. Making them a Retainer could be interesting, but a dog is definitely not going to anchor you to the human experience. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously#post847552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be the circumstances of the game we are playing in particular. The first session covered the PC's very first night as vampires, for example, and only about a week of in-game time has passed over, I would estimate, 10-12 sessions, rather than having characters who have already established themselves as vampires for several years before the start of a game, and making liberal use of time elapses as it seems is the norm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, the particular circumstances of your game are definitely going to make Touchstones seem less important. If your characters were all recently embraced, they probably don't yet need to maintain a relationship with a human to remind them what it was like to be alive - after all it was only a week or so ago. The default rules kind of assume that the characters have been vampires long enough to at least gain 3 dots of Disciplines, 3 dots of Merits, and to drop to Humanity 7. If you're playing characters who were embraced that recently, I would also start them at Humanity 10, because they shouldn't yet be used to things like lying in defense of the Masquerade, going over a day without human contact, possessing superhuman abilities, and using those abilities to steal the lifeblood of the unwilling, or to deprive them of the agency to attest their unwillingness. That's valuable stuff to play through if you're starting that early. Don't bother with Touchstones yet, have the players acquire them in-game, at a time when it feels dramatically appropriate. When they start forgetting things like the feeling of a sunburn, the rhythm of a heartbeat, and why exactly they're supposed to care about consent. When they start to experience that cognitive dissonance of &quot;wait... I should feel guilty about this. Why don't I feel guilty about this?&quot; that's when it's time to find a human you can confide in and who can serve as an example of what humans are like and why that's important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously#post847552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, having seen it in play, now, I'm wondering how, exactly, a freshly awoken vampire's touchstones first develop, how long they have to form a bond before they start feeling the penalties, etc., but rather than make that stuff up, my group and I discussed it, and we'd just like to downplay touchstones significantly. I said that if the PCs actually make a real connection to an NPC such that it's obviously a touchstone, I will still allow <i>some </i>of the touchstone mechanics to apply. They can get willpower from defending them and their touchstones can ignore their Nosferatu penalties or talk them down from frenzy, but they don't get a +2/+3/-2 to detachment rolls regardless, and I am not going to charge merit dots or tie them to Humanity lines or anything, either. It'll basically be a lot more hand wavy, and less hard coded, &quot;You better have some touchstones or else!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. It's not the way I would go with it, as I think that would be a really fun time in a character's life to play thorough, but if you and your group have talked it over and decided that downplaying Touchstones is what's going to serve your needs best, more power to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously#post847552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings me to my main problem: the Ventrue clan bane. I have to admit, I was already unhappy with it. &quot;You lose 1 XP more than a member of another clan at the same humanity, until you're borderline unplayable at 1 humanity anyway&quot; just doesn't have the same, well, <i>anything</i>, that the other clans get. I actually liked the old Ventrue flaw and thought it to be the best one of the bunch, but here, in the new edition, they fix everything up, make all the flaws better (Mekhet went from the lamest, basically non-flaw, to the most interesting!), and kind of drop the ball on the previous best.</div> </div> </div> </div>This point has been talked to death, so I won't dwell on it. I'll just say that the intention is for it to be a very roleplay-heavy Bane, not a mechanics-heavy one. As I mentioned in my first paragraph, keeping Touchstones is supposed to be hard work, and it's supposed to regularly drag you away from what ever else is going on at the time. In my experience, it's actually the harshest Clan Bane, not because of the 1exp tax, but because of the work that has to be done to obtain a new Touchstone. Of course, since your plan is to downplay the role of Touchstones for your game, it'll definitely be a non-flaw and need to be replaced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously#post847552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My stop gap solution is simple: -1 to detachment rolls, and on a detachment roll dramatic failure, gain a 1st edition style derangement (in addition to the jaded condition and other effects).<br /> <br /> However, I was wondering a few things. First, does anyone have some other ideas for a good Ventrue flaw? I read quite a few threads complaining about it, but the majority of the fixes I saw also tied into the Touchstone system, which, obviously, is something I do not want. Is what I outlined above a decent flaw? I did -1 because I figured -2 would be too severe (the die pools basically range from 1-4 with maybe a few bonus or penalties based on circumstances), but there have been very few detachment rolls so far (is it me or is the 2nd edition chart ridiculously more forgiving?). The derangement is mostly for flavor and fun rather than balance--I figured it wouldn't ever come up unless someone purposefully wanted one or they were already fairly low humanity committing fairly terrible acts, probably with one or more Banes in play.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else ever done a Blood and Smoke/2nd edition game downplaying/removing touchstones like this? How did it work out? What did you have to adjust that, maybe, I'm not thinking of, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... -1 seems pretty weak to me honestly, and if you're going to be giving derangements, I would recommend converting them into Conditions so the player can at least get Beats from them. I also don't really like the whole &quot;Ventrue go crazy more easily than other vampires&quot; thing. It's kind of dull in my opinion, and doesn't really fit the Clan's theme of lordship. Since Touchstones are out, I'd give them like a permanent (or at least recurring) Condition representing their drive to have power over others, and have it scale inversely with Humanity.<br /> <br /> Another side-note: 2e Humanity probably seems less harsh in part because Breaking Points are now caused by doing things that most humans can't or won't do, instead of things that are considered evil by an arbitrary standard, and in part because the list of Breaking Points is not meant to be exhaustive, it's just examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T01:17:04-07:00","id":847577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847566#post847566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side-note: Yeah, I wouldn't have allowed a dog as a Touchstone. Making them a Retainer could be interesting, but a dog is definitely not going to anchor you to the human experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree about the dog part as well, to add to this:<br /> <br /> Having Touchstones that are also other Merits is a great way to incorporate them into a game in a different fashion than the default as Charlaquin went over. Especially for a newly Embraced style game like this, where the characters are still very fresh to the stresses of unlife, the option besides downplaying Touchstones is to have them be True Friend/Mentor/Retainer/etc. Merits as well. Thus the players have an incentive to pull them into play, as the struggle to balance those relationships and being vampires can grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T10:13:01-07:00","id":847752,"title":"","content":"You could give the Venture a variant on the Lethargic Condition based on the success or failure of the detachment roll that kicks in any time they make a make a detachment roll that persists for a number of weeks based on their Humanity score.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T14:58:25-07:00","id":847881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847566#post847566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping connected to a normal mortal, with a mortal life, and mortal problems is <i>hard</i> for a vampire. They really have to go out of their way to maintain a relationship with someone who, quite frankly, doesn't fit into their unlife. It would be far more convenient to just ignore them and go about your business doing vampire things without having to check in on your human friend every once in a while. But if you do that, you lose the one person in your life who still reminds you of what it means to be human, and as a result, it's much harder to keep a grip on Humanity (that's the capital H kind there). A vampire should always be torn between the needs of their Coterie and the needs of their Touchstones. And if they chose to prioritize the Coterie, those Touchstones should become detached. That's all part of the drama of Vampire the Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the overarching issue is definitely the time frame thing, where the PCs are too new to have formed real bonds. However, I don't think I like touchstones very much regardless. So, ok, first, your words were very cool and made touchstones sound great. In fact, every time I read about touchstones, I think, &quot;that is a great idea,&quot; and every time I think about how they'd actually be implemented at the table, I think, &quot;ugh, never mind.&quot;<br /> <br /> Let's say your vampire has Bob, his old roomate from college, as his touchstone. So, once a week, say, you and Bob catch up for an hour or something. Maybe your tradition was bowling, so, the table options are:<br /> <br /> You: &quot;I go hang out with Bob. We go bowling.&quot;<br /> Everyone at the table is bored to tears as you and the GM have a conversation, mostly about nonsense, that has nothing to do with the rest of the game whatsoever.<br /> Touchstone interrupts and suckifies the game for a while.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> You: &quot;I go hang out with Bob. We go bowling.&quot;<br /> GM: &quot;Ok, you do that. It's fun. He and Christine are in a rough patch, but the [sports team he likes] are on a winning streak. What does everyone else do for a couple of hours? Feed? Hang out with their touchstones?&quot;<br /> Everyone kind of rolls their eyes at this pointless &quot;obligation minute,&quot; because they know it's silly, but they don't want a 4 die swing on their detachment rolls.<br /> Touchstone is successfully glossed over, which diminishes its value as a roleplaying tool.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> GM: &quot;Your touchstone is in trouble!&quot;<br /> Everyone sighs. It's super forced and obvious--this does not fit into the game whatsoever, but, it's necessary to give this mechanic that, othewise just suckifies the game or gets glossed over teeth. And everyone knows their turn will come as these random people have bad shit happen to them, not because they know a vampire, but because they know a PC and interesting stuff has to happen to them in order to keep the mechanic interesting and worthwhile.<br /> <br /> I don't know, I'm just not a fan of that. Touchstones work in theory--they work when talking about the game. It works great in other media--how many times do the heroes have a scene with an otherwise uninvolved person (their family, or a mentor or something), and achieve some kind of insight into the current plot from them? But, that only works for two reasons: everything, from the problem, to the lucky lesson learned from an old friend, is scripted (and, in my opinion, nothing should be in a roleplaying game), and because the other protagonists aren't sitting around a table watching this one character get his insight, waiting for their turn to do something.<br /> <br /> So, the short version is, I don't think I would like Touchstones even if my game didn't have special circumstances. Though, my mind is definitely changeable on that front. How have they worked at the actual table for others? Like, not just a flower prose version like you get in &quot;actual play&quot; posts, the real version, where solo scenes are full of side comments and bored groans from other players.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847566#post847566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side-note: Yeah, I wouldn't have allowed a dog as a Touchstone. Making them a Retainer could be interesting, but a dog is definitely not going to anchor you to the human experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could tell right away the players weren't really buying into the touchstone system. Every single one of them grasped desperately on the one line or two mentioning that places or items could be touchstones, too. I had to veto a car (&quot;But you don't understand! I worked on that with my dad, so it connects me to him!&quot; &quot;Is your dad dead?&quot; &quot;No.&quot; &quot;Then why isn't your dad the touchstone?&quot;), an apartment, an urn, even an ancestral daisho from the former Yakuza hitman. The dog finally broke me down, since it was at least alive and, well, the guy made an eloquent argument about his character not bonding with any humans in his life anyway. And, to his credit, the dog is the only touchstone that's seen play--he immediately went to retrieve him, and he's spent more time with him than without post embrace, so, I don't totally regret it even though it still feels kind of cheaty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847566#post847566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're playing characters who were embraced that recently, I would also start them at Humanity 10, because they shouldn't yet be used to things like lying in defense of the Masquerade, going over a day without human contact, possessing superhuman abilities, and using those abilities to steal the lifeblood of the unwilling, or to deprive them of the agency to attest their unwillingness.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of overboard, I think. It was always my impression that Humanity above 7 was literally more human than a normal human. Like, you became a caricature of humanity. I get that scene from Invader Zim in my head, &quot;I eat food, just like you. I HAVE A STOMACH!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847566#post847566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's valuable stuff to play through if you're starting that early. Don't bother with Touchstones yet, have the players acquire them in-game, at a time when it feels dramatically appropriate. When they start forgetting things like the feeling of a sunburn, the rhythm of a heartbeat, and why exactly they're supposed to care about consent. When they start to experience that cognitive dissonance of &quot;wait... I should feel guilty about this. Why don't I feel guilty about this?&quot; that's when it's time to find a human you can confide in and who can serve as an example of what humans are like and why that's important.<br /> <br /> That's fair. It's not the way I would go with it, as I think that would be a really fun time in a character's life to play thorough, but if you and your group have talked it over and decided that downplaying Touchstones is what's going to serve your needs best, more power to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's surprising to me that this is not the default way to play. In almost 20 years of running various vampire games, I've started at least 90% of them with freshly embraced vampires. I don't think I would really enjoy pre-established characters quite as much.<br /> <br /> For one, starting fresh gives you &quot;straight men&quot; to explain the setting with (in most fantasy, including the urban variety, or sci fi, the main characters deal with someone or themselves are, not familiar with the world, allowing the authors to explain things during the show/book/movie/etc. to the audience without breaking the 4th wall--it's Fry from Futurama, or John Crichton in Farscape). The players don't know anything about how the city works because their characters don't, either, so, they can discover it together in play. Otherwise, I'd have to infodump them some kind of massive document about how the city works and what things are like before the game started, and I'd have a player riot that they have to do homework before the game.<br /> <br /> Secondly, it requires a much more, I guess, &quot;active&quot; GM style than I prefer. It means that the GM is providing the destabilizing force that's driving the events of the game. It makes the PCs more reactive than proactive. They're not doing things on their own, they're just acting in response to something else, like in a typical super hero game, or a railroady quest in a D&amp;D adventure path. I much prefer the PCs to be the destabilizing factors. Otherwise, I always have to ask, &quot;how did the PCs not mess with stuff like this years ago? How did none of them have any chance to see this coming or prepare or, whatever?&quot; With fresh embraces, they're what drives the game, not offscreen threats. I just prefer more reactive GMing and proactive players, rather than the other way around. Yes, I recognize that this was a bit of a tangent, but I am also curious about how this is normally done at the table, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847566#post847566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This point has been talked to death, so I won't dwell on it. I'll just say that the intention is for it to be a very roleplay-heavy Bane, not a mechanics-heavy one. As I mentioned in my first paragraph, keeping Touchstones is supposed to be hard work, and it's supposed to regularly drag you away from what ever else is going on at the time. In my experience, it's actually the harshest Clan Bane, not because of the 1exp tax, but because of the work that has to be done to obtain a new Touchstone. Of course, since your plan is to downplay the role of Touchstones for your game, it'll definitely be a non-flaw and need to be replaced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see it as a serious roleplaying problem, either, though. It isn't any different than what other PCs go through--it just happens one humanity earlier. That's it. Still feels kind of weak. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847566#post847566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... -1 seems pretty weak to me honestly</div> </div> </div> </div>I was concerned. By taking away the +2 from touchstones that most people have, I didn't want to totally screw Ventrue over on detachment and go for a full -2. I mean, the base values for these things goes from 0-3 dice (since the curse wouldn't even apply if they had 7 Humanity and were thus subject to 4 dice detachments). Given that you can maybe get a +1 from circumstances like frenzy or upholding masks/requiems/virtues or whatever, -2 would be seriously steep.<br /> <br /> The chances to succeed on 1 die are only 30%. On two, it's 51%. Three is 65.7%, and four is roughly 76%. -1 is a pretty rough penalty in that light. Most of the things that are likely to cause detachment are in the 2 die range, so, you're looking at a -20% or so chance to succeed, or -15% with mitigating circumstances. A -2 would be brutal, dropping you to a chance die on most common situations, meaning you better have mitigating circumstances or you're screwed. I certainly wouldn't want to play a Ventrue with that big a flaw. You'd be left with &quot;strictly adhere to the chart or you will be falling fast and hard.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847566#post847566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">, and if you're going to be giving derangements, I would recommend converting them into Conditions so the player can at least get Beats from them. I also don't really like the whole &quot;Ventrue go crazy more easily than other vampires&quot; thing. It's kind of dull in my opinion, and doesn't really fit the Clan's theme of lordship. Since Touchstones are out, I'd give them like a permanent (or at least recurring) Condition representing their drive to have power over others, and have it scale inversely with Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I will be treating them like Conditions--that's basically the 2nd edition version of such permanent problems. That said, the beat stuff is much less relevant to me and my group. I started out running with group beats, because I absolutely will not run or play a game with uneven character advancement, but quickly noticed that it required a truly immense amount of stuff happening each session to push the pool up high enough to give even just 2 beats to everyone, nevermind 3 or more, so, I just kind of stopped tracking them exactly, and just giving 2-4 beats each session based on how much happened and got accomplished. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847566#post847566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another side-note: 2e Humanity probably seems less harsh in part because Breaking Points are now caused by doing things that most humans can't or won't do, instead of things that are considered evil by an arbitrary standard, and in part because the list of Breaking Points is not meant to be exhaustive, it's just examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that, but it still feels ridiculously lenient. Most of the &quot;do stuff humans can't do&quot; is of the variety that the PCs will (1) never engage in (2) technically constantly engaging in, which would make for a sucky game as they basically roll detachment every day until they fall or (3) things the GM has to force on the party in a heavy handed fashion, since the entire purpose would clearly be to force the detachment roll.<br /> <br /> Example: watching a human eat a meal. Unless you are a stickler pointing out that people are constantly eating all over and it's impossible to even walk down the street before midnight without seeing someone in a window or at a food cart or something, it's something no vampire is ever going to do. Why would you go and watch knowing it's going to hurt your humanity? So, the only way it's going to happen is if the GM forces a situation where they are made to watch someone eat (you have to meet with this ghoul at a restaurant), and that's going to come across shitty and obvious that it's just to make the PCs roll detachment.<br /> <br /> The new chart allows for quite a bit more casual violence, as long as people don't die, and makes feeding super easy, again, as long as nobody dies. In Masquerade and 1st edition, my PCs would routinely drop, fairly quickly, to the 3-5 range before stabilizing, but with this new chart, in a dozen sessions, there have only been two detachment rolls, and both were for feeding when starving, frenzying, and killing the victim by accident. Both succeeded, too, so, I have what I never thought possible: an entire coterie of Humanity 7 vampires several months into the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847577#post847577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree about the dog part as well, to add to this:<br /> <br /> Having Touchstones that are also other Merits is a great way to incorporate them into a game in a different fashion than the default as Charlaquin went over. Especially for a newly Embraced style game like this, where the characters are still very fresh to the stresses of unlife, the option besides downplaying Touchstones is to have them be True Friend/Mentor/Retainer/etc. Merits as well. Thus the players have an incentive to pull them into play, as the struggle to balance those relationships and being vampires can grow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree to some degree with this having seen it in play. The dog is the only on that has mattered so far, and the character clearly really cares about him in a way he absolutely does not care about anyone else. But, I don't think I want to, basically charge a different kind of merit tax on PCs. But I have learned that, if we ever use the full touchstone system again, I won't shy away from PCs using their touchstones as other merits, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847752#post847752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could give the Venture a variant on the Lethargic Condition based on the success or failure of the detachment roll that kicks in any time they make a make a detachment roll that persists for a number of weeks based on their Humanity score.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, they have to sleep when they're bad? I am not sure I really understand this or the thematics behind it. I like &quot;mad lords&quot; or &quot;detached lords,&quot; not so much &quot;sleepy lords.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T16:54:20-07:00","id":847922,"title":"","content":"I love the style you endorse, though I am a little less adverse to playing a more aggressive ST. I can't speak for Charlaquin but I do want to make some points your discussion has prompted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847881#post847881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's kind of overboard, I think. It was always my impression that Humanity above 7 was literally more human than a normal human. Like, you became a caricature of humanity. I get that scene from Invader Zim in my head, &quot;I eat food, just like you. I HAVE A STOMACH!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>At first I thought that you must have gotten wires crossed, and mixed up the ethical-humanity of 1E with the (err...) 'metaphysical'-humanity of 2E. However, it does say '[The humanity 9-10 vampire] appears as an iconic, idealized human'. It even says 'fresh vampires' are 7-8. So while I can't call you out for misreading the text, I still would advocate Charlaquin's approach of assuming all vampires start as human as human can be as it fully departs from the 1E sense of humanity. Added bonus: this rids the high humanity vampires of that overstated Zim-style humanity trope. (I'd get a kick out of exploring this topic further if you want.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847881#post847881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, the only way it's going to happen is if the GM forces a situation where they are made to watch someone eat (you have to meet with this ghoul at a restaurant), and that's going to come across shitty and obvious that it's just to make the PCs roll detachment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think meeting at a place where people meet is GM abuse but YMMV. You haven't forced the detachment roll anymore than it would be forced naturally by the in-game logic. What I can suggest is only rolling the detachment as a result of a heavily skewed call by a player, which gives them agency. What I mean by heavily skewed is when the player either completely forgets their nature such that it is brought directly to their attention or go out of their way to acknowledge it. So, if the player orders food at the diner, you can either wait until he is vomiting to roll detachment or until he reverses his choice. The latter carries bonus modifiers for being less physically intense. The other side of this though is where, upon hearing they will be meeting at the restaurant, the players resist. Meeting in an ally to avoid humans is more detaching than seeing others. It doesn't leave much in the way of winning rolls because at such a high level of humanity and for new vampires, they will detach at some point. (Which is why I reckon the 9-10 is wrote as it is. To be a fully human vampire, you have to acknowledge your distance and try anyway. Call it the last visage of the ethical-humanity and its original sin overtones.) However, if they go and don't make any choices that would be poignant, then don't detach. The essence of the seeing others eat is the sense of alienation. If they don't notice, they can't feel it. To me, making that happen is no more railroading than asking for vitae expense when you use blood buffs. Like blood buffs, you can only put them in situations where activation is their fault. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  spelling corrections 03-15-2016, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T17:37:52-07:00","id":847940,"title":"","content":"It sounds like your players and you want to run a certain kind of game. If getting rid of Touchstones helps you do that, you should go ahead with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T17:42:03-07:00","id":847941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847566#post847566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of Touchstones is to give vampires an anchor to humanity (that's small-h &quot;the human race&quot;, not big-H stat on the character sheet). Keeping connected to a normal mortal, with a mortal life, and mortal problems is <i>hard</i> for a vampire. They really have to go out of their way to maintain a relationship with someone who, quite frankly, doesn't fit into their unlife. It would be far more convenient to just ignore them and go about your business doing vampire things without having to check in on your human friend every once in a while. But if you do that, you lose the one person in your life who still reminds you of what it means to be human, and as a result, it's much harder to keep a grip on Humanity (that's the capital H kind there). A vampire should always be torn between the needs of their Coterie and the needs of their Touchstones. And if they chose to prioritize the Coterie, those Touchstones should become detached. That's all part of the drama of Vampire the Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think touchstones are huge in game terms. If you throw out your touchstone that's like carving off half of what the humanity system is. They are suppose to be things that keep you grounded, keep you from becoming the monster inside.<br /> <br /> Perhaps your PCs dont care about the touchstones because... ( please do not take this as rude or anything as it's not meant to be.. ) Because you do not care for them? It gives your players mixed signals.<br /> <br /> In a week or two I dont think touchstones should come in to play too much, but if we are pushing a month or so, have your players, text, call, write a letter, send an email or something to check up on your touchstone. I dont think it would be that far fetched our out of the box.<br /> <br /> They are far more than mechanical things on your paper and they are really not that hard to incorporate. Like heavyarms said. touchstones can be, retainers, ghouls, contacts, allies, true friends... There is even a ghoul merit that requires you to be a touchstone and a ghoul. They can be right there in your requiem without it being forced. I think they make for good fleshed out characters.<br /> <br /> <br /> A friend of mine pointed out that the Nosferatu bane works thematically for Ventrue. It makes it hard for you to understand and relate to people. That would be a good easy balanced substitute. Mechanically the same... flavor, slightly different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-15-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T17:44:41-07:00","id":847942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847922#post847922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At first I thought that you must have gotten wires crossed, and mixed up the ethical-humanity of 1E with the (err...) 'metaphysical'-humanity of 2E. However, it does say '[The humanity 9-10 vampire] appears as an iconic, idealized human'. It even says 'fresh vampires' are 7-8. So while I can't call you out for misreading the text, I still would advocate Charlaquin's approach of assuming all vampires start as human as human can be as it fully departs from the 1E sense of humanity. Added bonus: this rids the high humanity vampires of that overstated Zim-style humanity trope. (I'd get a kick out of exploring this topic further if you want.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I <i>might</i> prefer 1st edition flavor in general, though, 2nd edition combat/supernatural power balance. It's hard to move on, now, admittedly, to the new style, completely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847922#post847922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think meeting at a place where people meet is GM abuse but YMMV. You haven't forced the detachment roll anymore than it would be forced naturally by the in-game logic. What I can suggest is only rolling the detachment as a result of a heavily skewed call by a player, which gives them agency. What I mean by heavily skewed is when the player either completely forgets their nature such that it is brought directly to their attention or go out of their way to acknowledge it. So, if the player orders food at the diner, you can either wait until he is vomiting to roll detachment or until he reverses his choice. The latter carries bonus modifiers for being less physically intense. The other side of this though is where, upon hearing they will be meeting at the restaurant, the players resist. Meeting in an ally to avoid humans is more detaching than seeing others. It doesn't leave much in the way of winning rolls because at such a high level of humanity and for new vampires, they will detach at some point. (Which is why I reckon the 9-10 is wrote as it is. To be a fully human vampire, you have to acknowledge your distance and try anyway. Call it the last visage of the ethical-humanity and its original sin overtones.) However, if they go and don't make any choices that would be poignant, then don't detach. The essence of the seeing others eat is the sense of alienation. If they don't notice, they can't feel it. To me, making that happen is no more railroading than asking for vitae expense when you use blood buffs. Like blood buffs, you can only put them in situations where activation is their fault. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I like what you're getting at here. They can try and avoid the dinner. I guess I was thinking more about a &quot;surprise! he's eating!&quot; kind of thing. I actually might use this set up, now. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T17:52:50-07:00","id":847944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847942#post847942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I was thinking more about a &quot;surprise! he's eating!&quot; kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I agree seems jerkish. Let me know how it works out at the table though; I too want to see how it works beyond the 'flower prose version'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (and hey, thanks. I enjoy when my pitches are picked up and validated. :P )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T18:53:24-07:00","id":847961,"title":"","content":"I'll be upfront, I haven't actually played 2ed yet... that said, as far as playing the boring touchstone parts... what I'd recommend is letting another player play the touchstone instead of you GM-ing it, often if I need to isolate a PC I'll let the other players play an NPC. My players seem to enjoy picking up other characters and interacting with each other that way. Doesn't really help with inanimate object touchstones though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T20:47:05-07:00","id":847987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847941#post847941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think touchstones are huge in game terms. If you throw out your touchstone that's like carving off half of what the humanity system is. They are suppose to be things that keep you grounded, keep you from becoming the monster inside.<br /> <br /> Perhaps your PCs dont care about the touchstones because... ( please do not take this as rude or anything as it's not meant to be.. ) Because you do not care for them? It gives your players mixed signals.<br /> <br /> In a week or two I dont think touchstones should come in to play too much, but if we are pushing a month or so, have your players, text, call, write a letter, send an email or something to check up on your touchstone. I dont think it would be that far fetched our out of the box.<br /> <br /> They are far more than mechanical things on your paper and they are really not that hard to incorporate. Like heavyarms said. touchstones can be, retainers, ghouls, contacts, allies, true friends... There is even a ghoul merit that requires you to be a touchstone and a ghoul. They can be right there in your requiem without it being forced. I think they make for good fleshed out characters.<br /> <br /> <br /> A friend of mine pointed out that the Nosferatu bane works thematically for Ventrue. It makes it hard for you to understand and relate to people. That would be a good easy balanced substitute. Mechanically the same... flavor, slightly different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was this directed at me? Cause I can assure you, my players and I both love Touchstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T20:53:58-07:00","id":847989,"title":"","content":"Oh no no. Do forgive. I quoted you because I agreed with your statement about what they were for and such. <br /> <br /> <i>&quot; Perhaps your PCs dont care about the touchstones because... ( please do not take this as rude or anything as it's not meant to be.. ) Because you do not care for them? It gives your players mixed signals. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> The words ^ were for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8\" data-vbnamecard=\"8\">Storyteller</a> who posted the question. It seems he does not like them, so perhaps his players might not. I have run into that with other things as a story teller. I say my dislike for something, then suddenly my players are suddenly shying away from druids.. or mages. Or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T03:40:40-07:00","id":848065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847881#post847881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, they have to sleep when they're bad? I am not sure I really understand this or the thematics behind it. I like &quot;mad lords&quot; or &quot;detached lords,&quot; not so much &quot;sleepy lords.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>More along the lines of them becoming aloof/disinterested in night to night occurrences after their most recent trauma and thus not willing/disinclined to invest their maximum effort in things. Instead of rolling to resist sleep, they would have to roll their Composure + Resolve to spend willpower.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T04:52:34-07:00","id":848082,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I've had the most success with Touchstones that also serve as retainers. Or part of their haven. Or something else that integrates the Touchstone as part of the one (un)life. I find that trying to make Touchstones as something completely separate creates a kind of artificial divide between PC-as-human, and PC-as-vampire. If anything, this makes them push away their human side, instead of integrating their humanity within their vampire life. I made a Daeva PC that had a ghoul (also part of the herd) as a Touchstone. You say that having a dog Retainer as a Touchstone felt off, almost like a cheat. Personally, I say that's working as intended. Well, one way that they're intended to work - Touchstones should be something fluid and fit almost anything. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the core of the problem here isn't that the characters are too young, but rather that the players picked innapropriate ones? PCs don't always act out the way we think we do at char gen. They change and evolve rather drastically, even if only over the course of a single session? One reason I think its important to integrate Touchstones into one's vampire life is that one of the major functions of a Touchstone is to talk their vampire down from a frenzy. The Touchstone can't do that if they're safely in their white-picket house across town. In fact, I think that if your Touchstone is something that's not part of your life, something that you want to cut out for safety reasons? That's the opposite of a Touchstone. That's reinforcing that you are not human, and pushing your Humanity further down. <br /> <br /> How do Touchstones develop? Again, this is something flexible. The bare minimum for being a Touchstone is just that it reminds a vampire that they're still human (at least in part). It could be something as simple as a song that reminds them of simpler times, happier times that they hear for the first time while hunting. I find it rather evocative that a vampire would hear some music, maybe a musical jewelry box, that reminded her of her mother, a century dead, do anything to get that little trinket, and obsessively listen to the song. And maybe, just maybe, one of her ghouls would record the song on their phone, and the next time, in Elysium, on the verge of frenzy and attacking someone, that song starts playing, and cuts through the red rage like a sharp knife, bringing the vampire to her senses. All this, from just wandering around, and snap, instant connection.<br /> <br /> What about for neonates? Fresh fledgelings? Maybe it should be the car they're still driving around from their living days. Maybe its going to dinner every Sunday with their family, and eff any vampire that says they shouldn't. Its any number of things that mean they're maintaining their still-human lifestyle. Its something, anything, that they had a connection with as a mortal. The Touchstone should become a mechanical thing the moment they first rise hungry after Embraced.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't think that being freshly Embraced is the issue here. I think that its just a case of picking bad Touchstones, maybe misunderstanding what Touchstones represent. Your PCs still engage in things from their mortal life? So, those things that they're still using and part of should be the Touchstones. <br /> <br /> Now, the Ventrue clan bane. Its always been a bit fudgy, but to be honest? I think the Mehket and Daeva ones are insanely easy to ignore as well. Its insanely easy to pick a Bane that is rare enough that it doesn't impact your character at all, and a Daeva's weakness only comes into play if one's herd somehow becomes relevant to the plot. I've had games where neither one has had an impact in the story. You claim the Mehket is the most interesting, but it still comes down to the same thing as the 1e flaw - &quot;same weaknesses as everyone else, but worse!&quot; The new Ventrue flaw is actually meant to reflect the Julii flaw - they tend to become detached faster than the average vampire. The whole Touchstone thing is supposed to reflect them having a harder time holding onto their Humanity. They kind of dropped the old Ventrue flaw (madness) because too many people found that the whole immorality = insanity thing to be insensitive, and some of the derangements do honestly overlap with the general Banes that a Mehket might pick up. <br /> <br /> There's a couple options here for a new Ventrue bane. One is to just copy the Julii clan flaw. -1 to all detachment rolls. Represents the same thing as the current flaw, imho. Another is to just take a derangement if you like the idea of them being a bit unbalanced, though again, we get into Unfortunate-Implications territory. I would absolutely not do the derangement on the drop - not only because of unfortunate implications, but it makes less sense with the current Humanity than it does with the old. <br /> <br /> <br /> Have I ever downplayed Touchstones in a game before? Well, that one is a bit debatable. I consider Touchstones to be something that's Opt-In from a player's standpoint. As in, I leave it up to the players to decide what they're goign to do with them. I've had palyers that simply ignore their Touchstone and just go on with the game, and eventually had nothing to do with one. I've had others that made Touchstones a huge part of the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T05:48:21-07:00","id":848097,"title":"","content":"I think MCN asks a very good question: in the current chronicle, what mortals are your PCs actually interacting with the most and consider to be the most important to them? I know you said they're hardly interacting with their current Touchstones, the only outlier being the player with the dog (who I think chose the best Touchstone, considering theirs is getting screen-time and is being treated with importance by the character and player). The fact their Touchstone is doubling as a Retainer is perfectly fine in my opinion, because it makes them useful, thus more important, to the PC on a greater level than being some random NPC a character interacts with. It also gives them a great deal more agency as an NPC, because players aren't forced into interactions to avoid suffering a Detachment penalty - they're actively seeking these NPCs out because they <i>need</i> them.<br /> <br /> edit: mind you, if you and your players just aren't feeling them, there's really no problem with parting ways with them completely. They're supposed to be fun, and if they're not fun for your troupe, no shame in giving 'em the boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 03-16-2016, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T05:53:18-07:00","id":848101,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't touchstones be easier for the recently embraced since their friends and family are still alive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T05:58:35-07:00","id":848103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847566#post847566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side-note: Yeah, I wouldn't have allowed a dog as a Touchstone. Making them a Retainer could be interesting, but a dog is definitely not going to anchor you to the human experience.</div> </div> </div> </div> I respectfully disagree. If your Touchstone can be something as immobile as a house or a gravestone? Then a living being can serve just as well. I had a 1e character where her dog would have made a perfect Touchstone. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your characters were all recently embraced, they probably don't yet need to maintain a relationship with a human to remind them what it was like to be alive - after all it was only a week or so ago. The default rules kind of assume that the characters have been vampires long enough to at least gain 3 dots of Disciplines, 3 dots of Merits, and to drop to Humanity 7. If you're playing characters who were embraced that recently, I would also start them at Humanity 10, because they shouldn't yet be used to things like lying in defense of the Masquerade, going over a day without human contact, possessing superhuman abilities, and using those abilities to steal the lifeblood of the unwilling, or to deprive them of the agency to attest their unwillingness. That's valuable stuff to play through if you're starting that early. Don't bother with Touchstones yet, have the players acquire them in-game, at a time when it feels dramatically appropriate. When they start forgetting things like the feeling of a sunburn, the rhythm of a heartbeat, and why exactly they're supposed to care about consent. When they start to experience that cognitive dissonance of &quot;wait... I should feel guilty about this. Why don't I feel guilty about this?&quot; that's when it's time to find a human you can confide in and who can serve as an example of what humans are like and why that's important. </div> </div> </div> With all due respect, I'm going to have to disagree here as well. I don't think there's any point here that I do agree with. While this is fine baseline for some games, I'm not comfortable with saying it is the default assumptions for everyone. &quot;Time to learn 3 disciplines&quot; especially stands out to me, because the book makes it clear that many Disciplines (and Devotions!) are spontaneously developed, no teaching or learning periods required - drinking the vitae of someone who knows the power is the only requirement in the case of non-affinity powers. Theban, Cruac, and Coils are the only Disciplines that seem to absolutely require time and tutorship/experiementation to learn, and no one forces you to start with those. Three dots of merits? You can start a game with all mortal merits specifically from your time as a human. <br /> <br /> &quot;Drop to Humanity 7&quot; is also exceedingly problematic to me because I do not believe that Humanity 10 is appropriate for fledgelings to start with either. I'd say its the rare human that qualifies as an &quot;expert in the way humans behave, feel, and think,&quot; (VtR p106). Or to be an idealized human being. Humanity 7-8 is defined as being &quot;either very good at maintaining her attachments, or she\u2019s very new to the Danse Macabre,&quot; (VtR p106). That very new bit makes me think we're talking about a newly Embraced fledgeling. It sounds like the assumption is starting at Humanity 7 for all vampires, not dropping to 7 before the game begins.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T06:22:05-07:00","id":848115,"title":"","content":"Your problem seems to be that you aren't using touchstones as they are intended: This is, to be catalysts for drama and conflict. What happens when a Daeva takes Bob as a blood doll, because their clan bane makes the succubus obsessed with him? What happens when a Mekhet Hound keeps tabs on the character, finds out his touchstones and delivers pictures to the PC in a clear threat to him should he not do as he's told? How do you convince your coterie to give a fuck about Bob and help you one-up the Daeva or the Mekhet?<br /> <br /> What's better yet, how do you manouver the coterie into helping you, without tipping your hand as to why you are so opposed to the smug Mekhet Hound? Or does your character simply complies to the threats, and eventually forces you to go against your coterie's politic aims in a climax? Which do you choose? The mask, or the requiem?<br /> <br /> Not everything that goes on in the game should be displayed to the whole table. The above scenarios wouldn't. Email your players between sessions, text them or hold 1 on 1 sessions concerning these private issues over the phone, or skype. It works wonders.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, touchstones are weakspots. Savvy (power) players will take Two- or One-dimentional characters over having complications as above, because it detracts from some preconceived notion of awesomeness-in-untouchability. They want to play elders already, but becoming elders takes it's tools on the soul.<br /> <br /> The dog as a touchstone works, because anybody using animalism on it will predispose such complications. Do you take it to elysium? Did you ghoul it, so you won't risk detachment in say, 10 years? How does your character feels about violating the nature of such a loyal companion on such a manner?<br /> <br /> Regarding your STing style? Shit happens. STs are there to drop the shit on the moving fans. Otherwise it woudn't be much of a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T06:36:56-07:00","id":848119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848115#post848115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's better yet, how do you manouver the coterie into helping you, without tipping your hand as to why you are so opposed to the smug Mekhet Hound? Or does your character simply complies to the threats, and eventually forces you to go against your coterie's politic aims in a climax? Which do you choose? The mask, or the requiem?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Gosh, no. This is not the choice between Mask and Requiem/Dirge. Choosing Mask is not choosing humanity, it's choosing the lie, which you present to humanity. It's why they should not pull out pitchforks and torches. It has nothing to do with how connected to humanity you actually are. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, let's remember the other mechanical thing about Vampires. Willpower. With no default regeneration, they only get it back from Touchstones, Mask and Dirge. So do they do their human things (interacting with Touchstones) to get their fill back? or do they go for vampire things (Mask and Dirge) ?<br /> If we do feeding scenes for a resource, one can do touchstone scenes for a different resource <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T06:57:14-07:00","id":848127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848082#post848082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made a Daeva PC that had a ghoul (also part of the herd) as a Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, my issue with this is, how does a ghoul remind you of being human? They're, well, not human anymore. You've taken that away from them. They don't live a normal human life anymore. If they're awake during the day, it's because they're doing a specific job for you. Otherwise, its their only chance to sleep. At night, they're serving you. That just doesn't seem like an effective touchstone--it's like trying to get closer to animals by eating a burger. I know there is a merit for ghouls that requires they be a touchstone, but that always felt off to me, and I feel like it had to be written by a different author than the main touchstone section.<br /> <br /> The dog feels like cheating because it's utterly under the character's sway. It's something that accompanies him everywhere. It doesn't have a choice, it has to deal with him. It's just an animal. There's no risk at all--no risk the guy you're stalking will spot you, no risk your old buddy will notice something is off, no risk you girlfriend from life will reject you. It's basically a slave.<br /> <br /> It's worked out ok, but it still feels wrong, for what appears to be the spirit of the rules. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848082#post848082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One reason I think its important to integrate Touchstones into one's vampire life is that one of the major functions of a Touchstone is to talk their vampire down from a frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed that, but then, look at the example Touchstones in the book. I can't imagine <i>any</i> of them being around to talk someone down from frenzy. It seems like a mechanic more intended to keep you from accidentally frenzying and killing your touchstone than actually using you touchstone actively to avoid it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848082#post848082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Touchstones develop? Again, this is something flexible. The bare minimum for being a Touchstone is just that it reminds a vampire that they're still human (at least in part). It could be something as simple as a song that reminds them of simpler times, happier times that they hear for the first time while hunting. I find it rather evocative that a vampire would hear some music, maybe a musical jewelry box, that reminded her of her mother, a century dead, do anything to get that little trinket, and obsessively listen to the song. And maybe, just maybe, one of her ghouls would record the song on their phone, and the next time, in Elysium, on the verge of frenzy and attacking someone, that song starts playing, and cuts through the red rage like a sharp knife, bringing the vampire to her senses. All this, from just wandering around, and snap, instant connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great story, honestly. It makes for great italicized text. But in real play? That just feels like cheating even more than the dog. For one, there's zero risk. If your touchstone is something ephemeral, like a song, it is literally impossible to threaten or imperil your touchstone. Once again, you have total control over it and can even interact with it on your whim by just humming or singing the notes. That doesn't even match the mechanics where the touchstone is rolling and needs 3 x BP to stop the frenzy. What is this song's die pool? This kind of reinforces my &quot;Touchstones are awesome in theory, but only in theory&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848082#post848082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about for neonates? Fresh fledgelings? Maybe it should be the car they're still driving around from their living days. Maybe its going to dinner every Sunday with their family, and eff any vampire that says they shouldn't. Its any number of things that mean they're maintaining their still-human lifestyle. Its something, anything, that they had a connection with as a mortal. The Touchstone should become a mechanical thing the moment they first rise hungry after Embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of them acted human at all after they woke up. Now, it was partially the game's circumstances--they were all killed and then post mortem embraced. They woke up alone in dug up pine boxes and had to, basically, figure things out. So, they actually all avoided their human lives--they thought the people they loved and cared about knew they were dead. They immediately abandoned human life and leapt head first into vampire stuff, because, well, they had little choice. <br /> <br /> Now, I know those immediate circumstances were causes for detachment, but, as I had constructed the situation and forced it on them, I felt it unfair and just assumed they had all succeeded, instead having them wake up with a condition. <br /> <br /> I also think attending Sunday dinner would be ridiculous and foolish for a vampire, as you'd be risking detachment every week for no reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848082#post848082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the Ventrue clan bane. Its always been a bit fudgy, but to be honest? I think the Mehket and Daeva ones are insanely easy to ignore as well. Its insanely easy to pick a Bane that is rare enough that it doesn't impact your character at all, and a Daeva's weakness only comes into play if one's herd somehow becomes relevant to the plot. I've had games where neither one has had an impact in the story. You claim the Mehket is the most interesting, but it still comes down to the same thing as the 1e flaw - &quot;same weaknesses as everyone else, but worse!&quot; The new Ventrue flaw is actually meant to reflect the Julii flaw - they tend to become detached faster than the average vampire. The whole Touchstone thing is supposed to reflect them having a harder time holding onto their Humanity. They kind of dropped the old Ventrue flaw (madness) because too many people found that the whole immorality = insanity thing to be insensitive, and some of the derangements do honestly overlap with the general Banes that a Mehket might pick up.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, to me, a successful clan bane is one that influences you to (un)live in a specific manner such that your flaw is minimized. <br /> <br /> The Daeva curse is great. You <i>must</i> feed from a series of victims. You cannot have a herd. You cannot keep blood dolls. You must feed &quot;promiscuously.&quot; Eating is never going to be easy. Ever. So, yes, the flaw &quot;never comes up,&quot; but only because you have cut out an entire feeding strategy from your playbook and chosen to live in a specific way, which, well, is the <i>real</i> flaw.<br /> <br /> The Mekhet flaw works the same way, except it's even more interesting because every Mekhet's flaw is different. Avoiding fire and sunlight is dumb. All vampires do that. It has no real effect. My group and I used to joke that the Mekhet flaw was dying in 6 seconds in the sun, rather than 9. It just didn't matter. But now? They all have a weird bane they have to protect. It seems simple. Avoid church bells or salt or whatever you pick, but you have to arrange your existence around both avoiding that thing <i>and </i>not letting anyone know that you're avoiding it, because you don't want your enemies to know. Again, the bane never <i>comes up directly</i>, but it's an ever present force in your character's existence. That's awesome.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu is the next best. They take much larger penalties when relating to humans. So, uh, they stop doing that. I can say that in first edition, I saw the Nosferatu flaw actually affect a die roll <i>once</i> in like 10-15 years of play. Just like this version, you won't see it affecting rolls much at all--but you'll see it affecting decisions constantly as the Nosferatu chooses the way he interacts carefully, so he remains un-penalized. He cuts out entire options from his playbook to avoid it. Once again, flaw successful.<br /> <br /> Gangrel is...well, also problematic. It's certainly better than the crippling mental flaw from before, which, I'm sorry, you just couldn't avoid like you could the Nosferatu social penalty. But, it's still not really character defining. You frenzy more as your humanity dips is kind of it. Given most people's Res+Comp pools, I don't even think it will come up very often until you're pretty far down the chart--at least to 5, and maybe not even 4. So, what does that suggest for a Gangrel? There's not much they can do to avoid it that every vampire doesn't do anyway. It's not a new wrinkle, it's just an additional consequence on top of something that's already bad. Daeva try to keep their humanity in addition to not feeding on the same person twice. Gangrel just, uh, extra try to keep humanity? That doesn't really feel thematically appropriate, does it? Are Gangrel supposed to be the saints? No, it's not even really that anymore--it's also avoiding stuff that reminds you of being human (like watching people eat). So, what, they're like the crazy guy shutting his eyes and ears as he walks around, so he doesn't accidentally experience a human-only thing? I don't know. I don't like this flaw, either, but it's at least better than the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Which, yeah, brings me to Ventrue. They don't even have an additional roleplaying consequence (getting angrier, for example), they just have to spend their 1 XP and extra roleplaying touchstone effort 1 humanity earlier than everyone else. That's...just not a concern at all. That changes absolutely nothing, no new wrinkles, not even piled consequences, just exactly the same thing as every other vampire on a slightly advanced schedule.<br /> <br /> My version of the flaw isn't <i>amazing</i>, which is why I came asking for more suggestions. It still just penalizes a thing that all vampires deal with. But, it does <i>a little bit</i> of what I want. It sort of makes Ventrue into, maybe stuffed shirt types to a degree? They have to stick to this strict code more fiercely than other vampires because they are much more prone to falling than anyone else (around 20% more, as I mentioned before). I picture them having stronger codes of conduct and behavior, following social rituals to avoid human-stimuli and excessive violence/violation, etc. They have to be extra careful to avoid frenzy (the biggest cause for detachment rolls, it seems). You end up with Ventrue that follow this code of decorum, and Ventrue that have gone mad from failing to stick to the code. It's not great, but it's acceptable for now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848082#post848082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a couple options here for a new Ventrue bane. One is to just copy the Julii clan flaw. -1 to all detachment rolls. Represents the same thing as the current flaw, imho. Another is to just take a derangement if you like the idea of them being a bit unbalanced, though again, we get into Unfortunate-Implications territory. I would absolutely not do the derangement on the drop - not only because of unfortunate implications, but it makes less sense with the current Humanity than it does with the old.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want it to become a big <i>thing</i>, but I don't really think tying derangements to humanity loss has any implications. I get that it was pretty awful for some people unfamiliar with the gothic horror mindset when normal humans who did bad things went crazy, but vampires who slid from human to inhuman literally losing their human mind? Seems pretty damn fitting to me. Anyway, I'm not expecting it to come up, regardless. I just want a couple of crazy ventrue elders down the road. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848082#post848082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have I ever downplayed Touchstones in a game before? Well, that one is a bit debatable. I consider Touchstones to be something that's Opt-In from a player's standpoint. As in, I leave it up to the players to decide what they're goign to do with them. I've had palyers that simply ignore their Touchstone and just go on with the game, and eventually had nothing to do with one. I've had others that made Touchstones a huge part of the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, let's say no players buy in at all. You basically ignore, downplay it, then, right? So, what do you do for the Ventrue flaw to make sure it still matters?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T07:09:49-07:00","id":848134,"title":"","content":"The Gangrel &quot;Cap on frenzy rules&quot; is just stupid in my opinion. Exactly because it doesn't matter at high humanity, and at low the palyer can do nothing, except say &quot;I'l lraise humanity.&quot; As such, I use a houserule where instead of a hard cap, Gangrel get's a penalty to their Frenzy roll equal to their Himanity social penalty. That way, one can both increase his dice pool to offset it, and it matters at all humanity levels. (except the highest ones, but hey). <br /> <br /> As for the Ventrue, I use someone's elses made up rule: When regaining WP from touchstone roll humanit,y you get it back only on succ. If you were to regain all humanity from touchstones - you roll Humanity and regain Successes of WP instead.<br /> This, means tjhat now he has a clear choice: Do his vampire stuff (Mask/Dirge) which is fully rewarding and cool (normal WP regen), or interact with touchstones which isn't as rewarding and doesn't make you more happy as much (as you basically get less WP depending on your humanity).<br /> <br /> So do you work that much harder to keep in touch? Or do you let it go, because it's not as good? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T07:17:32-07:00","id":848139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848134#post848134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gangrel &quot;Cap on frenzy rules&quot; is just stupid in my opinion. Exactly because it doesn't matter at high humanity, and at low the palyer can do nothing, except say &quot;I'l lraise humanity.&quot; As such, I use a houserule where instead of a hard cap, Gangrel get's a penalty to their Frenzy roll equal to their Himanity social penalty. That way, one can both increase his dice pool to offset it, and it matters at all humanity levels. (except the highest ones, but hey).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is definitely a little bit better. I'd still prefer a better flaw overall, but that helps a little.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848134#post848134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Ventrue, I use someone's elses made up rule: When regaining WP from touchstone roll humanit,y you get it back only on succ. If you were to regain all humanity from touchstones - you roll Humanity and regain Successes of WP instead.<br /> This, means tjhat now he has a clear choice: Do his vampire stuff (Mask/Dirge) which is fully rewarding and cool (normal WP regen), or interact with touchstones which isn't as rewarding and doesn't make you more happy as much (as you basically get less WP depending on your humanity).<br /> <br /> So do you work that much harder to keep in touch? Or do you let it go, because it's not as good? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, our group <i>mostly</i> regains willpower from resting (1 per day) and occasionally from doing something awesome. Mask and Dirge really haven't come up much at all--maybe like twice--and nobody, even the dog owner, has gained willpower from touchstones.<br /> <br /> All these ways to gain willpower, I don't know. Unless you tone it down like we have, it seems like you'd be gaining willpower back just about every scene. How is that a resource to worry about, then? There's no risk to spending it knowing that you'll just get more by doing exactly what you'd do anyway.<br /> <br /> I knew I ran these games a little differently than the book, but, it is becoming more and more apparent that my games might not look anything like most people's...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T07:32:33-07:00","id":848148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848139#post848139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is definitely a little bit better. I'd still prefer a better flaw overall, but that helps a little.<br /> <br /> I don't know, our group <i>mostly</i> regains willpower from resting (1 per day) and occasionally from doing something awesome. Mask and Dirge really haven't come up much at all--maybe like twice--and nobody, even the dog owner, has gained willpower from touchstones.<br /> <br /> All these ways to gain willpower, I don't know. Unless you tone it down like we have, it seems like you'd be gaining willpower back just about every scene. How is that a resource to worry about, then? There's no risk to spending it knowing that you'll just get more by doing exactly what you'd do anyway.<br /> <br /> I knew I ran these games a little differently than the book, but, it is becoming more and more apparent that my games might not look anything like most people's...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vampires do NOT regain willpower from resting (1 per day).<br /> <br /> And at that point it becomes much more important to get WP from the sources they do regain WP from. Namely touchstones, mask and dirge. That's why Touchstones are supposed to net point of WP even for normal interactions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T07:45:16-07:00","id":848161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848148#post848148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Vampires do NOT regain willpower from resting (1 per day).<br /> <br /> And at that point it becomes much more important to get WP from the sources they do regain WP from. Namely touchstones, mask and dirge. That's why Touchstones are supposed to net point of WP even for normal interactions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, really? No Willpower from resting? I don't recall reading that. Hmm. I know they did in 1st edition, why the deliberate change?<br /> <br /> I will have to evaluate whether or not I should go with this new rule and change everything around or just keep running it the way I've been with an unwitting houserule.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T07:50:04-07:00","id":848167,"title":"","content":"Maybe exactly so that the Touchstone mechanics are more prominent? And useful? It's not forced, if the player goes out of his way to get to Touchstone now that it gives him actual benefit (WP regen), instead of the ST blackmail &quot;if you don't go you're gonna lose him&quot;. You know, just like the players go out of their way to regain Vitae, when the plot revolves around something else and not feeding. <br /> <br /> And, yes, you didn't recall reading the change. However, you won't find an entry which says that they regen wp from resting either <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> this has been cleared up by the devs in the forums, that indeed, they no longer regain wp from rest in second edition. Probably has something to do, with the fact that they don't really rest during day, but are dead or having nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T08:03:15-07:00","id":848178,"title":"","content":"I've interpreted each clan bane to be an expression of that clans beast. for exemple the mekhet's beast is superstitious so it makes the mekhet follow bizarre rules.<br /> For the gangrel, the beast is prone to savage reaction. So i would ask the gangrel character to pick situations in which the beast would manifest more readily. for exemple, one gangrel would be confident enough in his own strenght that violence doesnt make him react much, but being lied to pisses him off more. Mechanically it's the same but there is an element of customization that i like.<br /> For the ventrue (i also found the touchstone bane to be problematic, i do not get that ventrue have a more difficult time relating to humanity than the other clan) i try to find a bane that would be a consequence of the ventrue beast being a tyrant. For now i am going with the bane of the En bloodline that untrained social roll are at -3 and no 10 again on empathy roll. The point is to say that the ventrue's beast pushes the ventrue to make others do as he wishes but makes it difficult to relate to others and understand them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T08:37:04-07:00","id":848201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848167#post848167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe exactly so that the Touchstone mechanics are more prominent? And useful? It's not forced, if the player goes out of his way to get to Touchstone now that it gives him actual benefit (WP regen), instead of the ST blackmail &quot;if you don't go you're gonna lose him&quot;. You know, just like the players go out of their way to regain Vitae, when the plot revolves around something else and not feeding.<br /> <br /> And, yes, you didn't recall reading the change. However, you won't find an entry which says that they regen wp from resting either <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> this has been cleared up by the devs in the forums, that indeed, they no longer regain wp from rest in second edition. Probably has something to do, with the fact that they don't really rest during day, but are dead or having nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I don't think I like people constantly chasing their Dirges and Masks like that. It ends up feeling forced and weird. I'd rather people roleplay naturally in character, rather than looking at what they wrote down when the game started and just forcing that stereotype onto every scene. They become flanderized, then. Instead of deep characters, you get, &quot;I'm QUESTIONING! Whoo! Question!&quot; I don't want to encourage that. <br /> <br /> I can't even imagine the normal game flow. &quot;Oh, that scene was tough. I call my mom, then go beat up a random drunk guy.&quot; &quot;What?&quot; &quot;Yeah, I lost a lot of willpower, so, I need to interact with my touchstone and be a Monster.&quot; That's just bizarre. It seems like those rules are written for people who don't know how to roleplay at all and need constant coaching to act in character at all (&quot;ok, always remember that I'm a Jester, got it.&quot;). <br /> <br /> That's also daunting for a GM. I like to run games with nothing but dice in front of me. I don't have notes or sheets or anything. But how am I supposed to remember 2 unusual willpower triggers per character (so, for my game, upwards of 10 when everyone can make it)? If I rely on players to cue me, it'll be worse, because then I'll be getting constantly interrupted by, &quot;hey, so, do I get my willpower back for that?&quot; every other sentence. Sounds like a nightmare.<br /> <br /> I'll talk to my group about it, but I think I'd rather keep the Willpower from rest as the main way to get it.<br /> <br /> This whole thread is really making me wish I could just watch a game session run by someone doing it &quot;correctly&quot; and by the book. I've been running roleplaying games for more than 20 years now, and I can't picture this working well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848178#post848178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the ventrue (i also found the touchstone bane to be problematic, i do not get that ventrue have a more difficult time relating to humanity than the other clan) i try to find a bane that would be a consequence of the ventrue beast being a tyrant. For now i am going with the bane of the En bloodline that untrained social roll are at -3 and no 10 again on empathy roll. The point is to say that the ventrue's beast pushes the ventrue to make others do as he wishes but makes it difficult to relate to others and understand them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of works for me because you need to direct all social situations down pathways where your specific skills are relevant, but I think everyone already does that in general. -3 is bad compared to -1, but I don't ever see people volunteering to use -1s, either, and social skills are never like, a surprise. You can act in specific ways to control which skill you roll. Better than the Touchstone thing, yeah, but, it that feels insufficient for my purposes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T08:40:10-07:00","id":848202,"title":"","content":"It's not like recovering willpower from rest totally shatters the game, mind, so if you <i>were </i>to ditch touchstones it might be a good idea to reinstate it.<br /> <br /> As for issues about remembering mask and dirge, perhaps you could instigate a non-verbal form of indicating when the player feels they are acting in accordance, like a little flag or something. Then you can give a thumbs up if they get the willpower without it distracting from the actual story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-16-2016, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T08:41:16-07:00","id":848203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848201#post848201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, I don't think I like people constantly chasing their Dirges and Masks like that. It ends up feeling forced and weird. I'd rather people roleplay naturally in character, rather than looking at what they wrote down when the game started and just forcing that stereotype onto every scene. They become flanderized, then. Instead of deep characters, you get, &quot;I'm QUESTIONING! Whoo! Question!&quot; I don't want to encourage that.<br /> <br /> I can't even imagine the normal game flow. &quot;Oh, that scene was tough. I call my mom, then go beat up a random drunk guy.&quot; &quot;What?&quot; &quot;Yeah, I lost a lot of willpower, so, I need to interact with my touchstone and be a Monster.&quot; That's just bizarre. It seems like those rules are written for people who don't know how to roleplay at all and need constant coaching to act in character at all (&quot;ok, always remember that I'm a Jester, got it.&quot;).<br /> <br /> That's also daunting for a GM. I like to run games with nothing but dice in front of me. I don't have notes or sheets or anything. But how am I supposed to remember 2 unusual willpower triggers per character (so, for my game, upwards of 10 when everyone can make it)? If I rely on players to cue me, it'll be worse, because then I'll be getting constantly interrupted by, &quot;hey, so, do I get my willpower back for that?&quot; every other sentence. Sounds like a nightmare.<br /> <br /> I'll talk to my group about it, but I think I'd rather keep the Willpower from rest as the main way to get it.<br /> <br /> This whole thread is really making me wish I could just watch a game session run by someone doing it &quot;correctly&quot; and by the book. I've been running roleplaying games for more than 20 years now, and I can't picture this working well.<br /> <br /> That sort of works for me because you need to direct all social situations down pathways where your specific skills are relevant, but I think everyone already does that in general. -3 is bad compared to -1, but I don't ever see people volunteering to use -1s, either, and social skills are never like, a surprise. You can act in specific ways to control which skill you roll. Better than the Touchstone thing, yeah, but, it that feels insufficient for my purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All of that feels to come from the fact that the Masks/Dirges are wrongly chosen. For Mask/Dirge you shouldn't go out of your way, it should be how you want to roleplay. As for player cues - after a while, the players will get a feel for when they deserve WP and when they don't, so you won't be interupted needlessly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, perhaps, the right solution here, instead of looking for something &quot;correctly&quot;, talk it over with the players, and to hell with Touchstones/Masks/Dirges and whatever else you don't like? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They're supposed to be there to reward good roleplay, not to shoehorn something somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:32:25-07:00","id":848224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848203#post848203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of that feels to come from the fact that the Masks/Dirges are wrongly chosen. For Mask/Dirge you shouldn't go out of your way, it should be how you want to roleplay. As for player cues - after a while, the players will get a feel for when they deserve WP and when they don't, so you won't be interupted needlessly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyways, perhaps, the right solution here, instead of looking for something &quot;correctly&quot;, talk it over with the players, and to hell with Touchstones/Masks/Dirges and whatever else you don't like? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They're supposed to be there to reward good roleplay, not to shoehorn something somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't come from mask/dirge being wrongly chosen, it comes from real people being complicated and diverse. Even if you can call someone a jokester, they're not literally making jokes all the time in all situations. They're also not forcing jokes at weird times because they just were in a tough fight. But when you get willpower for cracking a joke? That's what happens.<br /> <br /> A real Monster isn't cruel to everyone all the time. That's a great way to get dead. But if you get willpower from it? Guess who is trolling the neighborhood looking for someone to bully whenever they do anything difficult?<br /> <br /> These rules are in place to encourage good roleplaying, but for them to result in actually good roleplaying, you need people who aren't good roleplayers normally, forgtting to act like their masks and dirges until they go, &quot;oh, right, I should say something snarky!&quot; (or whatever). If you have people who are conscious of their mask/dirge, they're going to act weird, not actually in character, but as a flanderized* version of their character.<br /> <br /> *If it's not known what I mean, Ned Flanders is Homer Simpson's neighbor. In the early episodes, he was just a really nice neighbor to provide a foil to Homer. Eventually, his niceness and other quirks (okily dokily) grew and grew until he ended up nice and devout to the degree of insanity. It's basically what happens to all side characters in long running shows. They start as normal, 3 dimensional people with a few quirks, but all anyone cares about or respond to are the quirks, so, they grow and grow until the character has actually become a 2-dimensional board holding up a few quirks.<br /> <br /> Getting willpower from Mask or Dirge every scene will lead to that, I fear. Normal vampires do not act as their mask/dirge 100% of the time, anymore than normal humans constantly indulge in virtues and vices. These things should be occasional, not a driving force. If you have people who are actually good roleplayers, playing in character, mask/dirge will only come up every once in a while. But if its the only way to get back willpower, they're going to purposefully stop being good roleplayers for a bit in order to make back some quick willpower.<br /> <br /> And seriously, to me, this is a roleplaying game. Good roleplaying is my default assumption. I'm not going to give anyone rewards for doing what they're supposed to do. That'd be like getting $100 in monopoly just for rolling the dice.<br /> <br /> Anyway, yeah, I am 75% sure I'm just going to keep running it the way we've been playing.<br /> <br /> Wow, this got off course, huh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:37:13-07:00","id":848226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848127#post848127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my issue with this is, how does a ghoul remind you of being human?</div> </div> </div> </div> One, I disagree that ghouls aren't human anymore. I fully believe that ghouls, wolf blooded, and proximi are human. Two, a <i>house </i>can help remind you of being human; with that in mind, anything can work. There's no limit on the mind to draw connections between things. Three, its quite common in both Vampire lore and general vampire stories for the elder vampire to have a younger one help them relate to people. A ghoul fits this niche as well as anyone else.<br /> <br /> All you need is one reason for it to work. Maybe the ghoul reminds you of your old wife when you were alive. Maybe the ghoul makes a point to take you out to movies, catch you up on human social mores and culture (of which the ghoul still possesses in full). The only restriction here is that it needs to <i>remind</i> you in some way of being human. Sitting down and watching anime with a ghoul every week can easily count. Maybe they'll even start a manga exchange.<br /> <br /> Just because you can't think of a reason doesn't mean that someone else can't. Hells, look at Promethean and the Silver Refinement. Those Created learn to be human by studying other supernaturals and the bits of humanity they all possess. An entire splat that effectively uses non-humans to learn about humans. The idea that you have to be human to teach something about humanity is not supported by any material in any gameline that I can see. Not Vampire, not Werewolf, not Promethean.<br /> <br /> There's even a section in the book talking about non-human Touchstones. Yes, they are rare. But they are very much part of the game. As long as it meets the rough guidelines, its allowed by the ruels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The dog feels like cheating because it's utterly under the character's sway. It's something that accompanies him everywhere. It doesn't have a choice, it has to deal with him. It's just an animal. There's no risk at all--no risk the guy you're stalking will spot you, no risk your old buddy will notice something is off, no risk you girlfriend from life will reject you. It's basically a slave. </div> </div> </div> Putting aside the slave comment... I really feel like you have some very strong misunderstandings on what a Touchstone is supposed to be. Touchstones are supposed to challenge you in some way, sure. But that doesn't mean that you have to have fear of rejection or being noticed. You can be completely candid with your Touchstone.<br /> <br /> And is it possible that part of the problem be that, as an NPC, the Storyteller don't have control over it? Honestly, I think that the mere fact that you are complaining that rejection or whatever can't happen without the player's say-so is slightly telling. The ST section on Touchstones (page 278-280) says that players should have a say in the destinies of their Touchstones.<br /> <br /> I honestly feel like the problem is differing perceptions of the rules here, not that one is a &quot;cheat&quot; somehow. You have certain expectations on what a Touchstone should be, your player has different, and because they don't line up, its a &quot;cheat&quot; despite fitting in by the rules. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's worked out ok, but it still feels wrong, for what appears to be the spirit of the rules. </div> </div> </div> And what, exactly, is wrong about it? So far, as near as I can tell, your reading and interpretation doesn't seem to match up with what I'm reading in the book.<br /> <br /> Now, if you said that the dog isn't challenging the character in any way, isn't making them ask any hard questions, isn't scared of the dog being hurt or killed, doesn't show moments of vulnerability? Then yes, I'd say that'd be an issue. Touchstones are supposed to make you think, make you vulnerable. So far, I haven't seen anything that suggests the dog isn't any of those things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I noticed that, but then, look at the example Touchstones in the book. I can't imagine <i>any</i> of them being around to talk someone down from frenzy. It seems like a mechanic more intended to keep you from accidentally frenzying and killing your touchstone than actually using you touchstone actively to avoid it. </div> </div> </div> Maybe, maybe not. You could be visiting a Touchstone, find out someone's abusing the Touchstone, and frenzy to kill the abuser. The Touchstone talks you down. There's a lot of possibilities in here, and focusing on just one is tunnel vision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's a great story, honestly. It makes for great italicized text. But in real play? That just feels like cheating even more than the dog. For one, there's zero risk. If your touchstone is something ephemeral, like a song, it is literally impossible to threaten or imperil your touchstone. Once again, you have total control over it and can even interact with it on your whim by just humming or singing the notes. That doesn't even match the mechanics where the touchstone is rolling and needs 3 x BP to stop the frenzy. What is this song's die pool? This kind of reinforces my &quot;Touchstones are awesome in theory, but only in theory&quot; thing. </div> </div> </div> In Werewolf, your Physical Touchstone can be a human religion. Think on that for a moment.<br /> <br /> For vulnerability? You have a precious song that means a lot, and its just been exposed in front of Elysium, with all the harpies. Open mocking season, anyone? The possibility of others ruining the song for you? How do you react to such situations? Its making drama and story. The Touchstone had fulfilled its purpose.<br /> <br /> As for dice pools? That is admittedly harder, but story comes first. If it makes a good story, then it should be allowed. As for the dice pool? I don't know, how do gravestones work on talking you down? Non-human Touchstones are supposed to be rare, and how they function is slightly glossed over. But they're still meant to be entirely viable by the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of them acted human at all after they woke up. Now, it was partially the game's circumstances--they were all killed and then post mortem embraced. They woke up alone in dug up pine boxes and had to, basically, figure things out. So, they actually all avoided their human lives--they thought the people they loved and cared about knew they were dead. They immediately abandoned human life and leapt head first into vampire stuff, because, well, they had little choice. </div> </div> </div> In which case, abandoning Touchstones is probably appropriate. Your specific story does encourage them to remove the Touchstones from their lives.<br /> <br /> And I think it was a mistake on not rolling to detach. You're undermining what it means to become detached from human society and keep full Humanity. If your story starts off with a Condition, then so be it. It might actually have made the Touchstones seem more important to the characters, so you might be having issues by undermining the need for Touchstones in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think attending Sunday dinner would be ridiculous and foolish for a vampire, as you'd be risking detachment every week for no reason. </div> </div> </div> Except not. You're generally not Humanity 10 - 9, the only points where such a dinner would be a detachment. Most vampires don't get that high. I'm really getting the impression this is all about different perceptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, to me, a successful clan bane is one that influences you to (un)live in a specific manner such that your flaw is minimized. </div> </div> </div> Not a philosophy I agree with, but sure, we can go with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Daeva curse is great. You <i>must</i> feed from a series of victims. You cannot have a herd. You cannot keep blood dolls. You must feed &quot;promiscuously.&quot; Eating is never going to be easy. Ever. So, yes, the flaw &quot;never comes up,&quot; but only because you have cut out an entire feeding strategy from your playbook and chosen to live in a specific way, which, well, is the <i>real</i> flaw. </div> </div> </div> Or... you maintain a herd that you feed from and happen to be attached to. Or maybe you mix things up. Or maybe you feed exclusively from animals because you're one of the vamipres who are young enough and freak out at the idea of drinking from a human being. There are a half-million ways you can do it, as many options as you can imagine. Its really not that different from any other vampire feeding; you're just more attached to your herd than the average vamp. <br /> <br /> The rest I'm going to skip over, because this next part is what's important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which, yeah, brings me to Ventrue. They don't even have an additional roleplaying consequence (getting angrier, for example), they just have to spend their 1 XP and extra roleplaying touchstone effort 1 humanity earlier than everyone else. That's...just not a concern at all. That changes absolutely nothing, no new wrinkles, not even piled consequences, just exactly the same thing as every other vampire on a slightly advanced schedule. </div> </div> </div> The role play aspect is that Ventrue have a harder time caring about people. They just dont' connect with other humans as easily. The mechanics might not fill that exactly, but its definitely the intent of the flaw. Ventrue are more detached than the average vampire. And that is something one can easily role play out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My version of the flaw isn't <i>amazing</i>, which is why I came asking for more suggestions. It still just penalizes a thing that all vampires deal with. </div> </div> </div> All the clan Banes are penalties to a thing that vampires deal with. Daeva are more attached to their herds than the average vamp, but all vampires have an attachment of some sort. Ven are more detached from people, but that is something everyone struggles with. Nosferatu have to deal with people being grossed out by them more than the average. Gangrel have greater issues with Frenzy, but everyone has a bit of that. Mehket are more susceptable to the banes that all vampires have in common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't want it to become a big <i>thing</i>, but I don't really think tying derangements to humanity loss has any implications. I get that it was pretty awful for some people unfamiliar with the gothic horror mindset when normal humans who did bad things went crazy, but vampires who slid from human to inhuman literally losing their human mind? </div> </div> </div> The gothic horror mindset is what was flawed. It linked acting moral to mental illnesses, and was insulting to those who had those actual problems, effectively suggesting that it was due to being immoral people.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the problem here is that vampires aren't losing their human mind by gaining derangements. Derangements aren't acting like undead monsters that feast on people. Its not making them more predatorial, more like the Beast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, I'm not expecting it to come up, regardless. I just want a couple of crazy ventrue elders down the road. </div> </div> </div> And the truth comes out?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, let's say no players buy in at all. You basically ignore, downplay it, then, right? So, what do you do for the Ventrue flaw to make sure it still matters? </div> </div> </div> Honestly, I don't do anything. The flaws generally scale as players lose Humanity, but there are a number of work arounds for all of them. For Mehket, just avoid banes - something every vampire does. Nosferatu learn Majesty, Gangrel learn to better Ride the Wave, or get Coils. In my experience, none of the flaws really matter in the end. The Gangrel one is the only one I consider difficult, because frenzy is the only option. The rest I've found to be negligable unless the ST makes a focus on those kinds of stories where they do come up.<br /> <br /> Already, the Ven are disincentived from being empathetic, or more gentle persuasion. They lie, intimidate and command. Their Disciplines are geared towards avoiding Empathy or caring about people's choices or feelings. This serves as a carrot for the Ven acting the way any flaw I'd make up would anyways, so I don't see why I need more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-16-2016, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:42:51-07:00","id":848228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848161#post848161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, really? No Willpower from resting? I don't recall reading that. Hmm. I know they did in 1st edition, why the deliberate change?<br /> <br /> I will have to evaluate whether or not I should go with this new rule and change everything around or just keep running it the way I've been with an unwitting houserule.</div> </div> </div> </div> It was something that was intended to go in, but was accidently cut and not put back in. So, it depends on the game if its run that way. Why the change? Not quite sure myself, I never really read the full thing from Rose on the issue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:57:17-07:00","id":848236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848119#post848119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gosh, no. This is not the choice between Mask and Requiem/Dirge. Choosing Mask is not choosing humanity, it's choosing the lie, which you present to humanity. It's why they should not pull out pitchforks and torches. It has nothing to do with how connected to humanity you actually are.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're harping too much in a dichotomy that isn't even central to my argument. A vampire isn't human. They mimic humanity thru their mask. It's the only way to remember to empathize with the flock of vessels around them after their loved ones have crumbled to dust, regardless of self-interest. It's the only way they may come to remember that they aren't walking and breathing snack instead of feeling and thinking people.<br /> <br /> They fake it till they make it.<br /> <br /> If you aren't going to address my previous points, don't bother replying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dog feels like cheating because it's utterly under the character's sway. It's something that accompanies him everywhere. It doesn't have a choice, it has to deal with him. It's just an animal. There's no risk at all--no risk the guy you're stalking will spot you, no risk your old buddy will notice something is off, no risk you girlfriend from life will reject you. It's basically a slave.</div> </div> </div> </div>No risk? You take that dog into elysia and watch the first ventrue pull a power-play by having your faithful hound piss on you, literally. And that's the least they can do just to fuck with you. Go read my previous post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 03-16-2016, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:01:05-07:00","id":848242,"title":"","content":"In a Hunger like Fire Bruise had a dog. It snapped at a vampire and they smacked it to death. In the Silent Knife one of the older vampires had a dog too, though it was ghouled. Both were probably considered touchstones, links to who and what they used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-16-2016, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:02:07-07:00","id":848243,"title":"","content":"Couple thoughts, Storyteller:<br /> <br /> First - It's true that the initial implementations of Mask / Dirge / Touchstone tend to be clunky when players are first starting to get used to them. Part of your job as Storyteller is to be the gatekeeper on what a meaningful expression or interaction with their anchor is. Whenever I feel like it's becoming a rote expression, I straight up ask the player, &quot;Share with me how this is meaningful to your character. Did they learn anything about themselves, or did you as a player experience anything new about the character?&quot; If they come up with an honest answer, that's fine with me. After a few of these, assuming your players are in a zone more skewed toward the dramatic vs. mechanic, they shouldn't have trouble coming up with stuff.<br /> <br /> Second, I also had trouble getting Touchstones to 'work right' at my table when I was first transitioning from 1E to 2E until I took a much more thematic approach. I found more success when I started looking at Touchstones as a representation of a specific relationship the character has, through which the lens of humanity would be focused for that character. To distill that into more relateable terms, I come up with sort of a relationship archetype to represent the Touchstone. So, 'My young niece who might be showing latent psychic abilities' becomes, &quot;<i>The Prodigy</i>&quot; - and 'The streetkid who I helped get her life together after her parents disappeared' becomes &quot;<i>The Orphan.</i>&quot; I then do my best to make that relationship archetype a theme of the character's interactions in the world. The Orphan is causing one character to deal with a lot of abandonment themes, while the Prodigy shades the second with themes of unrealized potential.<br /> <br /> I put it this way to my players now. &quot;Every Vampire has to personally experience the conflict between man and beast, human and kindred. Think of a type of relationship or archetype (Patron, Matron, Child, Bully, Con Man, Lawyer, Sibling, Lover, Enemy, Rival, Pet, Saboteur, etc.) that you want to represent on a thematic level that struggle or experience for your character. Now, think of a person who is important to your vampire who represents that type of archetype as a character. That person is your Touchstone.&quot; And, if the player more just has a stock character like a bartender, then I'll just reverse engineer a couple of options like, &quot;The Confidant,&quot; &quot;The Enabler,&quot; &quot;The Party Boy,&quot; and let them choose which one they like the best.<br /> <br /> Finally, let me second the good idea that MCN and others mentioned about representing Touchstones with other Merits. Retainer, Herd, etc. Anything which draws the Touchstone closer to the vampiric orbit, only increases the chances that the Touchstone will be more involved in the night-to-night stories. I'm currently toying with the idea of even giving an XP discount to such purchases. (1 XP = 2 Dots of Merits) to encourage this even more.<br /> <br /> But, at the end of the day, If you are keeping the 1 WP refresh per night, I do think you are eliminating a big mechanical function of Touchstones. That, combined with it maybe being a little too proactive ST / Reactive PC - I don't think you'd lose too much if you just cut them out. Rejiggering Breaking Points and the Ventrue Flaw being the obvious ones which you're already addressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:36:21-07:00","id":848296,"title":"","content":"Looks like I missed some points.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848097#post848097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think MCN asks a very good question: in the current chronicle, what mortals are your PCs actually interacting with the most and consider to be the most important to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it would be their feudal lord's ghouled personal assistant, probably. They've spoken to her more days than they haven't. Otherwise, they've never had more than brief contact with any humans.<br /> <br /> So far (again, this is about a week in game played over a dozen or so sessions), they've fed a few times. They encountered the former police man's land lord and told him he wasn't really dead, just under cover, so, he had to keep quiet, but it was ok to act like he was dead and resell the apartment and whatnot. They encountered the drug dealer's former girlfriend because he wanted his car. He died a john doe, so, she didn't know. But, for months before, he pretended he was in rehab and she knew he was lying, so, she sold his car and cheated on him. Another pc convinced her he was working for the cops as a CI, so, he had to lie. She felt terrible, but instead of pursuing the relationship at all, he told her to use the money to pay off a debt his family had occurred from his drug habit and intends to never see her again.<br /> <br /> And that's it. So far, it's basically just been further severing ties with humans, eating, and talking to a ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:59:40-07:00","id":848309,"title":"","content":"you could consider simply giving a touchstone to players who show the inclination toward developping them as a bulwark against theyre declining humanity. For those that dont care it doesnt really matter since its not like if you lose humanity you lose the game. It just depends on what aspect of the vampire unlife you and your players wish to work on. <br /> <br /> Tho i like the idea of beginning (seconds after the embrace) at humanity 10 and steadily declining until you stabilize at humanity 7. It can help show the dissociation between a vampire old life and his new unlife. I'd go with lose a humanity at the first feeding (dropping from 10 to 9) then another when you first learn and use a discipline (dropping from 9 to 8) and ... i dont know which last element from normal everynight unlife would cause the last drop. But i like the idea as a tool for the prelude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T14:15:18-07:00","id":848406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848201#post848201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, I don't think I like people constantly chasing their Dirges and Masks like that. It ends up feeling forced and weird. I'd rather people roleplay naturally in character, rather than looking at what they wrote down when the game started and just forcing that stereotype onto every scene. They become flanderized, then. Instead of deep characters, you get, &quot;I'm QUESTIONING! Whoo! Question!&quot; I don't want to encourage that.<br /> <br /> I can't even imagine the normal game flow. &quot;Oh, that scene was tough. I call my mom, then go beat up a random drunk guy.&quot; &quot;What?&quot; &quot;Yeah, I lost a lot of willpower, so, I need to interact with my touchstone and be a Monster.&quot; That's just bizarre. It seems like those rules are written for people who don't know how to roleplay at all and need constant coaching to act in character at all (&quot;ok, always remember that I'm a Jester, got it.&quot;).<br /> <br /> That's also daunting for a GM. I like to run games with nothing but dice in front of me. I don't have notes or sheets or anything. But how am I supposed to remember 2 unusual willpower triggers per character (so, for my game, upwards of 10 when everyone can make it)? If I rely on players to cue me, it'll be worse, because then I'll be getting constantly interrupted by, &quot;hey, so, do I get my willpower back for that?&quot; every other sentence. Sounds like a nightmare.<br /> <br /> I'll talk to my group about it, but I think I'd rather keep the Willpower from rest as the main way to get it.<br /> <br /> This whole thread is really making me wish I could just watch a game session run by someone doing it &quot;correctly&quot; and by the book. I've been running roleplaying games for more than 20 years now, and I can't picture this working well.<br /> <br /> That sort of works for me because you need to direct all social situations down pathways where your specific skills are relevant, but I think everyone already does that in general. -3 is bad compared to -1, but I don't ever see people volunteering to use -1s, either, and social skills are never like, a surprise. You can act in specific ways to control which skill you roll. Better than the Touchstone thing, yeah, but, it that feels insufficient for my purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I feel like if your players are going &quot;Oh that scene was hard I am going to call my mom&quot; That there is something way more wrong, fundamentally, than touchstones. Charlaquin and I both seem to be having a great time working the touchstone system. Hell your players might even have touchstones but not realize what they are. Do any of your players have friends? lovers? Family? From their life before? Or even someone they fed off and feel guilty about now they just watch and take care of this person from a distance?<br /> <br /> The mask and dirge should be natural things for your players. They shouldnt be forced. my group who has been gaming for 10 years or so already had a lot of these things, now they just have names. Touchstones, Mask/dirge help make fleshed out characters .. something thats more than just dice and paper.... <br /> <br /> <br /> I dont want to quote everything. It seems to bog it all down. But Someone said that a ghoul cant be a touchstone?? I would like to point out there are merits that require you to be both. Beloved. I like the example where the ghoul was taking you out to the movies, or catching you up on social things. I think that is perfect way to keep you human. Or just having a heart beat around might remind you of what you lost.. and remind you what it was like. &quot;I remember when I had a heart beat..&quot; ect... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T14:56:01-07:00","id":848429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848103#post848103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Time to learn 3 disciplines&quot; especially stands out to me</div> </div> </div> </div>It stands out to me, as well. I give all vampires one dot in each of their clan disciplines when newly created. It makes clans feel more distinct (EVERY Ventrue can talk to animals, mesmerize, and resist some damage), gives players a wide base to work with, and prevents power disparity. Even though every dot costs the same number of XP, it's hard to argue that the first dot of a discipline is ever as powerful as the third.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848115#post848115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your problem seems to be that you aren't using touchstones as they are intended: This is, to be catalysts for drama and conflict. What happens when a Daeva takes Bob as a blood doll, because their clan bane makes the succubus obsessed with him? What happens when a Mekhet Hound keeps tabs on the character, finds out his touchstones and delivers pictures to the PC in a clear threat to him should he not do as he's told? How do you convince your coterie to give a fuck about Bob and help you one-up the Daeva or the Mekhet?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I admit I may not be playing them correctly, but if what you describe is correctly, I'm not interested in it.<br /> <br /> What happens when Bob becomes a blood doll for a Daeva? I buy Bob a lottery ticket, that's what. Hundreds of thousands of people and the Daeva picks the guy I know? Really? And it's a Daeva foolish enough to feed from someone twice, rather than, you know, not becoming obsessed with a mortal for no reason? What are the odds of this? This is the kind of stuff that really bothers me about &quot;story games&quot; like FATE or Dogs in the Vineyard. I'm trying to play a roleplaying game here, not a story game. I don't want to directly mess with the story and try to make everything as interesting as possible all the time. I want things to be consistent and full of verisimilitude. I want the setting to be predictable (within the parameters set by the rules and our twists, of course). It seems like Bob becomes a target solely because he knows a PC. It is exceedingly unlikely to happen in any other way. That's heavy handed story manipulation, and just not the kind of thing we're interested in.<br /> <br /> The Mekhet Hound watching your touchstones.well, yes, that makes sense, absolutely. It's part of why I think a song, a car, or even your pet dog is a little inappropriate. You don't ever leave those things alone or vulnerable. You convince your coterie, though, because, uh, they're your coterie, so you guys do that kind of stuff for each other. I'm not interested in PvP roleplaying. I'd join a LARP if I wanted that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848115#post848115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's better yet, how do you manouver the coterie into helping you, without tipping your hand as to why you are so opposed to the smug Mekhet Hound? Or does your character simply complies to the threats, and eventually forces you to go against your coterie's politic aims in a climax? Which do you choose? The mask, or the requiem?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't imagine a scenario in which the game runs smoothly and the other PCs don't know who your touchstones are. Unless you're doing play by post or email or something primarily, that's a lot of solo play which would get mighty frustrating at a real table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848115#post848115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not everything that goes on in the game should be displayed to the whole table. The above scenarios wouldn't. Email your players between sessions, text them or hold 1 on 1 sessions concerning these private issues over the phone, or skype. It works wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that requires very specific kinds of players/groups interested in that kind of play. We are not that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848115#post848115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dog as a touchstone works, because anybody using animalism on it will predispose such complications. Do you take it to elysium? Did you ghoul it, so you won't risk detachment in say, 10 years? How does your character feels about violating the nature of such a loyal companion on such a manner?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Elysium isn't a big thing in this city, honestly. And, also, the dog is a ghoul and the PC has animalism already, so, it'd be really hard for some random NPC to come up and control him. Not only because the guy is right there with counter powers, but also because that's obvious and rude. Nobody in polite society would do that, and vampire society is nothing if not surface level polite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848115#post848115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding your STing style? Shit happens. STs are there to drop the shit on the moving fans. Otherwise it woudn't be much of a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, and my style has worked very well for many years. When I run Vampire, I like to build a complex city of sandcastles, then let the players run wild, either living in it, or kicking it down as they see fit. I build everything, then just keep it running as it would logically run, and the PCs gum up the works and make stuff happen. I don't have a specific story or quest in mind, just an open world to play with. I guess I'll explain my setting in another post later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848226#post848226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's even a section in the book talking about non-human Touchstones. Yes, they are rare. But they are very much part of the game. As long as it meets the rough guidelines, its allowed by the ruels.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I know they're allowed by the rules, but that doesn't mean I have to like them. They were very obviously trying to take the easiest possible touchstones, so that they could effectively ignore the subsystem. Nobody was playing in good faith, genuinely feeling like these things connected them to humanity. They were just trying to use the touchstone system to further lay protections on their stuff. They were layering Merit dots on their protected things, basically, so that our social contract would keep them safe. A touchstone that's also a Haven is that much harder to attack. If someone wants a super nice car they couldn't afford (in this case, a '67 Cobra), make it a touchstone! Of course it's cool! How about a weapon? It's hard to get weapons when you wake up dead with none of your possessions. If I make up some ancestral daisho as a touchstnoe, the GM can't take my katana away! Trust me, the party was crapping on the touchstone system when they went for nonhumans.<br /> <br /> I tried. I really tried to get them in the spirit of it. They ended up with things I thought sounded perfectly in line with the examples in the book. The Yakuza hitman was a tattoo artist, so, he chose a woman he had given a particularly beautiful tattoo to in life--she barely knew him, but that beautiful tattoo, his life's best work, reminds him of his mortal job and life. It was awesome! And then, uh, he made zero effort to look for her in any way whatsoever, over almost three months of play. In fact, I've repeatedly tried to draw in his tattoo business into the game--NPCs notice and comment on his tattoos. He started wearing long sleeves so they'd stop.<br /> <br /> This is just one example of many. None of them care. It is clearly a &quot;get this mechanic away from me, here, I'll make it basically a magic item.&quot; Then, when I pushed, they did exactly what, honestly, I would probably do: &quot;I'll come up with something fancy and cool so he'll get off my back.&quot;<br /> <br /> No, talking with the group, nobody was excited by the Touchstone system. Everyone considered a chore. In the end, I discovered that I agree. As great as it sounded in theory, it just didn't work in practice.<br /> <br /> That said, as far as that section being in the rules, look, I played and ran quite a bit of Geist, ok? I am very conscious of the fact that these books are made and edited by human beings, and not amazingly well paid ones at that (not that they don't deserve to be, just that they aren't, so, volume of work sometimes has to take precedence over meticulous care). Sometimes, shit happens during production. Sometimes, two authors work on the same section and their work is jammed together. Sometimes, like in Geist, two directly contradictory things get printed in the same book because different authors had different ideas and editing didn't perfectly marry them. It struck me that the vast majority of stuff written on Touchstones seemed to suggest one thing, while the two sentences or whatever on places and objects as touchstones, plus that one merit requiring a ghoul touchstone, were out of line with everything else. Obviously, you can disagree, and the actual writers/editors can correct me, but it just struck me as out of place, so, I went more with the general feel over those specific unusual exceptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848226#post848226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And is it possible that part of the problem be that, as an NPC, the Storyteller don't have control over it? Honestly, I think that the mere fact that you are complaining that rejection or whatever can't happen without the player's say-so is slightly telling. The ST section on Touchstones (page 278-280) says that players should have a say in the destinies of their Touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>While my group and I definitely play in such a way that the player controls their character completely and otherwise only interacts with the world in ways that character could, that's honestly not the issue. I don't really want control. I just want weird or unusual rules, like touchstones to either have teeth (i.e., a point to be in the game) or I want them out. If you let the PCs determine how important touchstones are to the game, and they universally ignore it, why include them at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848226#post848226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if you said that the dog isn't challenging the character in any way, isn't making them ask any hard questions, isn't scared of the dog being hurt or killed, doesn't show moments of vulnerability? Then yes, I'd say that'd be an issue. Touchstones are supposed to make you think, make you vulnerable. So far, I haven't seen anything that suggests the dog isn't any of those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the dog isn't making him ask hard questions, nor is he scared of the dog being hurt or killed. It's not vulnerable at all. Dogs are ridiculously badass in WoD. Have you looked at their stats? Big attack pool, high defense...add blood and disciplines in there, his dog is the best fighter in the party by far. What he has is an amazing weapon that can also track, relatively &quot;story protected&quot; due to its status as a retainer and a touchstone. He can even talk to it with Animalism, and command it to break its nature via the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848226#post848226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Werewolf, your Physical Touchstone can be a human religion. Think on that for a moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf has touchstones, too, now? Ugh, don't tell me every supernatural is going to be saddled with them. I am anxiously awaiting Changeling 2nd...I sure hope they're not dependent on this, too.<br /> <br /> Hmm, if nothing else, at least I have learned from this thread that I actually do not like touchstones. At first, I just thought it was the players. Or that we did it wrong. But no, now I am fairly convicted that I don't like them, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848226#post848226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for dice pools? That is admittedly harder, but story comes first. If it makes a good story, then it should be allowed. As for the dice pool? I don't know, how do gravestones work on talking you down? Non-human Touchstones are supposed to be rare, and how they function is slightly glossed over. But they're still meant to be entirely viable by the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, forgive me for this, but it seems like you're saying, &quot;You shouldn't dislike touchstones because the rules say this. Oh, they don't? Well, they should. So, like it.&quot; I mean, I get where you're coming from and I'm glad you like touchstones, honestly, but I don't think I do. Sorry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848226#post848226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or... you maintain a herd that you feed from and happen to be attached to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yikes, why would ever do that? Why would you want to make yourself obsessed? I see nothing to gain there. That's....bizarre. I can't imagine a game where Daeva do that on purpose beyond, say, their first victim, or maybe it's a desperate situation/accident. I don't know, wow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848226#post848226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the clan Banes are penalties to a thing that vampires deal with. Daeva are more attached to their herds than the average vamp, but all vampires have an attachment of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am really intrigued, actually, based on this and your previous comments, how we came to entirely different conclusions about how Daeva act. You say they're more attached to their Herds, while I interpreted them as being unable to have Herds. That's the sign of a good flaw, I think--we're both right despite holding opposite viewpoints.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848228#post848228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It was something that was intended to go in, but was accidently cut and not put back in. So, it depends on the game if its run that way. Why the change? Not quite sure myself, I never really read the full thing from Rose on the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found the thread and read it. I think I'm going to stick with it, though. I prefer it to what seems like the intended way Mask/Dirge/Touchstones work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848236#post848236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No risk? You take that dog into elysia and watch the first ventrue pull a power-play by having your faithful hound piss on you, literally. And that's the least they can do just to fuck with you. Go read my previous post.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned, I am downplaying Elysium a little, and I also think that it would be totally against protocol to walk up to someone's dog and animalism control them right in front of you. That's something that, I believe, would be met with disappointed head shakes and shunning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848243#post848243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, at the end of the day, If you are keeping the 1 WP refresh per night, I do think you are eliminating a big mechanical function of Touchstones. That, combined with it maybe being a little too proactive ST / Reactive PC - I don't think you'd lose too much if you just cut them out. Rejiggering Breaking Points and the Ventrue Flaw being the obvious ones which you're already addressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your points were all good ones, but, I don't think we're interested in playing in that style you're suggesting. So, yes, this is the path we're sticking with, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848309#post848309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you could consider simply giving a touchstone to players who show the inclination toward developping them as a bulwark against theyre declining humanity. For those that dont care it doesnt really matter since its not like if you lose humanity you lose the game. It just depends on what aspect of the vampire unlife you and your players wish to work on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I basically did that. We agreed that anyone showing obvious, real interest in a human could utilize many of the touchstone benefits while suffering some of the penalties. The only ones we did away with, really were the ones making them required. The +2/-2 for having/not having attached touchstones. That 4 die swing is too much to ignore. In order to make it something that only those who like and are interested in the system have to buy into, I felt removing that bonus/penalty was necessary. I said they can still use them to break frenzy, to gain willpower, to ignore the Nosferatu flaw, etc., but if they have them, they're also subject to Humanity loss if they are destroyed, and frenzy when they're threatened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848309#post848309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tho i like the idea of beginning (seconds after the embrace) at humanity 10 and steadily declining until you stabilize at humanity 7. It can help show the dissociation between a vampire old life and his new unlife. I'd go with lose a humanity at the first feeding (dropping from 10 to 9) then another when you first learn and use a discipline (dropping from 9 to 8) and ... i dont know which last element from normal everynight unlife would cause the last drop. But i like the idea as a tool for the prelude.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that kind of play would just be frustrating. Even though falling would be normal and expected, it'd be frustrating that you basically have no hope of not failing. And, honestly, rereading the Humanity levels, I still picture Humanity over 7 as being more human than humans.<br /> <br /> Like, imagine Civil War re-enactors. They surely know more about the Civil War than actual Civil War soldiers, yeah? It's the same way I imagine Humanity over 7 working. You know more about being human than actual humans because you've purposefully studied, perhaps even obsessed, over it. You've done things to understand that people actually living that way never have. Oh, one more metaphor: many, if not most, native New Yorkers have never been to the Empire State Building or the Statue of Liberty. I, myself, live within 20 minutes of Philadelphia and I've never seen the Liberty Bell. I couldn't even tell you how to get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  typo 03-16-2016, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T15:11:18-07:00","id":848434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848429#post848429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the kind of stuff that really bothers me about &quot;story games&quot; like FATE or Dogs in the Vineyard. I'm trying to play a roleplaying game here, not a story game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, this is the problem right here entirely. Anchors are absolutely dramatic tools, i.e. built for narrative games, not simulationist games. In fact, I would go so far as to say that 2E is specifically moving much more directly toward the 'story-game' vs. 'roleplaying-game' end of your spectrum. All the new systems and disciplines seem to me pretty much designed for that, so this will probably be a recurring theme for you throughout your process. I'd seriously consider if you want to make the jump at all, really, to 2E in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T15:42:44-07:00","id":848446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848406#post848406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mask and dirge should be natural things for your players. They shouldnt be forced. my group who has been gaming for 10 years or so already had a lot of these things, now they just have names. Touchstones, Mask/dirge help make fleshed out characters .. something thats more than just dice and paper....</div> </div> </div> </div>So, my counter is this: you've got these things naturally through normal roleplay. Why mechanize them, then? Why not just be happy with the way they're already working, rather than diluting it with a Pavlovian system?<br /> <br /> If you're already roleplaying the way you enjoy, why add a system that hands out rewards for doing the same thing? Especially because the additional rewards could end up harming normal flow, making people act out of character in order to earn the reward when they need it, rather than just when it's appropriate?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848434#post848434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, this is the problem right here entirely. Anchors are absolutely dramatic tools, i.e. built for narrative games, not simulationist games. In fact, I would go so far as to say that 2E is specifically moving much more directly toward the 'story-game' vs. 'roleplaying-game' end of your spectrum. All the new systems and disciplines seem to me pretty much designed for that, so this will probably be a recurring theme for you throughout your process. I'd seriously consider if you want to make the jump at all, really, to 2E in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am noticing that. In the past, WoD games were always my favorite, and I explained to people that, while the books constantly insisted they were storytelling/narrative games, they absolutely weren't. They were some of the best simulation around. I mean, seriously, nothing with a weight lifting chart is a story game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I love parts of 2nd edition. Mostly, the changes to the disciplines, merits, and combat. !st edition combat was, oh crap, terrible. I often called it a murder system, not a combat system. You just tried to go first and throw enough dice to one shot the other guy. Yuck. So, the game is way better balanced now. But, I'm starting to notice all those nonsense claims about being a storytelling/narrative game are, well, starting to get backed up. And those are the mechanics I'm noticing that I dislike, honestly. I'll probably be sticking to 2e and pulling most of those storytelling things out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":". 03-16-2016, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T15:46:01-07:00","id":848449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848434#post848434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, this is the problem right here entirely. Anchors are absolutely dramatic tools, i.e. built for narrative games, not simulationist games. In fact, I would go so far as to say that 2E is specifically moving much more directly toward the 'story-game' vs. 'roleplaying-game' end of your spectrum. All the new systems and disciplines seem to me pretty much designed for that, so this will probably be a recurring theme for you throughout your process. I'd seriously consider if you want to make the jump at all, really, to 2E in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, this is explicitly said by the devs, pretty much all the 2e mechanics are aiming towards fostering role-play and good story through use of the mechanics.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2698\" data-vbnamecard=\"2698\">The Storyteller</a> This ties into the other aspects of your problems I think. It seems that you (and your players) see Humanity going down as punishment, something to be avoided. But the devs have said that it is really supposed to go down, because that's the overall story of a vampire, slowly losing touch with humanity and facing their inner Beast. As a reference, since you seemed surprised by Werewolves having Touchstones (not all do by the way, just certain splats were it makes sense), Werewolf Harmony is now a balance scale, where the 'ideal' is to be at 5 but that is very difficult to maintain and you will likley slide back and forth around it. That's Flesh (mostly acting like a Human) at 10 and Spirit (acting like a Spirit) at 0.<br /> <br /> How have you worked with Aspirations? Because those are really in the same area for this kind of thing, they are there to foster the Storyteller to do things.<br /> <br /> Edit: A bit Ninjad by the OP, but I think my points still stand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T15:54:48-07:00","id":848455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848449#post848449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How have you worked with Aspirations? Because those are really in the same area for this kind of thing, they are there to foster the Storyteller to do things.<br /> <br /> Edit: A bit Ninjad by the OP, but I think my points still stand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? Everyone wrote them down session one. A couple people did a couple on their list (mostly &quot;find a Haven&quot; for all 5 and &quot;get my dog&quot; for the one), and then we eventually all forgot about them. I think I could only name a single aspiration that anyone has (one of them wants to find out who killed them), and I doubt any of the players would remember, either, without looking at the sheet.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I think we're ignoring or downplaying: touchstones, mask/dirge, aspirations, beats, the whole social doors system, City/Clan/Covenant Status, and like half of the feeding/hunting rules. I guess it's probably most accurate to say that we are playing 1st edition with 2nd edition rules? I don't know. We started with everything and just phased out all that stuff that felt off--basically all the story game stuff, yeah.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T16:03:16-07:00","id":848460,"title":"","content":"In the interest of full disclosure, let me explain the setting I'm working with in order to make it all clear why certain setting sanctions aren't sufficient:<br /> <br /> The game is set in Vancouver. A specific bloodline of vampires who are all related directly to the Prince are in total control. Every position of power is held by this specific family. The other vampires in the city have pushed and sort of forced in a feudal system as an attempt to gain power, but it mostly failed. The family maintained a concrete ceiling on power and remained at the top of every feudal chain. What's more, they make it easy to be a vampire. They have all kinds of support ready for vampires to, say, hide bodies or acquire havens, etc. They have a series of smart phone apps with disguised real information about vampiric life for neonates. They are always telling everyone that their goal is to make life in Vancouver easy and simple. Vampires don't need to worry about anything. They only ask for a single thing in response: if they call you and ask you to hunt down a specific person, you do it. See, the family in charge is in charge due to a pact made with some True Fae, and it is dependent on the vampires of the city returning escaped Changelings to their former masters. <br /> <br /> So, there are groups of vampires embraced and raised in Vancouver who just have no idea how to exist outside of Vancouver, because everything is just done for them and they just have to help out catching changelings every once in a while. There are others, though, that are discontent with the lack of agency, with the iron fist they are ruled. Everything is easy, but doing everything for everyone means nobody can survive without you. There are secret wars all the time over controlling city assets, but the family in charge always wins. Nobody down the line really has any clue how the city works. They just hit an easy button on their city mandated phones.<br /> <br /> The PCs were post mortem embraced and just left to fend for themselves and figure things out.<br /> <br /> I figure they'll play quite some time, get into trouble, rely on this family to save them, and then, the rug gets pulled away. There's actually someone hunting and killing the family in charge. Eventually, they'll all be gone, and the whole city of vampires will just have no idea what to do, how to live, how to take control...it'll be chaos. Fascinating chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T16:28:31-07:00","id":848471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848455#post848455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Everyone wrote them down session one. A couple people did a couple on their list (mostly &quot;find a Haven&quot; for all 5 and &quot;get my dog&quot; for the one), and then we eventually all forgot about them. I think I could only name a single aspiration that anyone has (one of them wants to find out who killed them), and I doubt any of the players would remember, either, without looking at the sheet.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I think we're ignoring or downplaying: touchstones, mask/dirge, aspirations, beats, the whole social doors system, City/Clan/Covenant Status, and like half of the feeding/hunting rules. I guess it's probably most accurate to say that we are playing 1st edition with 2nd edition rules? I don't know. We started with everything and just phased out all that stuff that felt off--basically all the story game stuff, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A lot of things in 2e are gonna need to change for you then. Good luck with that. The forums will help, but you really need to include the idea that you don't like any of this stuff when you do, cause it will save a lot of time and angst. Personally, I feel like that cleans up this side conversation. Its enough to know that you don't like these things, the question now is how to replace the mechanics that tie into them. I don't have anything to suggest on that that hasn't already been said. So I will bow out for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T18:41:00-07:00","id":848531,"title":"","content":"Ok, yeah. CofD is a storytelling game. It's about immersion, drama and conflict, and all of it's mechanics are based on that. You seem to be playing D&amp;D with vampires, to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:05:09-07:00","id":848541,"title":"","content":"(Commenting from phone) I will weight in more later but I kinda feel like the current tone is 'ooohhh, you want sim? Yeah, Wod doesn't do that' and so right off, I disagree. ElvesofZion is right in that knowing your preference saves angst and means we can tailor discussion more to be beneficial to you. However, I think the 'soft-systems' that encouraged role-play still can be made hard or justified. Off the bat for example: Dirge as a means to recover willpower. While we may not want to encourage flanderised roleplay, I still think Dirge is an excellent sort hand for simulating a persons need to stay true to themselves amidst the lies. As in, the roleplay encouragement is greater emphasis on sim, not less. I raise this flag of protest not to be a nuisance but because I really enjoy sim and that is why I'd love to discussion that really drill down to the core, as oppose to abandon them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T19:48:23-07:00","id":848564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848471#post848471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The forums will help, but you really need to include the idea that you don't like any of this stuff when you do, cause it will save a lot of time and angst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you're right. I hadn't really thought about it, though, until this thread.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848531#post848531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, yeah. CofD is a storytelling game. It's about immersion, drama and conflict, and all of it's mechanics are based on that. You seem to be playing D&amp;D with vampires, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to be honest, I don't even know what CofD stands for. What I will say is that, from the start of the world of darkness, people have claimed it to be a &quot;storytelling game&quot; and, well, it wasn't. It claimed to be up and down in every book they published, but it wasn't at all. So, yes, now with this second edition, they're finally backing up their talk, but that doesn't mean I don't belong here or something.<br /> <br /> And also for the record, I am actually after immersion. That's my number one goal with a roleplaying game. To get immersion, though, one needs the world to work, well, like a world actually would. Directly manipulating a story, pushing drama and conflict, that's literally the opposite of immersion. That is stepping outside of your character specifically to interact with meta-mechanics. That gets to a great story full with lots of twists, drama, etc., but it doesn't get you immersion. It gets you a world that doesn't make sense, but you don't care because you got a good story out of it. I want the world to make sense. I want everything to happen in a logical fashion, and the story will emerge later, when we talk about what happened.<br /> <br /> It's a different mindset, and neither one of us is right or better, nor are either one of us better suited to use this game to play our own way. And if we're using the outdated terms from the &quot;big theory,&quot; D&amp;D is more gamist than simulation. Maybe old school AD&amp;D was sim, but 3rd edition on? Pretty damn Gamist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848541#post848541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I think the 'soft-systems' that encouraged role-play still can be made hard or justified. Off the bat for example: Dirge as a means to recover willpower. While we may not want to encourage flanderised roleplay, I still think Dirge is an excellent sort hand for simulating a persons need to stay true to themselves amidst the lies. As in, the roleplay encouragement is greater emphasis on sim, not less. I raise this flag of protest not to be a nuisance but because I really enjoy sim and that is why I'd love to discussion that really drill down to the core, as oppose to abandon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to be clear about my objection to these systems. It's not because I want them hard, it's because I want to encourage actual immersion in the characters. I actually think these sorts of things <i>break immersion. </i>All of those storytelling reward mechanics, like FATE points or getting willpower back, they create reward cycles that encourage people to take specific actions. In storytelling games, those specific actions tend to be those that either highlight aspects of your characters or those that create more drama. When that's what you want, it's perfect. When you want something more, something like real immersion in a character so that they act, you know, like a real person and not like a character in a drama, those reward cycles are an obstacle. It will create an internal conflict for players between immersing and getting rewarded. I'd rather just trust they'll do it right without a carrot and stick to force them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T20:23:33-07:00","id":848577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848564#post848564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI have to be honest, I don't even know what CofD stands for. What I will say is that, from the start of the world of darkness, people have claimed it to be a &quot;storytelling game&quot; and, well, it wasn't. It claimed to be up and down in every book they published, but it wasn't at all. So, yes, now with this second edition, they're finally backing up their talk, but that doesn't mean I don't belong here or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe anyone has said you don't belong here, but you've expressed a disliking for almost every aspect of the game, even down to having paper in front of you to help you remember personal ambitions. And you've claimed to have simply not used other aspects of the game. And you go further to say that you want something, immersion, that you think the game doesn't offer.<br /> <br /> So why are you playing this game?<br /> <br /> You like the Disciplines, merits and combat? Why not just play with those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T20:45:24-07:00","id":848587,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2698\" data-vbnamecard=\"2698\">The Storyteller</a> Your definition of immersion doesn't adds up. Unless it's a convoluted mess in which you, yourself, as ST seek immersion in the setting. That's not going to work well if your players want a personal experience with fully fledged multidimensional characters. Which the anchors provide tools to. Otherwise it's like playing the archetypes of mask and dirge like alignments, then disregarding touchstones and the purpose of Humanity in personal horror like D&amp;D characters usually disregard every conceivable notion of attachment that could be threatened for plot reasons. BTW, if everything in your setting has to be neurotically planned for? I can come up with a dozen reasons of why a Daeva harpy would become specifically infatuated with a given touchstone. Beyond fucking with a particular PC.<br /> <br /> Horror is about loss. Loss of self. Loss of one's humanity as it trickles down the drain of the dance macabre. Loss of your loved ones to the machinations of the Requiem or the sheer, inexorable weight of the ages. That's what Requiem is about, to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 03-16-2016, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T20:56:11-07:00","id":848591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848564#post848564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI have to be honest, I don't even know what CofD stands for.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's... right at the top of the page.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> The official name of World of Darkness 2e.<br /> <br /> CofD instead of CoD to keep it from sounding like a certain videogame franchise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T21:53:46-07:00","id":848605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848577#post848577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe anyone has said you don't belong here, but you've expressed a disliking for almost every aspect of the game, even down to having paper in front of you to help you remember personal ambitions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, you play one way, I play another. I expressed dislike for like 5 things in a massive system. 5 things that seem pretty minor to me. I would even still say this is my favorite roleplaying game. I don't have to like every single aspect of a thing to like it in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848577#post848577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And you've claimed to have simply not used other aspects of the game. And you go further to say that you want something, immersion, that you think the game doesn't offer.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game does offer it with some changes the group made kind of automatically without thinking about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848577#post848577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S o why are you playing this game?<br /> <br /> You like the Disciplines, merits and combat? Why not just play with those?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, we are. I basically came to this forum to get fix for the ventrue and then discovered along the way why I wanted to change stuff. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848587#post848587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your definition of immersion doesn't adds up. Unless it's a convoluted mess in which you, yourself, as ST seek immersion in the setting. That's not going to work well if your players want a personal experience with fully fledged multidimensional characters. Which the anchors provide tools to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really understand why that's the conclusion you came to. But, I guess I am not surprised, as I have had trouble in the past explaining my style to story gamers.<br /> <br /> What my group does is immerse in their characters. They don't need meta mechanics leading them to play their characters &quot;properly.&quot; Because they are immersed, they just, you know, do it. Interacting with this extra mechanic giving them incentive to role play in a specific manner interferes with this immersion because they will be, in all circumstances, drawn to roleplay in a specific way that isn't always appropriate for the character. <br /> <br /> If my character is a smartass, I might take jester. Now, instead of just naturally playing my character as a smartass, which includes NOT being a smartass at certain times, I am just going to always be looking to make a joke no matter what, for the willpower. At a funeral? Who gives a shit, I could get willpower.<br /> <br /> &quot;But wait,&quot; one might say, &quot;that's bad roleplaying. That's the person's fault, nut the system. They should only make those jokes if their character would anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah-ha! Yes,&quot; I respond, &quot;so, if they already know when that is and would do it anyway, why add a reward system? Why not just let them be and trust them to do it?&quot;<br /> <br /> As for me, I don't immerse in the setting...no, I never do that in any media. But I do immerse in the npcs. Npcs always talk as themselves, and react realistically as fully fledged, three dimensional people would. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848587#post848587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise it's like playing the archetypes of mask and dirge like alignments, then disregarding touchstones and the purpose of Humanity in personal horror like D&amp;D characters usually disregard every conceivable notion of attachment that could be threatened for plot reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is the weirdest jump in logic I have ever seen. I honestly really dislike D&amp;D (3rd and up) because it encourages murder hoboing and because it's less of a roleplaying game than a tactical combat game that allows and expects some roleplaying in it sometimes. It's as much &quot;not a roleplaying game&quot; to me as Dogs in the Vineyard is, just for different reasons.<br /> <br /> I actually kind if saved my current gaming group from d&amp;d. They'd all roleplaying for years without ever trying another game. I got them hooked on savage worlds, my second favorite rpg, and now I am working in getting them to love my first.<br /> <br /> And I hate alignment in d&amp;d. I have never used it...just house ruled it right out the window first thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848587#post848587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, if everything in your setting has to be neurotically planned for? I can come up with a dozen reasons of why a Daeva harpy would become specifically infatuated with a given touchstone. Beyond fucking with a particular PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely don't have anything meticulously planned. That sounds lie some kind of hell. I like to be surprised, too. I plan almost nothing. I just set up the first domino and then watch, making sure stuff cascades in the correct fashion.<br /> <br /> The players are their characters. I am everything else, making sure the pcs feel like they're in a real world that makes logical sense, that decisions they make ripple realistically (or, more accurately, with verisimilitude).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848587#post848587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horror is about loss. Loss of self. Loss of one's humanity as it trickles down the drain of the dance macabre. Loss of your loved ones to the machinations of the Requiem or the sheer, inexorable weight of the ages. That's what Requiem is about, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's cool. Requiem to me is about how these human beings the players have made react to being a vampire in the city I set up. Being a vampire is kind of horrific, so, there's definitely personal horror. But I don't artificially create horror or drama, I let those things flow naturally from the choices players make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848591#post848591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's... right at the top of the page.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> The official name of World of Darkness 2e.<br /> <br /> CofD instead of CoD to keep it from sounding like a certain videogame franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok, that makes sense. I got to this forum straight from Google. I didn't knew they ever stopped calling it the post GMC NWoD. I still have my original NWoD rule book. I picked up the God Machine Chronicle and Blood and Smoke a few years ago when they first were released. I only knew Blood and Smoke was called Requiem 2e because I went to redownload it from drive thru recently and saw the name had changed. I played a game of 2e way back, but that group disbanded when people moved, so, I had to cultivate new people to play with. Just got back to the WoD recently after like 2 or 3 years away and I really missed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T23:33:01-07:00","id":848641,"title":"","content":"Ok, so this discussion about narrativism vs. simulationism (vs. gameism) is one of those topics that tends to get heated fast. I'm not going to make this a red text directive yet, but just... Let's be careful with this subject and try not to put down other people's playstyle preferences. The Storyteller has made it clear that they don't care for what they're calling story game mechanics. It's also been made clear that CofD contains a lot of these mechanics, and it's going to require some heavy lifting to remove them. No need to harp on either point further, let's just focus on advising The Storyteller in how best to remove the aspects they don't like.<br /> <br /> My advice: it sounds to me like you would be better off bringing the things you like in 2e over to 1e than the other way around. The list of things you preferred in 2e seemed shorter than the list of things you wanted to ignore or patch. Like, the changes to combat seemed like they were the biggest draw for you in 2e. It's easy as pie to adapt the 2e combat rules into the 1e system if that's all you want. Back-converting Disciplines might be a bit more involved, but not significantly so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-17-2016, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T23:54:36-07:00","id":848651,"title":"","content":"Here's the deal. Touchstones gives the character something to be invested upon, your players don't seem to wish to be invested in anything meaningful. Not even aspirations, which is a fancy way of calling a character's motivations. I have no clue whatsoever about how you can immerse yourself into something that isn't plain hack-and-slash without concise motivations to follow. Do you even award beats like the corebook suggests, or that's also out of your table?<br /> <br /> Making a jester and taking every opportunity to crack a joke despite your environment strikes me as downright pathological. That disregards the times when your Willpower is full. Have you read the diceless mechanic for feeding? if not? drop everything and do it. It works all those elements in, beautifully. If your players really do disregard their environment to pathologically follow 2 or 3 directives dictated by their anchors, they're doing it wrong.<br /> <br /> I've been playing a Monstrous PC. Said PC, a werewolf, gains Willpower back from terrorizing his prey. I've only enforced this once: by applying the coup de grace on a fallen and slowly regenerating Pure, in plain view of his and my pack, in a silent statement of &quot;Get out, or you'll be the next one&quot;. That's the only time I've ever gotten WP back. He doesn't goes around inflicting Lunacy willynilly at the first expense of WP. That's what drama is for. That's what brings out immersion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 03-17-2016, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T01:54:24-07:00","id":848684,"title":"","content":"I just like to also back a bit to the Aspirations. Why are you guys ignoring these? Like, do the player characters have no objectives at all? What are they doing in their games? Even if it's completely simulation of a &quot;normal vampire day&quot;, they still have something to do? In their duties, or in their nightlife? Aspirations are basically objectives set out by the players. So, what's the problem with announcing your objective before session?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T03:49:35-07:00","id":848707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because they are immersed, they just, you know, do it. Interacting with this extra mechanic giving them incentive to role play in a specific manner interferes with this immersion because they will be, in all circumstances, drawn to roleplay in a specific way that isn't always appropriate for the character. </div> </div> </div>If it isn't appropriate for the character then it shouldn't have been chosen by the player, but it doesn't need to be Always appropriate. Your not constantly trying to regain willpower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, instead of just naturally playing my character as a smartass, which includes NOT being a smartass at certain times, I am just going to always be looking to make a joke no matter what, for the willpower. At a funeral? Who gives a shit, I could get willpower. </div> </div> </div>Why would you think that? Just because something gives you willpower doesn't mean you'll do it in every scene, it just means you get incentives to do the thing related to it often. Often =! Constantly. The fact it doesn't always fit is a good thing.<br /> <br /> Often I find that people in certain situations alter their behaviour and don't act as they normally do, and when they do this altering it is generally at least minorly stressful and makes it harder for them to deal with their problems because they aren't themselves at the time... Not getting willpower, since you aren't fulfilling your anchors seems like a good representation of that to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Ah-ha! Yes,&quot; I respond, &quot;so, if they already know when that is and would do it anyway, why add a reward system? Why not just let them be and trust them to do it?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Because that way the game changes how you think and act. This isn't a &quot;why not trust them to do it thing&quot; in my opinion, since even without it, there is the assumption that your going to play your character properly. These mechanics make it so that when do self-affirming actions you have an actual representation of the effect doing that sort of thing has. When my character commits his vice, he regains willpower, not because &quot;Lol metagame&quot;, but because he just did something that gives him respite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-17-2016, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:10:44-07:00","id":848763,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2698\" data-vbnamecard=\"2698\">The Storyteller</a> First, let me real quick apologize if my comment of sim vs. nar felt like a blow-off. You definitely belong here. Even more than a Narrative game, CofD is a sandbox game, so take what you like, ditch the rest, etc. As Charlaquin mentioned, these discussions are hard to have without the tone of &quot;...but you're doing it wrong,&quot; bleeding in. But, fact is, you're the best judge of your table, and the all anyone can do here is try to armchair some advice for you.<br /> <br /> As for immersion, this is heavy YMMV territory. I actually don't see much conflict between that and story-game elements. Rolling dice, marking stats, and looking up rules already breaks people 'out of character' in that sense (best immersive game is straight up diceless LARP, imo). While it does take a little adjusting to add these elements and think about as a player, I've not found it significantly more difficult for people to do so. It's certainly much easier for an experienced player to consider Anchors/Beats and stay in character than I would say it is for a new player to try and process all the base rules while doing the same. <br /> <br /> A the end of the day, I suspect we're splitting hairs and aren't too far off baseline from how we make our decisions. Random scenario: The PCs need the permission of the Nos Priscus to set up a hideout in the Undercity, cause they're worried about heat from the Sheriff. I suspect you'd look at all the current goals of the Priscus, their willingness to work with the PCs, their relationship with the Sheriff, how they feel about possible non-Haunts in the Undercity - and then figure out what Boon/Favor the Priscus would be most likely to ask for at that time. I do all those same steps, only at the final decision point, rather than &quot;What are they most likely to ask for?&quot; I think about, &quot;Out of the options they could reasonably / realistically ask for, which request gives me the most interesting drama, conflict or experience?&quot;<br /> <br /> The analogy I use is pool. Narrative elements don't mean just hitting any random ball into the pocket (drama for drama's sake alone). It means you have to hit one of your stripes first (Choices still have to make sense), but you're thinking where you want to position the cue-ball after that initial hit to make your next shot even better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:23:15-07:00","id":848771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848641#post848641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also been made clear that CofD contains a lot of these mechanics, and it's going to require some heavy lifting to remove them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think it's that hard at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848641#post848641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice: it sounds to me like you would be better off bringing the things you like in 2e over to 1e than the other way around. The list of things you preferred in 2e seemed shorter than the list of things you wanted to ignore or patch. Like, the changes to combat seemed like they were the biggest draw for you in 2e. It's easy as pie to adapt the 2e combat rules into the 1e system if that's all you want. Back-converting Disciplines might be a bit more involved, but not significantly so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand. Given that we also mostly ignored Virtue/Vice and City/Clan/Covenant Status then, what is the difference between playing 1e with, effectively, nearly all of the mechanical changes (merits, combat, disciplines, XP cost changes so it doesn't scale, exanded conditions/tilts) from 2e, and playing 2e without like, four or five things that we don't like (Aspirations, Touchstones, Mask/Dirge, the way beats are handed out, and the doors system)? Oh, and I guess I like the old Crone better, too?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure the distinction is important. I think cutting a small handful of things from 2e is way less significant than adding massive amounts of rule changes to 1e. 1e is basically just those rules being replaced anyway. There's nothing else left of the game after those things are altered. Nothing was replaced for 2e, except Virtue and Vice being universal and the gothic horror &quot;moral decline = mental decline&quot; thing, which got silly and ignored anyway.<br /> <br /> It seems like people here are ascribing WAY more importance to these super minor side systems that are readily, easily ignored, than I ever did.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk about a major change we do, get ready to flip your lid, because we use cards for initiative! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848651#post848651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the deal. Touchstones gives the character something to be invested upon, your players don't seem to wish to be invested in anything meaningful. Not even aspirations, which is a fancy way of calling a character's motivations. I have no clue whatsoever about how you can immerse yourself into something that isn't plain hack-and-slash without concise motivations to follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me ask you: in real life, when you wake up in the morning, do you write down the things you intend to do during that day? I know I don't. And yet, I still have motivations. I still have goals. I don't make a list of my friends, but I still have relationships.<br /> <br /> It's not the characters having no motivation, it's the players not mechanizing their motivation into a game rules element. Their character's have goals. We just don't write them down ahead of time, and then reward people for mindlessly sticking to whatever they wrote down. We just let people's motivations be, and they can shift as they naturally would without penalty.<br /> <br /> Maybe you object to the mindset of, &quot;If I get a reward for doing X, I am effectively being punished for doing Y by not receiving a reward.&quot; I could understand that, even though my group and I would endorse that statement fully. We'd rather not have behavior based rewards, so that we can behave as we like without feeling penalized for not chasing the reward.<br /> <br /> The game is far from hack and slash. I don't really like that style. We've had three short combats. The first, the PCs walked by a fight between vampires and changelings. Their intervention prevented one of the five changelings from escaping before the Sheriff arrived and speed cuffed her with Cold Iron manacles. The second had the PCs chasing down Changelings and pretending to fight them in order to allow their escape while still looking like they tried to stop them in their superior's eyes. Things kind of went south when the changelings didn't really understand they were helping and faking it, and one of them dramatic failed with a shotgun, blowing his own leg off and leading to his capture. So, partial success, 2 of the 3 escaped. The last fight was a scuffle between two of the PCs, the dog, and five gang members that were starting to sell drugs on their turf, including two vampires and a changeling. The PC side was, shockingly, winning. Three of the other team were beaten down (so was one PC, but he was willing to spend Willpower to win), but the Changeling managed to frighten them with a contract to end the engagement (they ran to the gang's car, though, and stole it, along with lots of drugs, so, still pretty much a win).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848651#post848651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you even award beats like the corebook suggests, or that's also out of your table?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely not. We threw the corebook beats out the window session one, because uneven advancement does not fly for us and we could tell chasing beats would lead to ridiculous, anti-immersive activity. We started with group beats, but, it took way too much activity to generate even a single extra beat for the party (seriously, 5 beat worthy things had to happen) and we had already started kind of ignoring aspirations, so, I started just giving beats out like I would XP during Savage Worlds. It's roughly analagous, since you get an advancement in that game every 5 XP, and you get a &quot;real XP&quot; every 5 beats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848651#post848651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making a jester and taking every opportunity to crack a joke despite your environment strikes me as downright pathological. That disregards the times when your Willpower is full.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can get willpower back for cracking a joke, why would you not spend it on every roll?<br /> <br /> This is where we're having communication trouble. You say, &quot;Why would you do that? You just get the reward when you do X and you don't do X unless it's appropriate.&quot; And I say, &quot;Why not just trust people to do X when appropriate instead of muddying the waters and offering a reward that might tempt them to do X when it's NOT appropriate?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848651#post848651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read the diceless mechanic for feeding? if not? drop everything and do it. It works all those elements in, beautifully.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yuck, yeah, I no, I read them and, no. Just no. Actually doing that at a table? It's very off putting for immersion focused players. They don't want to play as someone else and they don't want to actively construct a story. That's literally the opposite of the immersion they are looking for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848651#post848651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your players really do disregard their environment to pathologically follow 2 or 3 directives dictated by their anchors, they're doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree. But they'd still be rewarded for doing it wrong. That's a problem. Why not just remove that reward, so they're not tempted to do it wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848651#post848651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been playing a Monstrous PC. Said PC, a werewolf, gains Willpower back from terrorizing his prey. I've only enforced this once: by applying the coup de grace on a fallen and slowly regenerating Pure, in plain view of his and my pack, in a silent statement of &quot;Get out, or you'll be the next one&quot;. That's the only time I've ever gotten WP back. He doesn't goes around inflicting Lunacy willynilly at the first expense of WP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you have done anything differently if you didn't have the word Monster written next to your Mask/Dirge/whatever it is in Werewolf? Would you have done anything differently if you did not receive a willpower or doing what you did that one time?<br /> <br /> If you wouldn't have done anything differently, why include that mechanic at all? It hasn't changed anything for you. You'd have done the same thing without it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848651#post848651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what drama is for. That's what brings out immersion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we're talking about the same meaning of Immersion, because what you're calling immersion is as close to the opposite of what I am calling it as you can get. I think you're talking about something like &quot;Story immersion.&quot; You are investing in what happens and getting excited by the rise and fall of drama and action. You are on the edge of your seat waiting for the next cool thing. Like, as if you were watching a great movie or something that you got &quot;immersed&quot; in.<br /> <br /> But my group, we immerse in the characters. We become them while playing. The characters can't control drama around them, they can only control themselves. When you, as a player, alter the story around their characters, you are taking an action outside of what your character is capable of doing, and affecting the game world in a way that would require the character to shatter the 4th wall to accomplish themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848684#post848684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just like to also back a bit to the Aspirations. Why are you guys ignoring these? Like, do the player characters have no objectives at all? What are they doing in their games? Even if it's completely simulation of a &quot;normal vampire day&quot;, they still have something to do? In their duties, or in their nightlife? Aspirations are basically objectives set out by the players. So, what's the problem with announcing your objective before session?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is 1) Remembering to announce them 2) figuring out what you want to do in rewardable objective statements 3) chasing rewards, rather than acting naturally if, say, your motivations change due to the organic flow of circumstance during the game.<br /> <br /> Ok, let's take two examples, one with aspirations, and one without.<br /> <br /> With: The session starts and you know your character wants to find a Haven. So, your aspiration is &quot;Acquire a Haven.&quot; You start working on that goal, then, half way through the session, an old friend calls you up. He needs help with something! Hmm, now you have to weigh helping your friend (for no reward other than helping a friend) or getting your Haven, which you still want to do, and getting a beat. In fact, if you can get the Haven and the beat quickly, you might be able to add a &quot;help your friend&quot; aspiration and get another beat out of it. Hmmm, tough decision. Your friend needs help, but, damn, a beat is awesome. It can feel to some, in fact, that you are being punished by helping your friend, rather than following through on the thing you wrote down at the beginning of the session. However you choose, though, you're thrown from immersion because you are now weighing a meta resource your character has no way to know about (a beat) against actual in character relationships.<br /> <br /> Without: The session starts and you know your character wants to find a Haven. You start working on that, then, halway through the session, an old friend calls you up. He needs help with something! So, you decide how much you care about this friend, and decide, yeah, you want to help. Done. Full character immersion maintained.<br /> <br /> Not using Aspirations doesn't mean characters don't have goals and motivations, it means we don't mechanize those things and reward/punish doing/not doing them with meta-rewards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848707#post848707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it isn't appropriate for the character then it shouldn't have been chosen by the player, but it doesn't need to be Always appropriate. Your not constantly trying to regain willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? If you know you can get it back super easily by flipping a switch, why would not always spend it and then always flip that switch? That's just foolish resource management.<br /> <br /> If someone told you that you could get $50 every time you tell someone a knock knock joke, why would you NOT tell knock knock jokes to literally everyone in all circumstances? Why would you ever be stingy with money knowing you could just tell a knock knock joke to get more?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848707#post848707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you think that? Just because something gives you willpower doesn't mean you'll do it in every scene, it just means you get incentives to do the thing related to it often. Often =! Constantly. The fact it doesn't always fit is a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. Because you still receive the reward when it doesn't fit. You are mechanically incentivized to take the action in ALL circumstances. There is no stipulation that requires your action be appropriate to how your character would actually act. If you're going to add such a thing, how is that different from just removing the reward? Both change the rules, but mine requires no judgment calls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848707#post848707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Often I find that people in certain situations alter their behaviour and don't act as they normally do, and when they do this altering it is generally at least minorly stressful and makes it harder for them to deal with their problems because they aren't themselves at the time... Not getting willpower, since you aren't fulfilling your anchors seems like a good representation of that to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I find that people are way more complicated than that. Summing someone up as a single word archetype does not do them justice, and so even if someone is a Jester, they do not crack jokes constantly, nor do they necessarily feel uncomfortable when they can't. Real human beings change fluidly from day to day, moment to moment, and while they tend to follow behavior patterns, those are not absolute. Most people, even comedians, don't make jokes at funerals--they don't even feel tempted to do it. It's not going to cause them discomfort and pain beyond what the funeral is already causing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848707#post848707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that way the game changes how you think and act. This isn't a &quot;why not trust them to do it thing&quot; in my opinion, since even without it, there is the assumption that your going to play your character properly. These mechanics make it so that when do self-affirming actions you have an actual representation of the effect doing that sort of thing has. When my character commits his vice, he regains willpower, not because &quot;Lol metagame&quot;, but because he just did something that gives him respite.</div> </div> </div> </div>This argument is much more nuanced, and I appreciate it. But I would just say that, when immersed in your character, you feel self affirmed when taking a self-affirming action. There is no meta-reward needed to feel affirmed. You just feel it because that is how your character would feel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848763#post848763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, let me real quick apologize if my comment of sim vs. nar felt like a blow-off. You definitely belong here. Even more than a Narrative game, CofD is a sandbox game, so take what you like, ditch the rest, etc. As Charlaquin mentioned, these discussions are hard to have without the tone of &quot;...but you're doing it wrong,&quot; bleeding in. But, fact is, you're the best judge of your table, and the all anyone can do here is try to armchair some advice for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, it was not you that suggested I should not be playing this game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I'm really not offended or upset with anyone else, either. I understand that other perspectives can be hard to understand. No big deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848763#post848763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A the end of the day, I suspect we're splitting hairs and aren't too far off baseline from how we make our decisions. Random scenario: The PCs need the permission of the Nos Priscus to set up a hideout in the Undercity, cause they're worried about heat from the Sheriff. I suspect you'd look at all the current goals of the Priscus, their willingness to work with the PCs, their relationship with the Sheriff, how they feel about possible non-Haunts in the Undercity - and then figure out what Boon/Favor the Priscus would be most likely to ask for at that time. I do all those same steps, only at the final decision point, rather than &quot;What are they most likely to ask for?&quot; I think about, &quot;Out of the options they could reasonably / realistically ask for, which request gives me the most interesting drama, conflict or experience?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly that. My gaming agenda calls for them to make the most likely and logical decision, not necessarily the most interesting/dramatic one. I absolutely understand lots of people prefer the latter. I do not. It's really simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848763#post848763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The analogy I use is pool. Narrative elements don't mean just hitting any random ball into the pocket (drama for drama's sake alone). It means you have to hit one of your stripes first (Choices still have to make sense), but you're thinking where you want to position the cue-ball after that initial hit to make your next shot even better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you're saying, but I don't think that analogy totally works, because it implies the other side isn't trying to make good decisions or plans. I feel like the agenda I ascribe to would take careful shots in order to run the table and win, whereas the more narrative (for lack of a better term) player might purposefully miss a shot, because a one-sided roflstomping isn't as exciting as one in which both sides have a chance. The defining feature of storygaming for me is purposefully making bad things happen to your character because it's more interesting or dramatic. The ability to get a beat for taking a dramatic failure is a prime example of that in 2e. But doing that makes you inherently not immersed in your character, because no person wants bad things to happen to them because it's more exciting--that's lunacy. You're directly influencing something your character could not influence in order to bring about an event your character would not want to happen. That is just not what we want on any level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  typo 03-17-2016, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:52:40-07:00","id":848789,"title":"","content":"Regarding Aspirations: To me, they're a carrot. As in, &quot;Hey Bob, you having written down your character's Aspirations really helped me plan the next few sessions, so here's a beet&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:59:25-07:00","id":848794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848429#post848429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I know they're allowed by the rules, but that doesn't mean I have to like them. They were very obviously trying to take the easiest possible touchstones, so that they could effectively ignore the subsystem. Nobody was playing in good faith, genuinely feeling like these things connected them to humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, fair enough. If no one is playing in good faith, then I completely agree with you. That's something that is an issue. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, the dog isn't making him ask hard questions, nor is he scared of the dog being hurt or killed. It's not vulnerable at all. Dogs are ridiculously badass in WoD. Have you looked at their stats? Big attack pool, high defense...add blood and disciplines in there, his dog is the best fighter in the party by far. What he has is an amazing weapon that can also track, relatively &quot;story protected&quot; due to its status as a retainer and a touchstone. He can even talk to it with Animalism, and command it to break its nature via the same. </div> </div> </div> Okay, that's odd if the dog is the best fighter. While dogs do have good stats, they can't use weapons or armor in 2e, which is huge. Auto-damage is imporant, and dogs don't have any. Even if the dog is ghouled, that's at best a one or two bonus damage, nothing compared to what a vampire with vitae boosts and Vigor should be able to do with a good weapon. A starting Daeva with a fire axe can deal upwards of 7L on a single success attack roll. <br /> <br /> Though, I would like to point out that being a dog should have absolutely no impact on their stats. The Retainer rules apply to animals and their dice pools as much as they do to human Retainers. So, if a PC put two dots of Retainer into the character, we should be talking about a dice pool of 4 for attacking, with one discipline dot. Meanwhile, a 5 dot ghoul Retainer would have a dice pool of 10 for combat related activities plus 3 disciplines. And that holds true if they owned a large dog or employed a regular person. You don't get a large attack dog with a one dot Retainer.<br /> <br /> That said, if he's putting something that's important on the front lines, that's asking for it to be hit with Animalism or some rather heavy weapons. Nothing is that protected from the whims of combat dice! I personally would have absolutely no qualms about having the dog suffer fatal attacks. Hells. I would have no qualms about someone using Animalism to force the dog to fight the party! With how you run the game, that's 40% of all vampires that can turn the dog against the PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, forgive me for this, but it seems like you're saying, &quot;You shouldn't dislike touchstones because the rules say this. Oh, they don't? Well, they should. So, like it.&quot; I mean, I get where you're coming from and I'm glad you like touchstones, honestly, but I don't think I do. Sorry. </div> </div> </div> Well, I was more objecting to calling them a cheat just because it was a dog. Just because its a dog doesn't make it a cheat. Manipulating an ST into being afraid of attacking a combat character becuase of special status is a cheat. So I agree with you, but not for the reasons you originally stated. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yikes, why would ever do that? Why would you want to make yourself obsessed? I see nothing to gain there. That's....bizarre. I can't imagine a game where Daeva do that on purpose beyond, say, their first victim, or maybe it's a desperate situation/accident. I don't know, wow. </div> </div> </div> Because for myself and a lot of others? Its fun. Its absolutely a blast delving into all the strange and crazy things that vampires do. Being obsessed with your herd is something classic for Anne-Rice style vampires, and that's the kind of vampire the Daeva represent. <br /> <br /> From a certain point of view, its not even a curse. Its like an addiction. Which is the other side to this coin - the Kiss of the Succubus merit. You literally make anyone you feed on addicted to your bite. They will keep coming back to you, and you'll both fall in love from the unhealthy and tragic tale of vampire lovers who go too far. Vampire is a game all about crazy stories like that. Especially with how the beat / Condition system works. You don't avoid drama. You dive head first into it, you take curses and flaws and the like head on, you suffer through them, and you earn beats / xp. Embracing it makes you stronger!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am really intrigued, actually, based on this and your previous comments, how we came to entirely different conclusions about how Daeva act. You say they're more attached to their Herds, while I interpreted them as being unable to have Herds. That's the sign of a good flaw, I think--we're both right despite holding opposite viewpoints. </div> </div> </div> Well, not so much opposite as both ways are viable. The reason I believe so is because that's what some of the Vampire writers have flat out said just that. You either make an effort to be promiscuous and avoid herds, or you develop a herd you are very attached to. There's room for more than one style of play. It might not be how you like to play, but its entirely viable way of playing. <br /> <br /> I have the impression that you feel that Humanity loss and curses and banes need to be avoided at all costs. That's not how I play the game. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I found the thread and read it. I think I'm going to stick with it, though. I prefer it to what seems like the intended way Mask/Dirge/Touchstones work. </div> </div> </div> Well, I do it that way too. I was just giving full disclosure, or at least as much as I could. There are people who feel that, because it didn't actually make it into the book, it shouldn't count. And there are people who feel that it should be an official rule asap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:01:23-07:00","id":848797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848789#post848789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Aspirations: To me, they're a carrot. As in, &quot;Hey Bob, you having written down your character's Aspirations really helped me plan the next few sessions, so here's a beet&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a cool way to handle them, but even that wouldn't apply to me, really, because I don't actually prepare anything for sessions before hand, I just react to what the players are doing. I don't actually ever need to know their goals, I just need to know the actions they're taking. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:16:52-07:00","id":848807,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848564#post848564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to be clear about my objection to these systems. It's not because I want them hard, it's because I want to encourage actual immersion in the characters. I actually think these sorts of things <i>break immersion. </i>All of those storytelling reward mechanics, like FATE points or getting willpower back, they create reward cycles that encourage people to take specific actions. In storytelling games, those specific actions tend to be those that either highlight aspects of your characters or those that create more drama. When that's what you want, it's perfect. When you want something more, something like real immersion in a character so that they act, you know, like a real person and not like a character in a drama, those reward cycles are an obstacle. It will create an internal conflict for players between immersing and getting rewarded. I'd rather just trust they'll do it right without a carrot and stick to force them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, point taken. One way I want to react is by echoing Milo V3 in saying that rewarding players for 'thinking as their character would' is awesome simulation. I don't think it is dramatic but correct modelling of vampire psychology. So I very much resist the notion that the player feeling compelled to crack a joke at a funeral is bad design, if the person is a jester. It actually matches player incentive (more resource) with character expression (that is just the type of person they are) so that behaviour emerges organically and isn't forgotten.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, to be fair, that is just my bugbear. If I carry on arguing why you are wrong for not following my one twue way, then I might get a willpower point back but I won't be too helpful or friendly. So my inner player is going to bypass the free willpower and engage with what is at stake: Immersion.<br /> <br /> Immersion is person specific and if what works for your players is to remove or amend the soft systems, then so be it. My advice has to presume traits about the group based one what you have supplied, so when I am really off, just ignore me. Oh and discuss all these changes first with the players.<br /> <br /> First, I would go all out and embrace player freedom by identifying player thought with character thought. That is to say, if dramatic systems are breaking immersion by creating distance between play-as-immersive-experience and play-as-optimal-solution, then outright scrap them where they interfere but retain them lorewise. For example, get rid of humanity as a stat. The beast is still doing beasty things and vampire society keeps it at bay but it sees no mechanical expression. Vampires with low humanity are simply those that don't resist the beast as often. (You do lose the corpse effect but minor loss). People sense the predator the same way we recognise a creep at a bar; body language and not-at-all-hidden intent. Getting rid of the mechanic means touchstones can go. Not needed. The numerous subsystems that use humanity can be hacked when you encounter them; fire and sun deal a set level of damage per turn, for example, and torpor requires resisting the urge to wake and feed, with being harder to resist with thin blood.<br /> <br /> Second, give your players a flat refresh whenever they get a day off. The day off is always off-screen and can be given a quick description. However, it competes with doing downtime stuff, and maybe feeding, as well as being inaccessible during long campaigns 'in the field' or if kidnapped. That way there are no competing concerns during play but willpower is still a resource you must tend to or lose the privilege of having. (sidenote: score points with your Marxist buddies by making job downtown willpower neutral or draining, thus highlighting the capitalist nature of leisure time. The poor characters will be way less productive than their rich peer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) The only problem I have with this is that 2E was wrote with the assumption WP is spent and regained quickly, and so you MIGHT run into trouble. Best practice is to test and calibrate.<br /> <br /> Third, change the curses to be major affects that require manoeuvring around. Plus, with Humanity not being a thing, they may need adjustment anyway. Just remember, this will affect all the clan in aggregate and thus may produce a certain stereotype. Suggestions:<br /> <br /> Deava can remain the same. They gain the stereotype of indulgence because they are either with everyone or all about one.<br /> <br /> Gangrel can't be stopped and doesn't want to stop. Whenever they must stop, because of rules or authority, they gains the Tempted condition. It doesn't make them frenzy but a long night of pussyfooting around Elysium takes its toll. They all gain the stereotype of being feral because they seem to have no time for social mores and rules.<br /> <br /> Mekhet can remain the same. They no longer burn faster but their clan as a whole is still weird.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu somewhat remain the same. Their creep factor is now level with blood potency. When they can feed on animals, they suffer a -1 penalty to social rolls, when they can only feed on people, that is -3, and when it is just vampires, they scare the batshit out of everyone [everyone gets frightened condition]. Whether this affects other splats is up to you and I recommend letting all people spend WP to suppress the effects for a scene, allowing those close to the Nos to treat them well but at a cost, so nobody wants to interact with them but can out of devotion or friendship. The stereotype? They're unnerving/terrifying.<br /> <br /> Venture don't have a weakness: the Deucalions are right. However, they do enjoy winning and their desire for control is so strong it would be seen as weakness by lesser individuals. All Venture have the Obsession (Authority) condition. There is some ambiguity around the concept of authority but 'personal' authority is not authority: the Venture want their excellence recognised. Furthermore, actions that risk 'victory' require a will power expenditure (one per scene). Lastly, since order begets control, disorder irritates Ven more than others. A lack of clear hierarchy* result in the Distracted condition and pressure to engage in an extended action before order is affirm provokes frenzy. (hierarchies have a least two levels and somebody must be present in both. The easiest hierarchy is 'I'm the boss; do as I say!')<br /> <br /> I think these options open up immersion. Ventures are better when focused and structured, Gangrels in places where regulation is light, Nos where they are not in the spotlight unless among friends, Davea when they can control their feeding, and Mekhets when they avoid their bane. The advantages and disadvantages are well within player agency to affect.<br /> <br /> What else needs amending?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  Spacing 03-17-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:17:27-07:00","id":848808,"title":"","content":"What happened to my font? :/<br /> <br /> Fixed it. Ignore this. :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:22:58-07:00","id":848815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848797#post848797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a cool way to handle them, but even that wouldn't apply to me, really, because I don't actually prepare anything for sessions before hand, I just react to what the players are doing. I don't actually ever need to know their goals, I just need to know the actions they're taking.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool, I've always wanted to be able to do that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> On a different note, would you mind compiling your house-rules? It would make a useful resource for the next person coming to these forums with the same questions as you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:30:57-07:00","id":848816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848797#post848797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a cool way to handle them, but even that wouldn't apply to me, really, because I don't actually prepare anything for sessions before hand, I just react to what the players are doing. I don't actually ever need to know their goals, I just need to know the actions they're taking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is actually why I mentioned Aspirations earlier. They are not mechanized player goals, they are mechanized Storyteller planning tools. That's why it says they can be out of character and negative things, i.e. 'I want my character to become Blood Bonded to my sires rival'. They are there to give the Storyteller interesting points for drama. Which ,as you've said, is totally not something you want.<br /> <br /> I have more questions and comments, but they are still not about touchstones. I'll leave it to you if you want to try and get this thread back focused on those more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T09:36:18-07:00","id":848839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848794#post848794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that's odd if the dog is the best fighter. While dogs do have good stats, they can't use weapons or armor in 2e, which is huge. Auto-damage is imporant, and dogs don't have any. Even if the dog is ghouled, that's at best a one or two bonus damage, nothing compared to what a vampire with vitae boosts and Vigor should be able to do with a good weapon. A starting Daeva with a fire axe can deal upwards of 7L on a single success attack roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my game, it'd be 5L, but I get the point.<br /> <br /> So, a few responses. First, carrying around obvious weapons like fire axes and wearing armor is just not socially acceptable. You'd garner lots of attention from people and authorities, nevermind the disapproval vampires would feel towards you. Guns are much eaiser to hide and carry compared to their deadliness, but the game is set in Canada, so guns are way harder to get a hold of and people are much less likely to be able to use them anyway.<br /> <br /> I know you can gear up effectively with Obfuscate, but then, you basically can't break Obfuscate until a fight starts, which severely limits your options. Fights are dangerous and not usually stuff you should be going out looking for, especially given how easy they are to escape now that you can't realistically one-shot people anymore.<br /> <br /> Second, if you're willing to walk around in armor, why can't you armor your dog? I feel like it would even be less noticeable, since dog armor is much less obviously armor than people armor and you'll just look like one of those weirdos that puts clothes on your dog. Oh, and the dog has Resilience, so, it has a version of psuedo armor when needed anyway.<br /> <br /> Third, God Machine didn't have animal stats, so, I used the same ones from my original WoD core. Dogs have a +2L bite, so, translated to 2e, that would become a 1L bite. They also ended up with 7 dice to attack (ok, not the best), but 8 defense, which is ridiculous, and beyond most peoples combat pools.<br /> <br /> After seeing it in action once, we agreed the dog would be dropped to 3 Athletics and would no longer benefit from the 1e rule that an animal got to use the higher of its Wits/Dex instead of the lower, bringing its defense more in line at 6.<br /> <br /> The best combatant in the party was a Nos with 10 dice to grapple (9 to punch), but only 4 defense. Post dog nerf, a player was unhappy with their character and requested a remake. Instead of Mekhet, she picked Daeva, and made her capable in a fight, so, now she'll have, I believe 8 dice to attack with a knife, and 7 defense, which is probably still not as good as the original dog with a 1L bite (since knives are 0L).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848794#post848794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, I would like to point out that being a dog should have absolutely no impact on their stats. The Retainer rules apply to animals and their dice pools as much as they do to human Retainers. So, if a PC put two dots of Retainer into the character, we should be talking about a dice pool of 4 for attacking, with one discipline dot. Meanwhile, a 5 dot ghoul Retainer would have a dice pool of 10 for combat related activities plus 3 disciplines. And that holds true if they owned a large dog or employed a regular person. You don't get a large attack dog with a one dot Retainer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another point with multiple responses. I sense a theme.<br /> <br /> I remember reading the God Machine retainer rules and thinking, &quot;wow, that's a brilliant short cut for retainers you mostly don't care about fleshing out that do mundane stuff.&quot; But, beyond that, it's not really a great tool. Several factors went into our decision on this front:<br /> 1) As people who like immersion, it would be wonky if his pet Husky had stats tremendously different from any other random Husky they encountered on the streets<br /> 2) By those rules, his 3 point husky retainer would have 6 dice to dog stuff, but then still have 3 dice to everything else. It could pilot a plane, pick a lock, hack a computer, repair a car, all with 3 dice. That's obviously not right, but if we denied the dog the ability to do so, it would make the dog an objectively weaker choice than a human retainer with no cost break or other upside to compensate.<br /> 3) We knew this thing would eventually be in combats, and possibly in the line of fire of magical powers, and there does not appear to be anything in the retainer rules to detemine secondary or resistance stats. What's the defense of a 3 dot retainer? How much health does it have? What is its composure if it gets hit with Nightmare? Too many questions.<br /> 4) It's a touchstone. It felt like it deserved more than just a die pool.<br /> <br /> We generated a cost by looking at its best pools (attack 7 die, tracking 8 dice), which led to a 4 dot cost, then we reduced it by 1 for the fact that, with fleshed out stats, it has a lot less utility for doing things outside of its wheelhouse, and it's a dog that can't do the vast majority of the things it could do as a human. I feel like it's fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848794#post848794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, if he's putting something that's important on the front lines, that's asking for it to be hit with Animalism or some rather heavy weapons. Nothing is that protected from the whims of combat dice! I personally would have absolutely no qualms about having the dog suffer fatal attacks. Hells. I would have no qualms about someone using Animalism to force the dog to fight the party! With how you run the game, that's 40% of all vampires that can turn the dog against the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and I had no qualms with people trying to attack it. But, literally, the first scene it was in a fight, he jumped and mauled a thug for like 4 or 5 damage, then when that thug's buddy attacked the dog with a chain, the 8 defense gave him a chance die he botched with and he wailed on his friend, too. It was pretty brutal. It didn't take any damage until the third attacker, the changeling, finally hit it with a beam of frost for 2 lethal cold damage. I told the player the dog didn't want to fight anymore, that it would just dodge without being pushed further with Animalism. He was ok with that.<br /> <br /> As for the 40% of vampires being able to Animalism, yes, that's true. But a large portion can do the same kinds of things to a human or vampire, too. And since he always has his Animalism in play, he'd at least get to Clash of Wills with anyone trying something.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm not upset about this dog at all. I think it's fine. I had no objections to him running around with a pet. I just objected to it being a touchstone. Which, well, is no longer relevant, since I'm well resolved to downplay touchstones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848794#post848794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the impression that you feel that Humanity loss and curses and banes need to be avoided at all costs. That's not how I play the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. You are correct, lower levels of Humanity penalize you. You wouldn't deliberaly choose a penalty, so, losing Humanity is not a positive thing. That said, it's also sort of inevitable, so the fun is in seeing how long you can hold out. Humanity is a struggle--if you're not struggling, if you're just giving in because it's cool or interesting, I feel like that's losing a lot of what it's there for and what it represents. At least to me, that is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848807#post848807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, get rid of humanity as a stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we want to do that. There is one player, yes, who initially didn't like Humanity because he wanted to, basically, be a super bad guy and revel in it, which would drop him to draugr really fast. But at this point, I think even he is on board. We like Humanity as it is. We might think of it differntly (as above, it's kind of an inevitable loss condition), but we like it.<br /> <br /> Your thoughts here are all very good, though, and might help someone else.<br /> <br /> Side note: whoever it was that talked about Werewolf Harmony being a stat you want to keep balanced at 5 or 6 made it sound really appealing. I like that a lot, actually, and almost wish Humanity worked in a similar way, such that losing humanity wasn't purely negative, it just made you more beast and less man, which carried benefits of its own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848815#post848815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's cool, I've always wanted to be able to do that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> On a different note, would you mind compiling your house-rules? It would make a useful resource for the next person coming to these forums with the same questions as you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, I guess I could try. That's kind of a daunting task, as I might not immediately recognize everythig I'm doing as a houserule. Mostly, it's just downplaying or ignoring the meta-story stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well, that and the card stuff.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I'll give it a shot later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848816#post848816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have more questions and comments, but they are still not about touchstones. I'll leave it to you if you want to try and get this thread back focused on those more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I'm ok with it. It looks like everyone else's houserules for Ventrue still interact with the touchstone rules, so, they won't help me, and my -1 to detachment is at least &quot;ok&quot; for now, so, feel free to fire away. Or we can use a different thread if you prefer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  clarity 03-17-2016, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:05:53-07:00","id":848850,"title":"","content":"Have you seen this? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/816385-official-chronicles-of-darkness-resources-animal-stats-condition-and-power-cards-faq-coming-soon\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...aq-coming-soon</a><br /> <br /> it presents new, not so frigging op stats for the dogs. As for a dog unable to do hacking being a worse option than a human retainer - that's not true. Dog is always loyal, while human has needs of his own <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:20:07-07:00","id":848856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848839#post848839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think we want to do that. There is one player, yes, who initially didn't like Humanity because he wanted to, basically, be a super bad guy and revel in it, which would drop him to draugr really fast. But at this point, I think even he is on board. We like Humanity as it is. We might think of it differntly (as above, it's kind of an inevitable loss condition), but we like it.<br /> <br /> Your thoughts here are all very good, though, and might help someone else.<br /> <br /> Side note: whoever it was that talked about Werewolf Harmony being a stat you want to keep balanced at 5 or 6 made it sound really appealing. I like that a lot, actually, and almost wish Humanity worked in a similar way, such that losing humanity wasn't purely negative, it just made you more beast and less man, which carried benefits of its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>The benefits are not having to hold onto your humanity. Low humanity vampires are less constrained; Inhuman vampires trade constrains but that tends to work out in their favor. Aside from that, I'm not sure how I'd model a Harmony-like Humanity. For one, there are no werewolf draugr, so creating a balanced humanity stat would mean amending that mechanic. Otherwise, the scales still weight heavy in favor of keeping humanity and as such, penalties for high humanity is double taxing IMHO. Second, not sure why you'd penalise high humanity. If you were to go down that line, disciplines and other powers of the blood might weaken for the highly humane but again, feels like double taxing because just using powers at that level of humanity would drive you towards center. So you use a power and not only is it lesser than it could be but the reason it is lesser is threatened. Suppose you could amp low humanity vampire powers.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:44:53-07:00","id":848869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848839#post848839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my game, it'd be 5L, but I get the point.<br /> <br /> Interesting. You are correct, lower levels of Humanity penalize you. You wouldn't deliberaly choose a penalty, so, losing Humanity is not a positive thing. That said, it's also sort of inevitable, so the fun is in seeing how long you can hold out. Humanity is a struggle--if you're not struggling, if you're just giving in because it's cool or interesting, I feel like that's losing a lot of what it's there for and what it represents. At least to me, that is.<br /> <br /> I don't think we want to do that. There is one player, yes, who initially didn't like Humanity because he wanted to, basically, be a super bad guy and revel in it, which would drop him to draugr really fast. But at this point, I think even he is on board. We like Humanity as it is. We might think of it differntly (as above, it's kind of an inevitable loss condition), but we like it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the character wouldn't delibretly choose a penalty but they don't know its a penalty. The character doesn't know what Humanity is, only the player does. So if the player chooses not to do something because it would lower their Humanity, then they are breaking the immersion you say you want. Which I think is why people suggested you remove Humanity, it is very much a story mechanic. If not remove it, make it secret, the players shouldnt know what their score is or what will affect it until it happens. If I was going for the deep in character immersion that you are that is what I would do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848839#post848839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Side note: whoever it was that talked about Werewolf Harmony being a stat you want to keep balanced at 5 or 6 made it sound really appealing. I like that a lot, actually, and almost wish Humanity worked in a similar way, such that losing humanity wasn't purely negative, it just made you more beast and less man, which carried benefits of its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was me actually, and I find it interesting that you like it. Since I brought it up to point out that it was a story enforcing mechanic too (the same way as Humanity).<br /> <br /> And while you could hack it to work with Vampire, the reason it is different is becuase they are both intended to inform the kind of stories that are told in the system. Werewolf is about balancing the Spirit and the Flesh, while vampire is about the eventual degradation of immortality.<br /> <br /> My next question is about conditions, you said you like them. But you dont use beats, and you dont like meta roleplay incentives so are conditions just a list of status effects with names and rules for you? Cause thats like the least important or impressive thing about the condition system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:22:03-07:00","id":848893,"title":"","content":"A common transition re: Humanity in Sim games is to actually make it a known quantity by the characters. The physical changes, the limits to frenzy, the social modifiers - all of these things can be perceived in the game world, and thus perceived by the characters and commented on or manipulated by the characters. The man-beast struggle, Golconda / Draugr - these are game-world events intrinsically linked to humanity. Sure, the characters shouldn't be referring to &quot;my Humanity stat&quot; any more than they should be referring to their talent for &quot;Streetwise&quot; - but how good someone is at perusing black market goods or making networks with streetkids, or identifying gang signs - one character can probably say if they are better at doing those than a different character. One character could easily understand they were &quot;more human&quot; and &quot;less monstrous&quot; before they committed a sin.<br /> <br /> Humanity as a mechanic is way easier to translate to an IC phenomenon, than say, Beats or Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:27:12-07:00","id":848897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848893#post848893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A common transition re: Humanity in Sim games is to actually make it a known quantity by the characters. The physical changes, the limits to frenzy, the social modifiers - all of these things can be perceived in the game world, and thus perceived by the characters and commented on or manipulated by the characters. The man-beast struggle, Golconda / Draugr - these are game-world events intrinsically linked to humanity. Sure, the characters shouldn't be referring to &quot;my Humanity stat&quot; any more than they should be referring to their talent for &quot;Streetwise&quot; - but how good someone is at perusing black market goods or making networks with streetkids, or identifying gang signs - one character can probably say if they are better at doing those than a different character. One character could easily understand they were &quot;more human&quot; and &quot;less monstrous&quot; before they committed a sin.<br /> <br /> Humanity as a mechanic is way easier to translate to an IC phenomenon, than say, Beats or Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure, I would keep that concept, just not the list of sins, the dot value itself maybe, maybe not. I just think it is a clear story mechanic for the players to be able to avoid behaviours becuase they would be negative (all of that from The Storytellers defeinitons and position, I personally love the story mechanics).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:32:56-07:00","id":848902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848897#post848897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh sure, I would keep that concept, just not the list of sins, the dot value itself maybe, maybe not. I just think it is a clear story mechanic for the players to be able to avoid behaviours becuase they would be negative (all of that from The Storytellers defeinitons and position, I personally love the story mechanics).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, just because something may cause detachment is neatly written on a list (as non-exhaustive as it may be) doesn't means my character knows it.<br /> <br /> On another subject? How does a character feels about violating his hound's flesh with vitae? About raping it's individuality with animalism whenever it suits him? about forcing it's loyalty not out of it's instinct but because of the Blood you feed it? All of those would be cause for detachment, if we're dealing with a touchstone. It stops being something to be regarded with a certain respect and becomes a tool.<br /> <br /> It's why Batman doesn't kills. Because after you've done it once, the next time becomes easier to justify, and easier, and easier until you're nothing but a murderer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:42:05-07:00","id":848906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848902#post848902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, just because something may cause detachment is neatly written on a list (as non-exhaustive as it may be) doesn't means my character knows it.<br /> <br /> On another subject? How does a character feels about violating his hound's flesh with vitae? About raping it's individuality with animalism whenever it suits him? about forcing it's loyalty not out of it's instinct but because of the Blood you feed it? All of those would be cause for detachment, if we're dealing with a touchstone. It stops being something to be regarded with a certain respect and becomes a tool.<br /> <br /> It's why Batman doesn't kills. Because after you've done it once, the next time becomes easier to justify, and easier, and easier until you're nothing but a murderer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with all of this, but the point of the discussion is about removing the story influencing mechanics. The Storyteller has made it clear that what xhe wants from the mechanics is primarily conflict resolution and powers. Story mechanics are not something xer group cares for, so I was asking why they like Humanity and suggested how I would change things to remove the story mechanic aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:03:53-07:00","id":848941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848850#post848850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen this? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/816385-official-chronicles-of-darkness-resources-animal-stats-condition-and-power-cards-faq-coming-soon\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...aq-coming-soon</a><br /> <br /> it presents new, not so frigging op stats for the dogs. As for a dog unable to do hacking being a worse option than a human retainer - that's not true. Dog is always loyal, while human has needs of his own <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, I looked at those stats and, yeah, they're absolutely identical to the original overpowered dog with one exception: the die pool is calculated incorrectly as 6 dice instead of 7, and the bite weapon is translated as 0L, instead of following the generalized rule of taking 1e values and subtracting 1 (or is the weapon translated as 0L with some inherent -1 to hit?). It even has the 8 Defense, which is what made it so powerful, far more than its weapon damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848856#post848856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The benefits are not having to hold onto your humanity. Low humanity vampires are less constrained; Inhuman vampires trade constrains but that tends to work out in their favor. Aside from that, I'm not sure how I'd model a Harmony-like Humanity. For one, there are no werewolf draugr, so creating a balanced humanity stat would mean amending that mechanic. Otherwise, the scales still weight heavy in favor of keeping humanity and as such, penalties for high humanity is double taxing IMHO. Second, not sure why you'd penalise high humanity. If you were to go down that line, disciplines and other powers of the blood might weaken for the highly humane but again, feels like double taxing because just using powers at that level of humanity would drive you towards center. So you use a power and not only is it lesser than it could be but the reason it is lesser is threatened. Suppose you could amp low humanity vampire powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were interested in doing this, and I am not right now, but maybe for the next game (but honestly, we'll probably be moving to Changeling by then, my favorite NWoD subgame...I just think vampire is easier for new players to the system), I would likely outline specific behaviors that the beast likes or doesn't, and apply bonuses to those things. Like, stealth rolls to stalk people, or intimidation, running, tracking, animal stuff. As your humanity dropped, you'd get a penalty to relating to people and resisting frenzy, but you'd get a bonus to those things. As your humanity rose, you'd get a bonus to relating to people and resisting frenzy, and maybe a penalty to things like lashing out or stuff tied to Blood Potency. Just in a very rough sense, at least. I'd like to read the Harmony rules first, though, to see more about how it's handled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848869#post848869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the character wouldn't delibretly choose a penalty but they don't know its a penalty. The character doesn't know what Humanity is, only the player does. So if the player chooses not to do something because it would lower their Humanity, then they are breaking the immersion you say you want. Which I think is why people suggested you remove Humanity, it is very much a story mechanic. If not remove it, make it secret, the players shouldnt know what their score is or what will affect it until it happens. If I was going for the deep in character immersion that you are that is what I would do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Humanity works ok for us because it is something that a character can't actually know, so, we are ok with a game mechanic telling us how it feels or works. In a similar vein, we'd be terrible annoyed by, say, an anger gauge telling us how angry we were, because we all understand anger and what it means, so, we don't need no stinking game mechanics to tell us what for. But Humanity? No, we're all human, so, none of us know what it's really like to no longer be. We can sort of relate to the struggles at higher humanities, like 7, where you're basically human except now you have to drink blood, but we can't really understand what it's like not to be able to eat or breath without concentrating on it. So, in that regard, a mechanic is perfectly warranted.<br /> <br /> I guess in my mind, the goal of the game in general (beside whatever your day to day or political goals are) is to hold on to the humanity you have while it lasts, and explore how you can actually pull that off in the context of vampire life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848869#post848869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while you could hack it to work with Vampire, the reason it is different is becuase they are both intended to inform the kind of stories that are told in the system. Werewolf is about balancing the Spirit and the Flesh, while vampire is about the eventual degradation of immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess Humanity could be taken that way, but I never did. Like I said above, it's more like a guage informing us what this thing we can't actually experience is like. It being a slide to the bestial works just as well as being a see-saw between beast and man--the point is that, either way, it's unrelatable without mechanically measuring it somehow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848869#post848869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My next question is about conditions, you said you like them. But you dont use beats, and you dont like meta roleplay incentives so are conditions just a list of status effects with names and rules for you? Cause thats like the least important or impressive thing about the condition system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sorry, but that's what they are to me. A nice, codified list of standardized effects that work cross game. For example, something I really like and used in particular is the Frightened condition. Now, instead of learning how a specific fear power works in each separate game (because they were all different), I can just use this one condition to represent the same thing regardless of how it was caused, by the Nightmare discipline, some Werewolf Gift, a Changeling contract, it doesn't matter. It's standardized. What's more, I can save time by just saying, &quot;you're frightened&quot; and now, anyone who knows the conditions well knows immediately what that is (or they can just pop over to quick list and find it fast), rather than us having to look up the specific power and reading paragraphs and interpreting them possibly differently from each other to see what that means for them.<br /> <br /> I also like them as the standard result for an exceptional success. Its basically a time saving thing for us, yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848893#post848893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A common transition re: Humanity in Sim games is to actually make it a known quantity by the characters. The physical changes, the limits to frenzy, the social modifiers - all of these things can be perceived in the game world, and thus perceived by the characters and commented on or manipulated by the characters. The man-beast struggle, Golconda / Draugr - these are game-world events intrinsically linked to humanity. Sure, the characters shouldn't be referring to &quot;my Humanity stat&quot; any more than they should be referring to their talent for &quot;Streetwise&quot; - but how good someone is at perusing black market goods or making networks with streetkids, or identifying gang signs - one character can probably say if they are better at doing those than a different character. One character could easily understand they were &quot;more human&quot; and &quot;less monstrous&quot; before they committed a sin.<br /> <br /> Humanity as a mechanic is way easier to translate to an IC phenomenon, than say, Beats or Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1<br /> Yes, I whole-heartedly agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848897#post848897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh sure, I would keep that concept, just not the list of sins, the dot value itself maybe, maybe not. I just think it is a clear story mechanic for the players to be able to avoid behaviours becuase they would be negative (all of that from The Storytellers defeinitons and position, I personally love the story mechanics).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the chart is the most important part of it, actually, and wish it was more comprehensive. It's a clear guideline for how someone should feel, what would feel wrong to them and what wouldn't, as they experience this slide into the Bestial that has no real translation to real human experience. &quot;Oh, I no longer care about injuring people for blood. Ok, I can work with that. Good.&quot; Or, &quot;Ok, so, a month without human contact is weird for me, but a few weeks is no big deal. Alright, so, I get lonely, but at a very slow rate. Got it.&quot;<br /> <br /> The humanity chart of sins is very descriptive, in my opinion. It describes very well, your slow degeneration into something other than human. At Humanity 5, you know you can survive car wrecks and other horrific accidents without sweating them, but at 6+, it's disturbing to you, and you probably still buckle your seat belt and get worried about driving too fast. At 5 or below, you probably wouldn't think twice about jumping off a bridge to get away from enemies, and you could drive at 60 miles per hour through a residential neighborhood without fear of anything but attention by cops. It's very telling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848902#post848902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, just because something may cause detachment is neatly written on a list (as non-exhaustive as it may be) doesn't means my character knows it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing. I, as a human, know what I find (un)comfortable. I have a conscience that lets me feel right from wrong. I know, personally, where my moral line is. I know I wouldn't steal a candy bar from a store, but that I wouldn't mind downloading a song from the internet. I get it. Why would my character not know where their lines are? Why would a vampire not know that a car crash is still (or is no longer) scary? Why would I not feel the loneliness intrinsic in missing human contact for 2 weeks or more? How could I not know whether I am ok with killing someone or not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848902#post848902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another subject? How does a character feels about violating his hound's flesh with vitae? About raping it's individuality with animalism whenever it suits him? about forcing it's loyalty not out of it's instinct but because of the Blood you feed it? All of those would be cause for detachment, if we're dealing with a touchstone. It stops being something to be regarded with a certain respect and becomes a tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an animal. It started out as a tool. Property destruction isn't on the list anymore, so, animals don't count anywhere on the chart. I'm sorry if you're an animal person or something, in which case, you might feel differently, but as far as I'm concerned? No, not an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  clarity 03-17-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:17:16-07:00","id":848948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848941#post848941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing. I, as a human, know what I find (un)comfortable. I have a conscience that lets me feel right from wrong. I know, personally, where my moral line is. I know I wouldn't steal a candy bar from a store, but that I wouldn't mind downloading a song from the internet. I get it. Why would my character not know where their lines are? Why would a vampire not know that a car crash is still (or is no longer) scary? Why would I not feel the loneliness intrinsic in missing human contact for 2 weeks or more? How could I not know whether I am ok with killing someone or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because humanity isn't integrity. Because of the trauma of realizing you aren't human anymore, by simple things like being able to enslave someone to your will on a caprice. Or being unable to see someone having your favorite dish and realizing it will never taste the same anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848941#post848941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an animal. It started out as a tool. Property destruction isn't on the list anymore, so, animals don't count anywhere on the chart. I'm sorry if you're an animal person or something, in which case, you might feel differently, but as far as I'm concerned? No, not an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you aren't an &quot;animal lover&quot; the character must be, if they're taking a dog as a touchstone. It's not a question for you, it's a question for the character. It's the sort of thing I explore with my characters, to make them resemble persons. To make them mature, and develop thru a story. Your players don't seem to want to go to any length in that direction, which is why I question your definition of immersion. Their sheets seems like a bunch dots filled out, maybe an outlined concept... and nothing else. How do you know they're being true to character? If one of your concerns are that they would drop any pretext of personality to gain a willpower back not unlike robots? I've no clue what you're simulating in that situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 03-17-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:24:18-07:00","id":848950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848941#post848941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'snip'<br /> <br /> It's an animal. It started out as a tool. Property destruction isn't on the list anymore, so, animals don't count anywhere on the chart. I'm sorry if you're an animal person or something, in which case, you might feel differently, but as far as I'm concerned? No, not an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that idea, but i think this last point is where it changes for me. What if I'm not an animal person, but my character is? You like Humanity because it gives you a sense of things you can't understand but how do you know that's true for all your players? And what about other situations, things that the players absolutley have no experience with, but aren't supernatural? Like the Frightened condition you mentioned, on top of being a mechanic effect, its supposed to encourage you to have your character act frightened. I've never been frightend to that degree, maybe you have, but having the conditon push me that way is part of the point.<br /> <br /> Not to say that you can't remove the things, but it sounds like you are saying you don't like the role-play/story mechanics, but only for things that you feel you already are familair with enough to not need them. The reason the humanity chart seems light is because your supposed to add more to it, the conditions don't cover everything cause your supposed to make more up yourself. Again, not saying you can't or shouldn't do it. Just trying to understand how you actually feel and interact with these mechanics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:39:51-07:00","id":848958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848948#post848948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because humanity isn't integrity. Because of the trauma of realizing you aren't human anymore, by simple things like being able to enslave someone to your will on a caprice. Or being unable to see someone having your favorite dish and realizing it will never taste the same anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Even if you aren't an &quot;animal lover&quot; the character must be, if they're taking a dog as a touchstone. It's not a question for you, it's a question for the character. It's the sort of thing I explore with my characters, to make them resemble persons. To make them mature, and develop thru a story. Your players don't seem to want to go to any length in that direction, which is why I question your definition of immersion. Their sheets seems like a bunch dots filled out, maybe an outlined concept... and nothing else. How do you know they're being true to character? If one of your concerns are that they would drop any pretext of personality to gain a willpower back not unlike robots? I've no clue what you're simulating in that situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>After reading this thread. ^ that right there is what I came up with as well. All it seems to be is dots on paper. I have been gaming for about 20 years, Dungeons and Dragons mostly, but now into Chronicles here. (started in 1E ).. but things like character goals and backstories should be something that comes Naturally to your players. Putting the label touchstone on your best friend, lover, dog, favorite restaurant, mother, family, grandmother's locket, whatever.... shouldnt be hard or far fetched. Even us who are still human might have them. When you have gone through something particularly shitty, who do you turn to? Where do you go? Having this makes your players Immersed in the game. it is EXACTLY what makes them like real people... it shouldn't be the opposite.<br /> <br /> Having a Mask/Dirge also helps players keep in mind who their characters are.. If they picked nurturer then are suddenly murdering everything in their path, they might want to rethink who they are. You are looking at it as an awkward step just to gain WP back... it is there to remind them of who they fundamentally are and what they stand for.<br /> <br /> <br /> A lot of new players struggle with what humanity is and like Ephsy said.. it is not Integrity. Not at all. It is you trying not to become the beast inside...<br /> <br /> These things are 110% meant to immerse your players into the game. To make them more than dots on paper. They are guidelines to help you play your role.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848455#post848455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Everyone wrote them down session one. A couple people did a couple on their list (mostly &quot;find a Haven&quot; for all 5 and &quot;get my dog&quot; for the one), and then we eventually all forgot about them. I think I could only name a single aspiration that anyone has (one of them wants to find out who killed them), and I doubt any of the players would remember, either, without looking at the sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you dont care about the character's goals and their aspirations... where they want to be.. how will you ever get there? The game will feel like you are on railroad tracks. It will make your players feel like they are nothing more than dots.. tools. Pointless.<br /> <br /> If my character's dreams were to fall in love, get married and make little ghouls...<br /> Or if someday I wanted to be the leader of the Ordo....<br /> Or buy a sports car and race it under the full moon with my best friend...<br /> <br /> how could I ever be more than dots if you didnt give me the time of day to get those goals done?<br /> perhaps not the most perfect of examples, but I hope my point is getting through...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848455#post848455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah, I think we're ignoring or downplaying: touchstones, mask/dirge, aspirations, beats, the whole social doors system, City/Clan/Covenant Status, and like half of the feeding/hunting rules. I guess it's probably most accurate to say that we are playing 1st edition with 2nd edition rules? I don't know. We started with everything and just phased out all that stuff that felt off--basically all the story game stuff, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly are you trying to accomplish with this thread and your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-17-2016, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:48:20-07:00","id":848962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848948#post848948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because humanity isn't integrity. Because of the trauma of realizing you aren't human anymore, by simple things like being able to enslave someone to your will on a caprice. Or being unable to see someone having your favorite dish and realizing it will never taste the same anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand why you wouldn't know that it might bother you to see someone eating your favorite food until you see it. That doesn't make a lot of sense to me. If it'd be a breaking point for you, I am pretty sure even just the thought of it might get you worked up a bit. You might not be constantly aware, but if someone invites you to your favorite restaurant from life, and going there and watching them eat would be a breaking point, I am positive that you would know right away, when they extended the invitation, that accepting is going to be uncomfortable. You won't go there totally fine and then be like, &quot;Oh crap! I forgot I don't eat!&quot; I don't see that happening. That would require someone who was remarkable self-unaware.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848948#post848948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you aren't an &quot;animal lover&quot; the character must be, if they're taking a dog as a touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, remember, they didn't really pick touchstones in good faith. They didn't like the system from the start and railed against it. I just didn't realize &quot;officially&quot; until recently. His character cares about the dog the way someone else might care about their mint condition Boba Fett action figure. It's a prized possession, but, it's still a dog and not a person. You can't &quot;rape it&quot; with Animalism--that just makes it a more effective tool. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848948#post848948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you know they're being true to character?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not my job, or anyone else's, to police whether or not they're being true to character. I trust that they are because they're my players, and that's that. It's up to them to be true. If they say they'd do X in Y situation, they would. For me to tell someone they're playing a character they invented wrong would be ridiculous, as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848948#post848948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one of your concerns are that they would drop any pretext of personality to gain a willpower back not unlike robots? I've no clue what you're simulating in that situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that situation? Nothing, which is why I took the meta reward out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848950#post848950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that idea, but i think this last point is where it changes for me. What if I'm not an animal person, but my character is? You like Humanity because it gives you a sense of things you can't understand but how do you know that's true for all your players? And what about other situations, things that the players absolutley have no experience with, but aren't supernatural? Like the Frightened condition you mentioned, on top of being a mechanic effect, its supposed to encourage you to have your character act frightened. I've never been frightend to that degree, maybe you have, but having the conditon push me that way is part of the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I have never been that scared. That's what the condition is there for. It lays out explicitly what it means to be that scared. As for the dog, if the guy was an animal person, I don't think he'd do anything to hurt the dog. I wouldn't have to police his behavior, because he'd have a stricter sense of what's wrong or right in regard to the dog than I would, that's for sure. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848950#post848950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to say that you can't remove the things, but it sounds like you are saying you don't like the role-play/story mechanics, but only for things that you feel you already are familair with enough to not need them. The reason the humanity chart seems light is because your supposed to add more to it, the conditions don't cover everything cause your supposed to make more up yourself. Again, not saying you can't or shouldn't do it. Just trying to understand how you actually feel and interact with these mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you could say that. I don't really see Humantiy as a story mechanic, though, so, it's hard to understand your position and what you think mine is. I generally don't add to the Humanity chart, no, not without consultation with the players so as to avoid a &quot;gotcha!&quot; moment. I think it's general enough to extrapolate things that make sense as falling within a certain category or another. But, as I said, we've only had two detachment rolls so far in almost 3 months of game. And that's ok, nobody is upset that it hasn't had as much of an impact as I expected from having played 1e (none of my current players have played 1e or the &quot;classic&quot; WoD). Conditions, well, no, I haven't officially created any, but we've made a couple up off the cuff for various reasons. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T14:10:34-07:00","id":848977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848958#post848958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading this thread. ^ that right there is what I came up with as well. All it seems to be is dots on paper. I have been gaming for about 20 years, Dungeons and Dragons mostly, but now into Chronicles here. (started in 1E ).. but things like character goals and backstories should be something that comes Naturally to your players. Putting the label touchstone on your best friend, lover, dog, favorite restaurant, mother, family, grandmother's locket, whatever.... shouldnt be hard or far fetched. Even us who are still human might have them. When you have gone through something particularly shitty, who do you turn to? Where do you go? Having this makes your players Immersed in the game. it is EXACTLY what makes them like real people... it shouldn't be the opposite.<br /> <br /> Having a Mask/Dirge also helps players keep in mind who their characters are.. If they picked nurturer then are suddenly murdering everything in their path, they might want to rethink who they are. You are looking at it as an awkward step just to gain WP back... it is there to remind them of who they fundamentally are and what they stand for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having character goals and backstories does come naturally. Codifying and setting those thing in stone (or just pencil) is the problem. Not using aspirations doesn't mean the PCs have no goals, it means nobody writes the goals down.<br /> <br /> Like, let's say I need to go to the bathroom. I don't first declare out loud &quot;I need to go to the bathroom&quot; before I go. I just do it. They don't codify their goals and aspirations, but they still pursue them. And it is obvious what their goals are based on the actions they take in the game. So, I don't need it written on a sheet to see that they want to find a haven. When I say, &quot;Ok, what do you do tonight?&quot; and they say, &quot;I start looking for a Haven by...&quot; I am made well aware of what their goals are.<br /> <br /> It's not <i>having</i> goals that is a problem. It's not having a personality type that bothers us. It's not having people you turn to in a crisis that's an issue. It's <i>mechanizing</i> those things. It's making them something you write down ahead of time, then get rewarded for following through with.<br /> <br /> I don't understand why this is so hard to grasp. Let me try an example. One of the characters in the group is snarky. She just is. She doesn't have the word &quot;Snarky&quot; written down anywhere because she doesn't need it written down to remember that she's snarky. She doesn't need me to reward her when she remembers to be snarky because it's not something she could forget. She just <i>is</i> snarky. That's it. Simple. <br /> <br /> Last session, the PCs wanted to investigate some children that went missing from their territory, just in case it was a vampire poaching from them (and breaking the law, since feeding from children is illegal in this city). Nobody had to write down on the sheet, &quot;Find missing kids.&quot; They just went and did that. I said, &quot;What do you guys do?&quot; and they described how they started investigating. Specifically, in this case, they went to local parks near where the majority of the kids were last seen. At no point did anyone require a meta-reward to do this. They just did it.<br /> <br /> But see, leaving that reward in there could have led to problems. What if, at the beginning of the session, they had written down &quot;Find missing kids&quot; only to discover during the session that there was a more pressing problem (just call it &quot;Problem X&quot;). Now, there's a conflict of interest. Do they stick to what they decided before the game started for the reward, or do this other thing that's more important to the character, but carries no reward? There's no reason to create this cognitive dissonance. Just remove the reward and they will do what their characters want without any carrot/stick. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848958#post848958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These things are 110% meant to immerse your players into the game. To make them more than dots on paper. They are guidelines to help you play your role.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they are. I think they are there to keep players acting in a consistent and predictable manner, to help...I don't want to say weaker exactly, but have no better word...GMs and players handle taking over the persona of someone else. They are there to make sure interesting stuff happens <i>no matter what</i>, so things are artificially more dramatic than they would normally be. It has very little to do with the kind of immersion I am talking about. Immersed people don't need these things codified, and the codifications create more opportunity for being pulled from immersion. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848958#post848958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you dont care about the character's goals and their aspirations... where they want to be.. how will you ever get there? The game will feel like you are on railroad tracks. It will make your players feel like they are nothing more than dots.. tools. Pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't even understand how you jump to the railroad conclusion. It's not that I don't care about the character's goals and aspirations, I just, you know, don't care about forcing them to write them specifically down. I can tell what they want from their actions and words at the table. I don't need to see it in writing to pick up on it. And, as I said earlier, I don't drive the action when I run a game. I don't tell PCs what they do..they tell me. They go where they want to go and do what they want to do, and I just make sure the world keeps up and reacts in a plausible fashion. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848958#post848958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my character's dreams were to fall in love, get married and make little ghouls...<br /> Or if someday I wanted to be the leader of the Ordo....<br /> Or buy a sports car and race it under the full moon with my best friend...<br /> <br /> how could I ever be more than dots if you didnt give me the time of day to get those goals done?<br /> perhaps not the most perfect of examples, but I hope my point is getting through...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really, sorry. If you wanted to get married and make ghouls, you would, you know, pursue that in game. You would buy a sports car (or try to make enough money to do so) and then, race it. You would try and climb the ranks of the Ordo. I don't understand how not writing this down means you can't do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848958#post848958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly are you trying to accomplish with this thread and your game?</div> </div> </div> </div>My initial purpose was seeing if anything other than the Ventrue flaw broke if I took Touchstones out, and secondarily, crowdsourcing what I could replace the Ventrue bane with that didn't involve touchstones. As the thread went on, I discovered more and more how I felt about things and why, and just fully embraced removing the stuff I didn't like. I'm still interested in Ventrue bane ideas, but now, I'm just having fun talking about how different people roleplay and how these mechanics interact/interfere with that. I'm trying to help people understand where I'm coming from and having a good time talking about a game I love.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T14:27:24-07:00","id":848987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848977#post848977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having character goals and backstories does come naturally. Codifying and setting those thing in stone (or just pencil) is the problem. Not using aspirations doesn't mean the PCs have no goals, it means nobody writes the goals down.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not what I interpreted. my bad there. It sounded like you didnt have any goals. Personally I dont make my players write down aspirations either nor reward them, but my players are consistantly letting me know what their characters want to do... In more ways than just saying they need to go to the bathroom. Then it is my job to incorporate that into my story. Which is why it's good to know what they are and not &quot;forget about them&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848977#post848977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not <i>having</i> goals that is a problem. It's not having a personality type that bothers us. It's not having people you turn to in a crisis that's an issue. It's <i>mechanizing</i> those things. It's making them something you write down ahead of time, then get rewarded for following through with.<br /> <br /> I don't understand why this is so hard to grasp. Let me try an example. One of the characters in the group is snarky. She just is. She doesn't have the word &quot;Snarky&quot; written down anywhere because she doesn't need it written down to remember that she's snarky. She doesn't need me to reward her when she remembers to be snarky because it's not something she could forget. She just <i>is</i> snarky. That's it. Simple.<br /> <br /> Last session, the PCs wanted to investigate some children that went missing from their territory, just in case it was a vampire poaching from them (and breaking the law, since feeding from children is illegal in this city). Nobody had to write down on the sheet, &quot;Find missing kids.&quot; They just went and did that. I said, &quot;What do you guys do?&quot; and they described how they started investigating. Specifically, in this case, they went to local parks near where the majority of the kids were last seen. At no point did anyone require a meta-reward to do this. They just did it.<br /> <br /> But see, leaving that reward in there could have led to problems. What if, at the beginning of the session, they had written down &quot;Find missing kids&quot; only to discover during the session that there was a more pressing problem (just call it &quot;Problem X&quot;). Now, there's a conflict of interest. Do they stick to what they decided before the game started for the reward, or do this other thing that's more important to the character, but carries no reward? There's no reason to create this cognitive dissonance. Just remove the reward and they will do what their characters want without any carrot/stick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it is my player base... But I have never run into characters doing out of character stupid stuff just to get the reward that follows. I give my players more credit than to worry about whether or not they will do that. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848977#post848977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't even understand how you jump to the railroad conclusion. It's not that I don't care about the character's goals and aspirations, I just, you know, don't care about forcing them to write them specifically down. I can tell what they want from their actions and words at the table. I don't need to see it in writing to pick up on it. And, as I said earlier, I don't drive the action when I run a game. I don't tell PCs what they do..they tell me. They go where they want to go and do what they want to do, and I just make sure the world keeps up and reacts in a plausible fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because you said &quot; <i>Honestly? Everyone wrote them down session one. A couple people did a couple on their list (mostly &quot;find a Haven&quot; for all 5 and &quot;get my dog&quot; for the one), and then we eventually all forgot about them. I think I could only name a single aspiration that anyone has (one of them wants to find out who killed them), and I doubt any of the players would remember, either, without looking at the sheet. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848977#post848977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial purpose was seeing if anything other than the Ventrue flaw broke if I took Touchstones out, and secondarily, crowdsourcing what I could replace the Ventrue bane with that didn't involve touchstones. As the thread went on, I discovered more and more how I felt about things and why, and just fully embraced removing the stuff I didn't like. I'm still interested in Ventrue bane ideas, but now, I'm just having fun talking about how different people roleplay and how these mechanics interact/interfere with that. I'm trying to help people understand where I'm coming from and having a good time talking about a game I love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I think that this thread is mislabeled .. There are tons of threads about the ventrue flaw and how to fix it.. I believe Griatus posted the links ( or it could have been someone else )<br /> <br /> Touchstones are way more than just the ventrue bane.. As we can see from this thread. it links heavily into the whole humanity thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T14:48:20-07:00","id":848993,"title":"","content":"Addition: my group does not play with beats or writing down aspirations either. So i really do see your point of not writing certain things down... But we do love the humanity, touchstones, mask/dirge,, conditions and banes. it makes for a very flavorful character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T14:52:19-07:00","id":848998,"title":"","content":"Other mechanical ideas for tweaking the Ventrue Bane sans Touchstones I had today while stuck in traffic.<ul><li>Allow characters to spend Willpower on Detachment to gain the (+2) bonus they would normally get from having a touchstone. Then you can hit the Ventrue with the (-2) penalty to make it a little more robust at base, and they can still spend WP to break even.</li> <li>Require Ventrue to check for Detachment on Breaking Points at one above their humanity. In otherwords, a Humanity 6 Ventrue still has to roll for Breaking Points on the chart at level 7. They aren't hit with a penalty to the Detachment roll itself, but will be rolling more often then their counterparts for doing the same stuff.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848977#post848977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they are. I think they are there to keep players acting in a consistent and predictable manner, to help...I don't want to say weaker exactly, but have no better word...GMs and players handle taking over the persona of someone else</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where you get into trouble. : ) Maybe the word you are looking for is 'less experienced' rather than 'weaker' - but I suspect the argument would by 180'd by a lot of people reacting to your ideas in that isn't it actually a sign of a weaker/less experienced player if they completely break out of character when mechanics get involved? I've got years under my belt, and I don't find it difficult at all to keep something in the back of my player mind and still roleplay the character.<br /> <br /> I think you underestimate how much we parse these kind of meta-things all the time. I mean, I might have two important character goals to complete in a night. I need to go beat up a rival's ghoul to send a message, and I need to talk to the Harpy about a boon dispute. All things being equal, the character wants to do the ghoul thing first. However, I know our session ends in about 30 minutes, and I don't want to start a big combat scene, but I could still get the Harpy bit done. So I make the less 'true' choice because of the OOC constraints without batting an eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T15:20:37-07:00","id":849009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848987#post848987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it is my player base... But I have never run into characters doing out of character stupid stuff just to get the reward that follows. I give my players more credit than to worry about whether or not they will do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great, but why include the rewards at all, then? I can see you actually don't, so, we...agree?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848987#post848987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because you said &quot; <i>Honestly? Everyone wrote them down session one. A couple people did a couple on their list (mostly &quot;find a Haven&quot; for all 5 and &quot;get my dog&quot; for the one), and then we eventually all forgot about them. I think I could only name a single aspiration that anyone has (one of them wants to find out who killed them), and I doubt any of the players would remember, either, without looking at the sheet. &quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I see. So, what I meant was that finding out who killed the guy was the only thing actually written down on anyone's sheet that I can remember. I didn't mean to imply they had no goals, just that they wrote down goals right away, and then we stopped looking at them and just played. Which, apparently, you did, too. Nice to see I'm not the only one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848987#post848987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I think that this thread is mislabeled .. There are tons of threads about the ventrue flaw and how to fix it.. I believe Griatus posted the links ( or it could have been someone else )<br /> <br /> Touchstones are way more than just the ventrue bane.. As we can see from this thread. it links heavily into the whole humanity thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and seeing where it links was kind of the purpose. I saw a ton of old threads on the Ventrue bane, but almost all the suggestions tied back to the touchstone system, or were basically what I was already intending to do, so, they didn't help. And besides, the Ventrue bane was secondary in my mind initially. But threads often change course and become about something their title no longer reflects. I see that as natural on a message board.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848993#post848993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Addition: my group does not play with beats or writing down aspirations either. So i really do see your point of not writing certain things down... But we do love the humanity, touchstones, mask/dirge,, conditions and banes. it makes for a very flavorful character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like Humanity, conditions, and banes. Turns out we just don't like touchstones and mask/dirge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848998#post848998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other mechanical ideas for tweaking the Ventrue Bane sans Touchstones I had today while stuck in traffic.<ul><li>Allow characters to spend Willpower on Detachment to gain the (+2) bonus they would normally get from having a touchstone. Then you can hit the Ventrue with the (-2) penalty to make it a little more robust at base, and they can still spend WP to break even.</li> <li>Require Ventrue to check for Detachment on Breaking Points at one above their humanity. In otherwords, a Humanity 6 Ventrue still has to roll for Breaking Points on the chart at level 7. They aren't hit with a penalty to the Detachment roll itself, but will be rolling more often then their counterparts for doing the same stuff.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>These are interesting, and I will consider them. The first seems kind of, I don't know, like it's just throwing numbers around the base system to make the flaw work, so I am less inclined, but the latter is better. I will have to evaluate whether it, or my flat -1 detachment will have a greater effect on making Ventrue act...in a similarly limited fashion to the Daeva/Mekhet adjusting for their flaws.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848998#post848998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is where you get into trouble. : ) Maybe the word you are looking for is 'less experienced' rather than 'weaker' -</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know it wasn't great. Weaker isn't really what I meant, but I couldn't come up with anything. I wouldn't even say less experienced, because it's not necessarily something experience gets you. It's some ephemeral quality that tends to come out more with different play agendas. Its more for people who are...I want to say &quot;directors&quot; or &quot;actors&quot; rather than immersing in the person. It's a quality people have when they excessively think of their character as someone other than themselves, and it makes it hard for them to act as that person rather than themselves without guidance/reminders.<br /> <br /> I knew a guy in D&amp;D, actually, who had to keep a little piece of paper next to his gruff dwarven barbarian that said something like, &quot;Be aggressive and gruff. Stay loyal to your friends and protect the weak. Rush ahead. Stumble over words.&quot; I wouldn't say the guy was a bad roleplayer, and &quot;weak&quot; is not the right connotation for him, but he definitely had difficulty <i>being</i> his character, rather than just controlling him. It was more like a weak connection than a weak person. I don't know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848998#post848998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you underestimate how much we parse these kind of meta-things all the time. I mean, I might have two important character goals to complete in a night. I need to go beat up a rival's ghoul to send a message, and I need to talk to the Harpy about a boon dispute. All things being equal, the character wants to do the ghoul thing first. However, I know our session ends in about 30 minutes, and I don't want to start a big combat scene, but I could still get the Harpy bit done. So I make the less 'true' choice because of the OOC constraints without batting an eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but that's kind of a perfect example of exactly what I'm talking about. You picked the less &quot;true&quot; choice because of OOC concerns. That's literally what I'm trying to avoid. Now, I'm not saying my players will automatically mess up and always do something stupid and out of character to feed a reward cycle--I am only saying that doing so is an unnecessary temptation, that the game works fine without those reward cycles, so, why use them and put anything at risk for no reason?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T15:34:01-07:00","id":849012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848962#post848962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not my job, or anyone else's, to police whether or not they're being true to character. I trust that they are because they're my players, and that's that. It's up to them to be true. If they say they'd do X in Y situation, they would. For me to tell someone they're playing a character they invented wrong would be ridiculous, as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> In that situation? Nothing, which is why I took the meta reward out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>These two statements are contradictory. You DO feel that it is wrong for them to play their character that way, otherwise you wouldn't remove the reward. You say you trust your players to play to their concept but then say that they will drop their concept (or overplay to the point of ridiclousness it in this case) if there is mechanical incentive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848962#post848962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I have never been that scared. That's what the condition is there for. It lays out explicitly what it means to be that scared. As for the dog, if the guy was an animal person, I don't think he'd do anything to hurt the dog. I wouldn't have to police his behavior, because he'd have a stricter sense of what's wrong or right in regard to the dog than I would, that's for sure.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is the guy in this case the player or the character? As for the condition point, that's kinda the part that I was saying you seemed to be ignoring before, the condition is there to point you at roleplaying at being frightened and then rewards you for doing so with its resolution. Thus is a 'story mechanic'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848962#post848962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess you could say that. I don't really see Humantiy as a story mechanic, though, so, it's hard to understand your position and what you think mine is. I generally don't add to the Humanity chart, no, not without consultation with the players so as to avoid a &quot;gotcha!&quot; moment. I think it's general enough to extrapolate things that make sense as falling within a certain category or another. But, as I said, we've only had two detachment rolls so far in almost 3 months of game. And that's ok, nobody is upset that it hasn't had as much of an impact as I expected from having played 1e (none of my current players have played 1e or the &quot;classic&quot; WoD). Conditions, well, no, I haven't officially created any, but we've made a couple up off the cuff for various reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>My position is not really what I'm arguing from (which is likely why its confusing), I am trying to put myself in your position and asking questions to help that but with the perspective of the stated intention of the mechanics that the devs have shared on these forums.<br /> <br /> As far as creating Breaking Points and Conditions, yeah, the intention would be that it is done with player inclusion, but that is also something that would seem to be a 'story-mechanic'. <br /> <br /> It seems like you seperate the 'story mechanics' you like or not based on whether you think you need them to inform you about 'how' to roleplay a thing. Feeling you aren't familiar with = good, one you are familiar with = bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last session, the PCs wanted to investigate some children that went missing from their territory, just in case it was a vampire poaching from them (and breaking the law, since feeding from children is illegal in this city). Nobody had to write down on the sheet, &quot;Find missing kids.&quot; They just went and did that. I said, &quot;What do you guys do?&quot; and they described how they started investigating. Specifically, in this case, they went to local parks near where the majority of the kids were last seen. At no point did anyone require a meta-reward to do this. They just did it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is what I was talking about with Aspirations. The thing with Aspirations is that they should have had Find Missing Kids as an Aspiration BEFORE you had the kids go missing. That's the players clue to you that they want their character to be in a situation to find missing kids, its there to tell you the storyteller to have kids go missing for them to find not the other way around. If their Aspirations are just written in response to the situation you've already put them in then yeah they are going to be boring. And if you give them a situation, they say they want to do it and then you give them something else to do that is more pressing, well you chose to do that.<br /> <br /> Ninja'd a bit on some of this, but here it is anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T15:36:57-07:00","id":849013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849009#post849009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's great, but why include the rewards at all, then? I can see you actually don't, so, we...agree?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you give your players EXP ? That is a *reward* for playing. So yes. I give my players rewards. If you dont reward your players, how do they grow?<br /> <br /> I dont see getting will power back as a reward, but more of something you have to do. See you &quot;reward&quot; your players for day sleep, the way that many of us &quot;reward&quot; our players for having meaningful conversations and connections with their touchstones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849012#post849012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, this is what I was talking about with Aspirations. The thing with Aspirations is that they should have had Find Missing Kids as an Aspiration BEFORE you had the kids go missing. That's the players clue to you that they want their character to be in a situation to find missing kids, its there to tell you the storyteller to have kids go missing for them to find not the other way around. If their Aspirations are just written in response to the situation you've already put them in then yeah they are going to be boring. And if you give them a situation, they say they want to do it and then you give them something else to do that is more pressing, well you chose to do that.<br /> <br /> Ninja'd a bit on some of this, but here it is anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was trying to say... They tell you what they want BEFORE, then you shape the story....<br /> <br /> to expand on my original thing... What if my goal was to become the leader of the Ordo.... But the city you put me in has no ordo, no one to teach me, no covenants at all? How do I complete my goal, you know, In game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-17-2016, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T16:04:07-07:00","id":849021,"title":"","content":"To clear one thing up, I actually think that Aspirations do not work for you The Storyteller. They are not at all in line with the simulationist outline you have laid out before. They are defeintly a meta story mechanic. My previous point was just about illustrating WHY they don't work for you and why you dont understand why they work for others. It's not the reward that is the problem, it's that they are intended to shape the story from a meta perspective, something that you personally do not want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T16:11:19-07:00","id":849024,"title":"","content":"um.. also.. Willpower is not a META reward. Beats and experience is. But Willpower is something very tangible in world and to the characters. It's basically how tired and exhausted mentally they are. (Hence why reaffirming yourself and hanging out with touchstones restores it, and why when you have more of it, you perform better).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T16:13:17-07:00","id":849025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849021#post849021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clear one thing up, I actually think that Aspirations do not work for you The Storyteller. They are not at all in line with the simulationist outline you have laid out before. They are defeintly a meta story mechanic. My previous point was just about illustrating WHY they don't work for you and why you dont understand why they work for others. It's not the reward that is the problem, it's that they are intended to shape the story from a meta perspective, something that you personally do not want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do not agree with this at all. My players mostly pick IC aspirations, and they frequently shift them as things change. We only shift them between sessions, but it could as well be made during a session, and it rewards a player for succeeding at his tasks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So in the task where player sets out a Haven and then Problem X happens, well, he can start out with anAspiration &quot;Get a Haven&quot;,and then shift it to &quot;Fix Problem X&quot;, which indicates to everybody that Haven is no longer that important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T16:22:45-07:00","id":849028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849025#post849025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I do not agree with this at all. My players mostly pick IC aspirations, and they frequently shift them as things change. We only shift them between sessions, but it could as well be made during a session, and it rewards a player for succeeding at his tasks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So in the task where player sets out a Haven and then Problem X happens, well, he can start out with an Aspiration &quot;Get a Haven&quot;,and then shift it to &quot;Fix Problem X&quot;, which indicates to everybody that Haven is no longer that important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at it from The Storyteller's playstyle, you say it is an IC choice, so does that mean that your player' character states outloud that Finding a Haven is no longer important because Solving problem X is important? Because if its not stated in-character, then it is a meta concept, even if it is ALSO something that the character wants. If the player is telling the other players that its changing and not the character then that is meta. And rewarding characters with Beats(or Experience) is meta as you just said yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T16:35:27-07:00","id":849033,"title":"","content":"Sorry, ElvesofZion.. wrong quote. I meant to quote this:<br /> See, this is what I was talking about with Aspirations. The thing with Aspirations is that they should have had Find Missing Kids as an Aspiration BEFORE you had the kids go missing. That's the players clue to you that they want their character to be in a situation to find missing kids, its there to tell you the storyteller to have kids go missing for them to find not the other way around. If their Aspirations are just written in response to the situation you've already put them in then yeah they are going to be boring. And if you give them a situation, they say they want to do it and then you give them something else to do that is more pressing, well you chose to do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do not agree with the BEFORE part <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yes, other than that Aspirations is a meta consideration. And they can easily be removed - you just reward around 1 more beat per session for good roleplay (for those who do) and you don't lose anything. Assuming that you weren't using Aspirations for planning further stories and stuff, and since we're not considering planning sessions here - it's all good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T16:42:47-07:00","id":849035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849028#post849028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looking at it from The Storyteller's playstyle, you say it is an IC choice, so does that mean that your player' character states outloud that Finding a Haven is no longer important because Solving problem X is important? Because if its not stated in-character, then it is a meta concept, even if it is ALSO something that the character wants. If the player is telling the other players that its changing and not the character then that is meta. And rewarding characters with Beats(or Experience) is meta as you just said yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Characters have brains, they can think things they don't need to say things outloud for it to be in-character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T16:45:54-07:00","id":849038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849033#post849033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, ElvesofZion.. wrong quote. I meant to quote this:<br /> <br /> I do not agree with the BEFORE part <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yes, other than that Aspirations is a meta consideration. And they can easily be removed - you just reward around 1 more beat per session for good roleplay (for those who do) and you don't lose anything. Assuming that you weren't using Aspirations for planning further stories and stuff, and since we're not considering planning sessions here - it's all good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, ok then.<br /> <br /> But you kinda make my counterpoint for me there. If you only make reactive in-character Aspirations, whats the point? You could just give extra beats out for playing in the session at all. I could see it if they were out of character (and likely negative or otherwise interesting) then it would essentialy be an additional good roleplaying beat. <br /> <br /> That wouldn't be a very inovative tool, just shifting some of the beats around. Having them done at character creation and then replaced at the end of each session ( I don't have my books right now, but I'm pretty sure it says to replace them at the end of each session) gives the storyteller fodder for the next Chapter, that i<br /> s a much more interesting mechanic to add to the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T16:48:12-07:00","id":849039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849035#post849035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Characters have brains, they can think things they don't need to say things outloud for it to be in-character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Graitius said <i>which indicates to everybody that Haven is no longer that important.</i> , indiciating that others were aware of it, thus its either said in-character in such a way that others can perceive it or out of character and it is meta knowledge for the other players and/or storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T22:16:15-07:00","id":849145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849012#post849012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These two statements are contradictory. You DO feel that it is wrong for them to play their character that way, otherwise you wouldn't remove the reward. You say you trust your players to play to their concept but then say that they will drop their concept (or overplay to the point of ridiclousness it in this case) if there is mechanical incentive.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, Willpower is a concrete, in character thing. You know when you get willpower. So, when you receive it as a meta-reward, your character knows you got it. It's this confusing intermixing of knowledge that just...doesn't work.<br /> <br /> And I will say, I've even had this discussion with at least one guy in the group, and we both agree: we don't just want to immerse in our characters, we want our characters to succeed in their endeavors. So, I don't want to call it winning, but, I mean, it's winning. We also want to win. I guess the best phrasing is that we want to immerse in winners.<br /> <br /> So, when we could get willpower, we're going to get it. We're going to get it, and we're going to use it to win. And so, we don't want to be offered Willpower for things that will make us choose between winning or immersion. We want both, so making them mutually exclusive, regardless of what we choose, is not a good thing.<br /> <br /> Now, honestly, it wouldn't affect the entire group that badly...most just absolutely don't care about the rules whatsoever. But for at least two of us, it's important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849012#post849012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like you seperate the 'story mechanics' you like or not based on whether you think you need them to inform you about 'how' to roleplay a thing. Feeling you aren't familiar with = good, one you are familiar with = bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I can parse it out that way. The things you are saying are story mechanics that I like, I just don't see them as being story mechanics. If this description helps you understand me, then, ok, go for it, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849012#post849012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, this is what I was talking about with Aspirations. The thing with Aspirations is that they should have had Find Missing Kids as an Aspiration BEFORE you had the kids go missing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, so, that absolutely makes me not want to use them. We're not interested in directly affecting the &quot;story&quot; in that way. The kids should go missing because someone took them, not because a player wanted their character to save kids. So, yeah, definitely don't want aspirations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849013#post849013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">to expand on my original thing... What if my goal was to become the leader of the Ordo.... But the city you put me in has no ordo, no one to teach me, no covenants at all? How do I complete my goal, you know, In game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you make someone who wants to become the leader of the Ordo in a city with no Ordo? How would your character even know about the Ordo in order to want to be their leader?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849021#post849021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clear one thing up, I actually think that Aspirations do not work for you The Storyteller. They are not at all in line with the simulationist outline you have laid out before. They are defeintly a meta story mechanic. My previous point was just about illustrating WHY they don't work for you and why you dont understand why they work for others. It's not the reward that is the problem, it's that they are intended to shape the story from a meta perspective, something that you personally do not want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, ok. While I don't actually understand, as in, internalize, why people like Aspirations, I know intellectually why they do. The have a different gaming agenda. That's fine. People can do what they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849024#post849024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">um.. also.. Willpower is not a META reward. Beats and experience is. But Willpower is something very tangible in world and to the characters. It's basically how tired and exhausted mentally they are. (Hence why reaffirming yourself and hanging out with touchstones restores it, and why when you have more of it, you perform better).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Willpower is a tangible, in character resource. But you can receive it for doing things that don't make sense in character, so, that could potentially make it a meta reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T00:31:24-07:00","id":849172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849038#post849038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you kinda make my counterpoint for me there. If you only make reactive in-character Aspirations, whats the point? You could just give extra beats out for playing in the session at all. I could see it if they were out of character (and likely negative or otherwise interesting) then it would essentialy be an additional good roleplaying beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indicating what your character and you find interesting and important? For example, as a storyteller in a more freeform story, I could present my players with some issues with Invictus, with someone messing in their feeding grounds, and with one of their touchstones getting human problems you could easily help with (given your newfound power). If you only take an Aspiration to fix one of these problems, I know that that kind of story interests you and others - not so much (or at least not as much as that one)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T03:58:35-07:00","id":849192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849009#post849009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are interesting, and I will consider them. The first seems kind of, I don't know, like it's just throwing numbers around the base system to make the flaw work, so I am less inclined, but the latter is better. I will have to evaluate whether it, or my flat -1 detachment will have a greater effect on making Ventrue act...in a similarly limited fashion to the Daeva/Mekhet adjusting for their flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps we can work from the other end: figure out how you want the Ventrue to act, then write a flaw that encourages that behaviour.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T06:51:39-07:00","id":849225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849145#post849145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, Willpower is a concrete, in character thing. You know when you get willpower. So, when you receive it as a meta-reward, your character knows you got it. It's this confusing intermixing of knowledge that just...doesn't work.<br /> <br /> And I will say, I've even had this discussion with at least one guy in the group, and we both agree: we don't just want to immerse in our characters, we want our characters to succeed in their endeavors. So, I don't want to call it winning, but, I mean, it's winning. We also want to win. I guess the best phrasing is that we want to immerse in winners.<br /> <br /> So, when we could get willpower, we're going to get it. We're going to get it, and we're going to use it to win. And so, we don't want to be offered Willpower for things that will make us choose between winning or immersion. We want both, so making them mutually exclusive, regardless of what we choose, is not a good thing.<br /> <br /> Now, honestly, it wouldn't affect the entire group that badly...most just absolutely don't care about the rules whatsoever. But for at least two of us, it's important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered the Will to Power Twist? Basically, Willpower is assigned to one of the Aspirations a player has and can only be spend to move towards that goal. Spending the Willpower also yields a beat. It is suggested you drop both the beat given for completing a goal, and the option of taking dramatic failures for beats. That way, it makes sense for players to have long reach goals (which you can limit to character knowledge and desire to remove the meta part) that focus on victory!<br /> <br /> Do I think you should use it? No. You made it clear you don't like uneven advancement and this might produce that.<br /> <br /> Why bring it up? It seems to have the seeds of a good Venture flaw. Venture are tied to a goal at all times. Willpower can only be spend in pursuit of the goal. They just can't bring themselves to invest in what isn't a goal. Throw in Willpower refresh only upon goal completion (or a milestone) and suddenly all Venture are driven by nature, being completely despondent in loss and exuberant in victory! (It would also model the idea that the Ven always win: It doesn't help them win but it does add a cost to pursuing hopeless goals. Better attach yourself to the winning horse than back the underdog unless you have a trump card.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  Some moar splaining 03-18-2016, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T08:05:09-07:00","id":849272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849145#post849145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, Willpower is a concrete, in character thing. You know when you get willpower. So, when you receive it as a meta-reward, your character knows you got it. It's this confusing intermixing of knowledge that just...doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure your character does NOT know what will power is and how to spend it and when you get it. It's not like dollar bills in your wallet where you can count them. You dont In character know that you have 6 will power points and that you become depressed and unmotivated when you run out. You dont have the bad guy hand you one when you get it back. So I whole heartedly disagree that it's an in character thing. I know that your characters know that they can try really hard some times... but I dont think they know that doing so costs them 1 will power and to reiterate I do not think they feel it when they get that will power back. They might feel better or comforted but they dont take that 1 willpower point and put it back on their card. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849145#post849145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you make someone who wants to become the leader of the Ordo in a city with no Ordo? How would your character even know about the Ordo in order to want to be their leader?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because upon character creation you make a ton of out of character choices. Like you pick Deava because you want Majesty Or you pick a Gangrel because you want some X bloodline because you think the 5th dot is awesome and you want to work toward achieving it. Players dont always know what the story teller has in mind. So If OOC you get an idea for a character concept and want to play it. ( like being ordo ) your story teller should give you options to get there. Those are out of character things you do for your character. How do you even know what a Daeva is until you suddenly are one? ... Unless your human got to meet all 5 of the clans, the vampires explained to them what they are and then your human picked a clan... It was a player choice for your character...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T09:50:13-07:00","id":849320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849172#post849172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indicating what your character and you find interesting and important? For example, as a storyteller in a more freeform story, I could present my players with some issues with Invictus, with someone messing in their feeding grounds, and with one of their touchstones getting human problems you could easily help with (given your newfound power). If you only take an Aspiration to fix one of these problems, I know that that kind of story interests you and others - not so much (or at least not as much as that one)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you need Aspirations to be mechanized for that, though? Why wouldn't your players just tell you which is more interesting? Or see by their actions which they prefer?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849192#post849192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps we can work from the other end: figure out how you want the Ventrue to act, then write a flaw that encourages that behaviour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I have grown fond of what I said earlier--the idea that they are more prim and proper. That they have to basically follow a code of behavior to stay who they are, or they descend rapidly into madness and/or the beast. So, you end up with Ventrue that follow codes of conduct super strictly. They act with decorum and deliberate thought to prevent degeneration. And I'm fond of the &quot;mad lords&quot; concept from 1e.<br /> <br /> So, I think my houserule already sort of works. They are trying extra hard not to lose any Humanity, because they are both less likely to hold on to their humanity, and there is an extra consequence to it--they might lose their minds. So, they act very carefully to avoid detachment, which, well, makes them detached. They have, like, regimented appointments with humans to avoid missing the 2 week deadline or whatever, they drive carefully to avoid surviving a car crash. They speak politely to avoid angering people and starting fights where they might kill. They feed carefully to avoid frenzy, which can lead to detachment rolls.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of them being detached because they fear being detached. Their dealings with humans become businesslike to avoid provocations that could lead to detachmnt, which makes them feel cold and weird to humans. <br /> <br /> I supposed I could do this with some kind of obsession for planning or, I don't know. I feel like doing it with a specific condition might be too pigeon holing.<br /> <br /> If anything, I think it's the Gangrel flaw that bugs me, now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849225#post849225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why bring it up? It seems to have the seeds of a good Venture flaw. Venture are tied to a goal at all times. Willpower can only be spend in pursuit of the goal. They just can't bring themselves to invest in what isn't a goal. Throw in Willpower refresh only upon goal completion (or a milestone) and suddenly all Venture are driven by nature, being completely despondent in loss and exuberant in victory! (It would also model the idea that the Ven always win: It doesn't help them win but it does add a cost to pursuing hopeless goals. Better attach yourself to the winning horse than back the underdog unless you have a trump card.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a cool idea for a clan flaw, honestly, but I don't want to add a whole subsystem to make that work. It also doesn't totally fit my vision of Ventrue. I think lots of people have them being in charge at the forefront of their minds, and I just don't, and never had. Dominate is the reason they get what they want, but I never thought of them as being especially driven to rule, just that Dominate made it easier to do so. To me, other clans were usually in charge, actually, with Ventrue backing. I think I've only ever had one Ventrue prince in all of the NWoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849272#post849272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am pretty sure your character does NOT know what will power is and how to spend it and when you get it. It's not like dollar bills in your wallet where you can count them. You dont In character know that you have 6 will power points and that you become depressed and unmotivated when you run out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's definitely a way to know you have/are getting willpower without having a concept of a concrete number of willpower. I wasn't suggesting a character could accurately say &quot;I have exactly 5 moments of awesome to go,&quot; just that willpower was a thing you could feel in general.<br /> <br /> I don't think characters can say &quot;I have 6 health left!&quot; either, but they absolutely have an idea of how hurt they are and they know when their wounds are healed.<br /> <br /> Same with blood--you know generally in character how hungry you are, and you know when you use or gain more blood, even if you can't put a specific number on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849272#post849272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players dont always know what the story teller has in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's your problem. Why would your GM not communicate that stuff to the players? Sounds like a bad GM. Or at least, a group with poor communication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T10:12:01-07:00","id":849330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849320#post849320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a cool idea for a clan flaw, honestly, but I don't want to add a whole subsystem to make that work. It also doesn't totally fit my vision of Ventrue. I think lots of people have them being in charge at the forefront of their minds, and I just don't, and never had. Dominate is the reason they get what they want, but I never thought of them as being especially driven to rule, just that Dominate made it easier to do so. To me, other clans were usually in charge, actually, with Ventrue backing. I think I've only ever had one Ventrue prince in all of the NWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say it: My flaw is about winning, not ruling. Winning is Venture, Ruling is Invictus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I'm not sure if I was included in 'lots of people' or if it was just to clarify you don't see the Venture as default leader-person. To an extent, them not being DLP is backed by both RAW and RAI. They are simply the elite and want people to know it. As that presumes social rungs, with them at the top, they incidentally end up ruling. Or so they say. :P )<br /> <br /> I agree that the 1E flaw seems to work fine for what you are going for. Still want new ideas or is that settled then?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T10:17:40-07:00","id":849332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849330#post849330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to say it: My flaw is about winning, not ruling. Winning is Venture, Ruling is Invictus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I'm not sure if I was included in 'lots of people' or if it was just to clarify you don't see the Venture as default leader-person. To an extent, them not being DLP is backed by both RAW and RAI. They are simply the elite and want people to know it. As that presumes social rungs, with them at the top, they incidentally end up ruling. Or so they say. :P )<br /> <br /> I agree that the 1E flaw seems to work fine for what you are going for. Still want new ideas or is that settled then?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's...settled enough. I am happy enough with it. It isn't perfect, so, I'll take new ideas, but I am satisfied enough that I won't be upset if I get nothing else.<br /> <br /> No, the Gangrel flaw has my eye, now. I discovered that I like clan flaws to be things that mostly don't actually happen, and therefore guide the clan to act in a specific way that avoids the flaw. In order for the Gangrel to avoid their frenzy flaw, they have to maintain their Humanity,which, feels, uh, backwards from their archetype. They were clearly designed to embrace their flaw, rather than avoid it. But, in my ideal situation, they would be bestial because being bestial avoids their flaw in some fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T10:25:31-07:00","id":849335,"title":"","content":"Two problems I see with the 1e flaw is that it doesn't scale with Humanity, and there's no longer a second roll after a failed Degenertion roll to see if you gain a Derangement. You just gain a Condition based on the results of the Breaking Point roll. If I were to try to reproduce the 1e Ventrue flaw in 2e, I'd have them roll Humanity after a failed Breaking Point and on a failure they gain Broken, Fugue, or Madness (player's choice) in addition to the Condition they get for the Breaking Point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T10:39:01-07:00","id":849340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849320#post849320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there's your problem. Why would your GM not communicate that stuff to the players? Sounds like a bad GM. Or at least, a group with poor communication.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like reading a good book... If i knew everything that was going to happen... uh why would i read it?<br /> <br /> Sure with the Ordo example, if my player told me that they wanted to be the king of the ordo and I wasnt planning on having any whatsoever in my game, I would totally tell that player that might not be the best choice. But as a player I sure as heck wouldnt want to know every detail of the story before I played it. It would suck the fun out as well as make any of my in game choices pointless if the story was already set.<br /> <br /> But I realize that there are tons of different play styles and that might be what someone would like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849320#post849320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's definitely a way to know you have/are getting willpower without having a concept of a concrete number of willpower. I wasn't suggesting a character could accurately say &quot;I have exactly 5 moments of awesome to go,&quot; just that willpower was a thing you could feel in general.<br /> <br /> I don't think characters can say &quot;I have 6 health left!&quot; either, but they absolutely have an idea of how hurt they are and they know when their wounds are healed.<br /> <br /> Same with blood--you know generally in character how hungry you are, and you know when you use or gain more blood, even if you can't put a specific number on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, how is doing something to make yourself feel better meta?<br /> Like calling/ hanging out with your bestie (touchstone)--- (Authoritarian) Proving yourself the best? (Junkie) Getting your fix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-18-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T10:58:11-07:00","id":849350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849332#post849332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the Gangrel flaw has my eye, now. I discovered that I like clan flaws to be things that mostly don't actually happen, and therefore guide the clan to act in a specific way that avoids the flaw. In order for the Gangrel to avoid their frenzy flaw, they have to maintain their Humanity,which, feels, uh, backwards from their archetype. They were clearly designed to embrace their flaw, rather than avoid it. But, in my ideal situation, they would be bestial because being bestial avoids their flaw in some fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an idea, but I'm AFB right now. I'll edit this post when I get home.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, here we go: Apply the Humanity penalty to human interaction on rolls to resist Frenzy. Also, Gangrel cannot spend Willpower to hold off Frenzy for a turn. Neither of these apply to attempts to Ride the Wave.<br /> <br /> That should do it. Now, Gangrel are encouraged to be loners (no Frenzy triggers if no one's around) and savages (piss them off at your own risk).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","user":"Justin Sane","date":".  Got home. 03-18-2016, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T11:42:38-07:00","id":849372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849335#post849335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two problems I see with the 1e flaw is that it doesn't scale with Humanity, and there's no longer a second roll after a failed Degenertion roll to see if you gain a Derangement. You just gain a Condition based on the results of the Breaking Point roll. If I were to try to reproduce the 1e Ventrue flaw in 2e, I'd have them roll Humanity after a failed Breaking Point and on a failure they gain Broken, Fugue, or Madness (player's choice) in addition to the Condition they get for the Breaking Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Madness condition is definitely the best way to handle it in the system, actually. I don't really want specific, realistic mental illnesses, really just something wild and unpredictable and weird. Like CWoD Malkavians--not the Fish-Malks, the ones that were actually well played and creepy.<br /> <br /> So, my original idea was giving this condition, Madness, now, I'm pretty sure, on a dramatic failure on the detachment roll. I figured with the -1 sitting there, they'd hit a chance die when they got low enough, but I kind of wasn't thinking and for some reason thought that a chance die just automatically meant a dramatic failure, not a 10% chance for one, so, they'd still be exceedingly unlikely.<br /> <br /> I'm going to talk to the Ventrue player and talk about this. Rolling Humanity after a breaking point roll is literally the old way, yeah. That's definitely an option. I might also pitch to him removing the -1 penalty to detachment, but giving him the Madness condition on a failure. Or keeping the -1 and giving Madness. Or even removing the -1 and getting Madness on a success, so Ventrue have to try extra hard to avoid breaking points at all, since they're screwed when they come up at all. I don't know, I like this line of thinking, I'll have to hammer it out without annoying the player. He felt like his character, in life, was fairly detached from people, so, he saw his character as always struggling with detachment and trying extra hard to avoid it, even when that comes across awkward and stilted.<br /> <br /> He's kind of already playing as I imagine and want Ventrue to feel compelled to act, so, I want something that will reinforce what he's doing, if possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849340#post849340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like reading a good book... If i knew everything that was going to happen... uh why would i read it?<br /> <br /> Sure with the Ordo example, if my player told me that they wanted to be the king of the ordo and I wasnt planning on having any whatsoever in my game, I would totally tell that player that might not be the best choice. But as a player I sure as heck wouldnt want to know every detail of the story before I played it. It would suck the fun out as well as make any of my in game choices pointless if the story was already set.<br /> <br /> But I realize that there are tons of different play styles and that might be what someone would like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you took a rather large leap over the excluded middle there. You can read the jacket of a good book and know, pretty well, if there are, say, elves in it or not, such that, if you are in the mood for a book about elves, you'd read something else, or if you really want to read this specific book, you wouldn't hold out hope for elves to appear in it.<br /> <br /> Players don't need to know all the information about a setting to know that there are no Ordo there. They just need a super basic overview, like, &quot;The Invictus are in power, the Sanctum is their second and integrated. There's a faction of Carthians stirring shit, and a secret cult of Crone the Lance are trying to ferret out. No Ordo exist in the setting.&quot; Done, with just a super short paragraph. You have absolutely no idea what is going to happen (and frankly, as GM, I know less about what is going to happen than the players do, since they drive the story anyway), but you know that you an pursue membership in 4 of the 5 covenants, that a party of Carthians will be causing trouble while Invictus will be enforcing the status quo, and that the group almost certainly should not contain both an Acolyte and an Anointed. If your GM isn't giving you basic information about the setting, that's an issue. I imagine a setting agnostic character would work in only a very small minority of games. I know I, for example, very rarely set up cities with all 5 covenants present. Most of the time, it's just 2-3, maybe 4.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849340#post849340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how is doing something to make yourself feel better meta?<br /> Like calling/ hanging out with your bestie (touchstone)--- (Authoritarian) Proving yourself the best? (Junkie) Getting your fix?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it comes down to Masks and Dirges being too much like caricatures of how people act, rather than reflecting real people. I don't think there are two specific activities that make people feel good, I think they feel good from a ridiculously wide range of things. So, saying, only these two things make you feel good, is offputting and weird. It becomes meta, because the character should feel good from doing more than that. Like I said, a real person who feels self-affirmed cracking jokes doesn't feel self-affirmed for cracking a joke at a funeral (or other inappropriate situation, they just feel awkward and weird). It's not realistic. It's distiling a character into digestible chunks. It's highlighting their strongest quirks. It's something that's important in short duration media, like, say, TV shows, or even stand-alone movies, so you can quickly identify what broad archetype the character falls into and process it as such. It's a shortcut that purposefully limits the depth of the character to make it easier to understand and follow.<br /> <br /> Now, that kind of thing works great in, like I said, TV or movies. It works for people who want to play a story game, where the group of players gets together to tell the best, most interesting, most dramatic story possible, because you are not worried about verisimilitude, just drama. It doesn't work for people who play for other reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":". 03-18-2016, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T12:42:14-07:00","id":849398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848446#post848446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I am noticing that. In the past, WoD games were always my favorite, and I explained to people that, while the books constantly insisted they were storytelling/narrative games, they absolutely weren't. They were some of the best simulation around. I mean, seriously, nothing with a weight lifting chart is a story game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I love parts of 2nd edition. Mostly, the changes to the disciplines, merits, and combat. 1st edition combat was, oh crap, terrible. I often called it a murder system, not a combat system. You just tried to go first and throw enough dice to one shot the other guy. Yuck. So, the game is way better balanced now. But, I'm starting to notice all those nonsense claims about being a storytelling/narrative game are, well, starting to get backed up. And those are the mechanics I'm noticing that I dislike, honestly. I'll probably be sticking to 2e and pulling most of those storytelling things out.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a former champions player who has taken heat on these forums for suggesting there is a need for mechanic to deal velocity damage that should be there when vamp hits some at high speed regardless of the discipline causing the speed, I found this funny.<br /> But you are right that it has become even more story oriented than before. I just wouldn't call the previous version simulationist.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848797#post848797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not my job, or anyone else's, to police whether or not they're being true to character. I trust that they are because they're my players, and that's that. It's up to them to be true. If they say they'd do X in Y situation, they would. For me to tell someone they're playing a character they invented wrong would be ridiculous, as far as I'm concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a Paladin back stabbing and robbing in game not an issue with you?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848797#post848797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a cool way to handle them, but even that wouldn't apply to me, really, because I don't actually prepare anything for sessions before hand, I just react to what the players are doing. I don't actually ever need to know their goals, I just need to know the actions they're taking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is an example. I used play Rune quest which is a Bronze age world where everyone has some magic.Iron is that worlds adamantium. It is literally God Bones. Oh You want some for a weapon but damn rare.<br /> <br /> Well they came out with ritual enchantment rules for metals for all the cults. All the warrior cults had rules for Iron and another metal. In my cult's case silver. Sun worshipers it was gold etc.<br /> So all the players on their own realized hell Iron is super rare so we we decided to pursue the other metals. So we began training in game to learn craft silver or gold etc. To learn enchantment.<br /> To learn the spells we wanted in these weapons. Planned how to get enough metal to make the weapons etc. We had about a season worth of goals to occupy us in game. Of course this a going we were also adventuring. Then the gamemasters swapped out(we did that a lot). And the new gamester just decided to gives all Iron weapons in game.<br /> <br /> He was surprised by our disappointment. Sure took them . But he did not understand that he just wipe about a seasons worth of goals and questing for the entire group who were gearing to enchant personal weapons.<br /> <br /> All because he did not pay attention to our goals.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848797#post848797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With: The session starts and you know your character wants to find a Haven. So, your aspiration is &quot;Acquire a Haven.&quot; You start working on that goal, then, half way through the session, an old friend calls you up. He needs help with something! Hmm, now you have to weigh helping your friend (for no reward other than helping a friend) or getting your Haven, which you still want to do, and getting a beat. In fact, if you can get the Haven and the beat quickly, you might be able to add a &quot;help your friend&quot; aspiration and get another beat out of it. Hmmm, tough decision. Your friend needs help, but, damn, a beat is awesome. It can feel to some, in fact, that you are being punished by helping your friend, rather than following through on the thing you wrote down at the beginning of the session. However you choose, though, you're thrown from immersion because you are now weighing a meta resource your character has no way to know about (a beat) against actual in character relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the thing Aspiration can be long term or short term. General or Specific. You don't have to resolve any of them in three weeks of play it is just a nice way to reward the players for doing something they should be pursuing anyway. Just because a long term goal is on the sheet doesn't mean you can't help the clanmate who is in the crisis of the week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848797#post848797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you can gear up effectively with Obfuscate, but then, you basically can't break Obfuscate until a fight starts, which severely limits your options. Fights are dangerous and not usually stuff you should be going out looking for, especially given how easy they are to escape now that you can't realistically one-shot people anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touch of Shadow is your friend on this.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848797#post848797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an animal. It started out as a tool. Property destruction isn't on the list anymore, so, animals don't count anywhere on the chart. I'm sorry if you're an animal person or something, in which case, you might feel differently, but as far as I'm concerned? No, not an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he is treating the dog like an object or a tool then it isn't a touchstone. Yeah I'd be hitting up with detachment rolls. Yes I know you sad it was not a serious attempt at the rules . More on that in a minute.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=848797#post848797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why you wouldn't know that it might bother you to see someone eating your favorite food until you see it. That doesn't make a lot of sense to me. If it'd be a breaking point for you, I am pretty sure even just the thought of it might get you worked up a bit. You might not be constantly aware, but if someone invites you to your favorite restaurant from life, and going there and watching them eat would be a breaking point, I am positive that you would know right away, when they extended the invitation, that accepting is going to be uncomfortable. You won't go there totally fine and then be like, &quot;Oh crap! I forgot I don't eat!&quot; I don't see that happening. That would require someone who was remarkable self-unaware.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deckerd- from Blade Runner</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Replicants weren't suppose to have feelings, Neither were Bladerunners.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the curse is that you get used to being inhuman. Then one day something you done countless nights before hits you how bizarre it would be if you still breathed.<br /> Or how something you used to do like breaking bread with your friends is now alien to you. You either deal with it or you take a hit on your humanity.<br /> <br /> Rolling for detachment is for those moments when your character notices just how inhuman he has become. It then he must decide how he feels about that. Does it bother him ? or does he just shrug? So no you don't hit everytime he see a group eating but when it is a dramatic or story worthy point.<br /> <br /> But even then I suspect that is not your style.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to hacking humanity. There were two humanity hacks in first edition that might work.<br /> <br /> Hell is other people, a system where each dot represented an NPC . They could be friends, old rivals, the guy that runs the news stand etc. But the relationship had to be maintained and the curse got in the way.<br /> <br /> But I don't think that would work with your group from what I can tell. Not with this story at least.<br /> <br /> The other system would be atrocity dice. I liked atrocity and it would be a bit of a hack to work it into 2nd edition but it might work for.<br /> Atrocity was a measure of how monstrous your are becoming. You temporary dice and if you didn't deal with it could accrue to permanent dice.<br /> Not unlike dissonance and discord in In Nomine.<br /> <br /> If the player had atrocity dice, the ST could ask to replace some of his dice pool with atrocity dice(say red dice). If any of the successes came up on the atrocity dice, the action reflected your monstrous nature slipping thru somehow. It was an interesting system. There is more too it. But that is what I remember off the top of my head.<br /> It is in Danse Macabre. But like I said it take hacking.<br /> Perhaps clan flaws don't kick in until you have permanent atrocity for example<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","user":"Chattnos","date":". 03-18-2016, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T12:47:15-07:00","id":849401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849372#post849372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because you are not worried about verisimilitude, just drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>People can walk and chew bubblegum at the same time. : ) I've played a lot of Sim-based WoD, and have had a great time. But I also enjoy concepts like themes, archetypes, setting conceits. Doesn't mean verisimilitude gets tossed out and that I don't care about it when I put those other things in. I can feel one thing as a player and not let it interfere with how my character feels. I can appreciate and enjoy something bad happening to the character, or hardships happening to the character without feeling like I'm betraying the character's hopes or anything. At this stage in my gaming, I don't think I'd enjoy a story driven by all dramatic and no realistic decision, any more than one driven by all realistic and no dramatic decisions. <br /> <br /> Also, the Mask/Dirge All Willpower &amp; Single Willpower comments in the book are <i>starting points</i>. RAW is using those as a baseline, not as the only way to indulge. Same with Breaking Points. Same with Conditions. They aren't the exhaustive list it seems you might be taking them for with the <i>only feeling good from two things</i> point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T13:05:57-07:00","id":849413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849398#post849398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Paladin back stabbing and robbing in game not an issue with you?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not for me. But it might be for the player when they lose their Paladin powers. They're not roleplaying <i>wrong</i> as much as playing a character that's bad at being a Paladin. If they want to do that, ok, go right ahead, though I know I would never want to. I want to immerse in successful characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849398#post849398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the gamemasters swapped out(we did that a lot). And the new gamester just decided to gives all Iron weapons in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the problem with swapping game masters without swapping games, or settings, or whatever. I don't think it's someone who didn't pay attention to the character goals--he gave you your goals: iron weapons. It's just someone clueless about people wanting to earn what you get, or having wasted time. The point is, there are deeper issues there.<br /> <br /> I won't be swapping out with another GM--nobody else is going to run this city this way. And I won't be randomly handing out iron weapons..or, well, actually, technically, the administration of the city will probably be doing that because of the changelings, but I digress. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849398#post849398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the curse is that you get used to being inhuman. Then one day something you done countless nights before hits you how bizarre it would be if you still breathed.<br /> Or how something you used to do like breaking bread with your friends is now alien to you. You either deal with it or you take a hit on your humanity.<br /> <br /> Rolling for detachment is for those moments when your character notices just how inhuman he has become. It then he must decide how he feels about that. Does it bother him ? or does he just shrug? So no you don't hit everytime he see a group eating but when it is a dramatic or story worthy point.<br /> <br /> But even then I suspect that is not your style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I see what you're saying as <i>a </i>take on Humanity, not <i>the </i>take on Humanity. I just don't see it that way. It could be my own personal view on introspection and self-analysis getting in the way, but, I just don't see why you couldn't already know how you feel about this stuff. <br /> <br /> For me, it's more like cognitive dissonance, and how strongly you still believe you're basically human. A vampire with Humanity 6 rolls when they're in a car crash. If they fail, they just fully recognize, embrace, are ok with, etc., the fact that they can survive car crashes without fear. In the future, they're not going to care about car wrecks. They can survive that. No problem. A vampire that succeeds is completely freaked out and terrified of the fact that they just lived through a car crash. It's a miracle, not &quot;duh, right, I'm dead.&quot; They will still always buckle their seat belts and drive with caution. It's still scary.<br /> <br /> A vampire with Humanity 8 is in denial. They're totally human, of course. They have some cool powers, but, no, they're human. They see someone eating food, and, roll. On a success, &quot;Oh, yeah, that's...cool. I can still do that. No problem. I'm still human. I mean, I just don't want to eat. I have an upset stomach. I eat something else, but it's really no different. I mean, I have to throw up, but I can still make myself taste and whatever. No...I'm still human.&quot; Or, if they fail, &quot;Hmm...that's right, I can't eat. Well, ok, so, I'm not the same. Weird.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not about drama, it's about measuring how inhuman you feel. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849398#post849398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell is other people, a system where each dot represented an NPC . They could be friends, old rivals, the guy that runs the news stand etc. But the relationship had to be maintained and the curse got in the way.<br /> <br /> But I don't think that would work with your group from what I can tell. Not with this story at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no thanks. Like I said before, I like Humanity the way it is. I don't know why people keep thinking I want to change it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849398#post849398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other system would be atrocity dice. I liked atrocity and it would be a bit of a hack to work it into 2nd edition but it might work for.<br /> Atrocity was a measure of how monstrous your are becoming. You temporary dice and if you didn't deal with it could accrue to permanent dice.<br /> Not unlike dissonance and discord in In Nomine.<br /> <br /> If the player had atrocity dice, the ST could ask to replace some of his dice pool with atrocity dice(say red dice). If any of the successes came up on the atrocity dice, the action reflected your monstrous nature slipping thru somehow. It was an interesting system. There is more too it. But that is what I remember off the top of my head.<br /> It is in Danse Macabre. But like I said it take hacking.<br /> Perhaps clan flaws don't kick in until you have permanent atrocity for example</div> </div> </div> </div>So, when I read Danse Macabre way back, I remember looking at Atrocity Dice and thinking, &quot;LOL No. Hell no. This is ridiculous!&quot; And just never pursuing it at all. I'll go re-read it now, because I absolutely don't remember <i>why </i>that was my reaction, so, I'll give it a shot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T13:17:47-07:00","id":849420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849413#post849413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, no thanks. Like I said before, I like Humanity the way it is. I don't know why people keep thinking I want to change it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because touchstones are a HUGE part of humanity. Because banes are a part of humanity. Breaking points are a huge part of humanity. Perhaps this thread has devolved so far from what you had intended that we are all arguing circles. <br /> <br /> <br /> I think your group should homebrew whatever works for your people and have fun. But arguing RAW and RAI isnt really working here. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Side note: I would totes have issues with a paladin robbing and stabbing because fundamentally a paladin wouldnt do that and the player should reevaluate their character.. make some meta changes. And if you didnt have a problem with it, you wouldnt punish them for doing it.. like taking away the paladin powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T13:20:21-07:00","id":849421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849413#post849413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about drama, it's about measuring how inhuman you feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a counterpoint, that slow descent into inhumanity? Yup, that's drama <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T14:49:39-07:00","id":849465,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; Side note: I would totes have issues with a paladin robbing and stabbing because fundamentally a paladin wouldnt do that and the player should reevaluate their character.. make some meta changes. And if you didnt have a problem with it, you wouldnt punish them for doing it.. like taking away the paladin powers. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> It's not the DM's place to say you can't stab that person because you're a paladin, it's the DM's place to enforce the rules that explicitly state that a paladin who does an evil act immediately loses their paladinhood. It's certainly probable that paladins could go around robbing and stabbing people within the setting because if there was some mystical godforce that just intervened and froze time to prevent it from happening, then there would be no such thing as fallen paladins and blackguards. It's no different than saying &quot;Oh, you failed your detachment roll, so you lose a dot of Humanity and gain the Bestial or Wanton condition.&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T14:50:20-07:00","id":849467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849320#post849320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you need Aspirations to be mechanized for that, though? Why wouldn't your players just tell you which is more interesting? Or see by their actions which they prefer?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I've been avoiding this thread's tangents for a bit, I think there's an issue where.<br /> <br /> The line of, &quot;Why do you need X to be mechanized?&quot; is pretty much always a non-starter in RPG design. Need is never the question, because in theory the right group doesn't need mechanics at all. The design assumption is always, &quot;Why would you <i>want</i> X to be mechanized?&quot; because the assumption is that people buy and use RPGs because they want mechanics; not need them.<br /> <br /> Now, the answer to why people would want Aspirations mechanized are clearly unsatisfying for you, but they're pretty simple: it encourages a player-ST feedback of communicating character goals and giving opportunities to fulfill them, as well as making it more fair for how character goals interact with social mechanics (aka when to give modifiers as characters make social approaches that align or work against things like Aspirations and Virtues/Vices).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:09:04-07:00","id":849515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849420#post849420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because touchstones are a HUGE part of humanity. Because banes are a part of humanity. Breaking points are a huge part of humanity. Perhaps this thread has devolved so far from what you had intended that we are all arguing circles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it has devolved, I don't know. I like banes and breaking points just fine. Frankly, I love the Banes. I just (learned during this thread that I) don't like touchstones. That's it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849420#post849420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your group should homebrew whatever works for your people and have fun. But arguing RAW and RAI isnt really working here.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I actually enjoy arguing RAW and RAI, but, I don't actually think that was happening here. I think what's going on is that I said I didn't like this particular kind of mechanic (which we are identifying as story-game mechanics, but that's not necessarily the best term), and I listed examples of it that I did not like. In this case, specifically, I mentioned touchstones, Mask/Dirge, Aspirations, beats, and the doors system. I think a lot of people are then extrapolating that I must dislike these other systems they identify as story-game mechanics, but that I don't. So, there's a lot of confusion, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849420#post849420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side note: I would totes have issues with a paladin robbing and stabbing because fundamentally a paladin wouldnt do that and the player should reevaluate their character.. make some meta changes. And if you didnt have a problem with it, you wouldnt punish them for doing it.. like taking away the paladin powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, the GM, have no problem with the paladin doing anything he wants. His actions are not up to me. However, Paladins (I assume we're talking about D&amp;D) get holy power from their god by following a code. When they break that code (and robbing/backstabbing generally breaks that code), their god has a problem with it and takes their powers away. That's the key distinction. I don't care about the robbing, his god does. As the GM, it is not my job to punish players for playing wrong, it is my job to keep the world running in a logical fashion. In D&amp;D's case, the world is set up so that logically, a paladin will lose their powers when they break their code, so, it is my job to act as this god and take his powers away. But I am dispassionate about it. I don't care one way or the other. I'm just keeping the setting going to its logical conclusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849421#post849421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a counterpoint, that slow descent into inhumanity? Yup, that's drama <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It might be something that leads to drama, but it is not a mechanic that directly manipulates the &quot;story&quot; in any way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849467#post849467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The line of, &quot;Why do you need X to be mechanized?&quot; is pretty much always a non-starter in RPG design. Need is never the question, because in theory the right group doesn't need mechanics at all. The design assumption is always, &quot;Why would you <i>want</i> X to be mechanized?&quot; because the assumption is that people buy and use RPGs because they want mechanics; not need them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. My point was that it might cause a conflict of interest. If it was needed, however, I would still leave it in despite the risk. Since it's not needed, why risk it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849465#post849465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the answer to why people would want Aspirations mechanized are clearly unsatisfying for you, but they're pretty simple: it encourages a player-ST feedback of communicating character goals and giving opportunities to fulfill them, as well as making it more fair for how character goals interact with social mechanics (aka when to give modifiers as characters make social approaches that align or work against things like Aspirations and Virtues/Vices).</div> </div> </div> </div>So, personal opinion, I think that sort of thing belongs in the GM advice chapter, rather than as rules. But, yes, I know why other people like this stuff and I don't begrudge them it, I just find it unnecessary myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  typo 03-18-2016, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:11:41-07:00","id":849516,"title":"","content":"I feel like part of the problem is revealed in you claiming mask and dirge are just two actions which regain willpower. They aren't. They are far broader than that. A jester doesn't just get WP from cracking jokes. Though, for the record, I see absolutely nothing wrong or forced about a vampire cracking a joke during a funeral if that's their coping mechanism. Might be socially crass, but there are people that handle stress with humor, and this isn't out of place or unrealistic. But a Jester gets WP for pointing out absurdities and flaws and not taking things seriously. That's more than just jokes. They also gain willpower for wit and cunning.<br /> <br /> These only seem like caricatures because you reduce them to a single action and assume that players will or are expected to do this one action any time they use WP. They are broad character archetypes, and any action that fits them earns WP. And any action that falls in line with them can be justified instead of forced by a decent roleplayer. Ideally, these actions should just happen in the course of play because Mask/Dirge are core parts of the PC's personalities and the WP regeneration is less a carrot and more just a simulation of what such self-affirming actions do for the psyche. But even if your players are the sort to only RP for the sake of regaining WP, the actions they take should and will be perfectly IC if you use Anchors according to RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:35:12-07:00","id":849529,"title":"","content":"Jester doesn't get Willpower back from cracking jokes at random anyway. You have to make an observation that lightens the tone of the scene by pointing out absurdities in it. Telling a Knock-Knock joke won't do it. It has to be relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:58:11-07:00","id":849547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849529#post849529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jester doesn't get Willpower back from cracking jokes at random anyway. You have to make an observation that lightens the tone of the scene by pointing out absurdities in it. Telling a Knock-Knock joke won't do it. It has to be relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am fond of hyperbole as a rhetorical device. <br /> <br /> I will say, though, in response to the insistence that mask/dirge are broad character archetypes, my copy of Blood and Smoke says, &quot;Each anchor has two conditions that give willpower recovery.&quot; Two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T18:24:54-07:00","id":849559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849516#post849516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like part of the problem is revealed in you claiming mask and dirge are just two actions which regain willpower. They aren't. They are far broader than that. A jester doesn't just get WP from cracking jokes. Though, for the record, I see absolutely nothing wrong or forced about a vampire cracking a joke during a funeral if that's their coping mechanism. Might be socially crass, but there are people that handle stress with humor, and this isn't out of place or unrealistic. But a Jester gets WP for pointing out absurdities and flaws and not taking things seriously. That's more than just jokes. They also gain willpower for wit and cunning.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;We're gathered here because <b>someone </b>couldn't stay alive (Despite having been dead for 200 years already).&quot; *Gives the coffin a dirty look.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T18:45:37-07:00","id":849565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849547#post849547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say, though, in response to the insistence that mask/dirge are broad character archetypes, my copy of Blood and Smoke says, &quot;Each anchor has two conditions that give willpower recovery.&quot; Two.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtR2e: p84<br /> <br /> <b>Mask and Dirge Archetypes</b><br /> <br /> Here are numerous sample archetypes for your characters\u2019 Masks and Dirges. Feel free to pull from this list, or come up with your own. Each includes a brief description, and <i>sample actions</i> that could recover Willpower for each. Note that the risks and costs listed should always be meaningful. They should have value in the story, to count as Willpower conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T19:52:22-07:00","id":849580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849547#post849547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I am fond of hyperbole as a rhetorical device.<br /> <br /> I will say, though, in response to the insistence that mask/dirge are broad character archetypes, my copy of Blood and Smoke says, &quot;Each anchor has two conditions that give willpower recovery.&quot; Two.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to Holy's response, look at the actual Mask/Dirge sections for the &quot;two actions&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire the Requiem 2e pg 84</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any time a vampire overcomes a small hurdle in defense of<br /> her Mask, she gains a point of Willpower. When committing<br /> atrocious or existentially risky acts in defense of her Mask, she<br /> regains all her spent Willpower points.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire the Requiem 2e pg 84</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any time a vampire withdraws from his outside life in<br /> defense of his truer self, he gains a point of Willpower. When<br /> committing terrible, damning acts in defense of his personal<br /> identity, he regains all his spent Willpower points.</div> </div> </div> </div>The actions listed under the archetypes themselves are just examples of how you'd fulfill the above conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T20:50:01-07:00","id":849596,"title":"","content":"Ok. It feels kind of silly just typing a post saying I was wrong about one thing, but, I mean, I'm not sure how else to respond. That doesn't suddenly make me like the mechanic, though. I still don't, I just have one less thing to say negatively about it, I guess?<br /> <br /> Oh, and I re-read Atrocity Dice in Danse Macabre. I will echo my memory of my initial reaction: &quot;Oh, hell no!&quot; That whole subsystem is a story-game mechanic. No aspect of it is something I want. People around the table evaluate the scene to assign it. You add it to pools when it's dramatically appropriate. It's also always bad. You can't avoid the penalty at all (you can cope with lost humanity, but not with atrocity, it always comes into play). You can't get rid of it. It's just, no, thank you. About the only thing appealing about it is that it counts up instead of down, which is really minor in the end. Now, I'm not saying I don't appreciate the suggestion, just, this is not one for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T06:54:42-07:00","id":849695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849596#post849596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. It feels kind of silly just typing a post saying I was wrong about one thing, but, I mean, I'm not sure how else to respond. That doesn't suddenly make me like the mechanic, though. I still don't, I just have one less thing to say negatively about it, I guess?<br /> <br /> Oh, and I re-read Atrocity Dice in Danse Macabre. I will echo my memory of my initial reaction: &quot;Oh, hell no!&quot; That whole subsystem is a story-game mechanic. No aspect of it is something I want. People around the table evaluate the scene to assign it. You add it to pools when it's dramatically appropriate. It's also always bad. You can't avoid the penalty at all (you can cope with lost humanity, but not with atrocity, it always comes into play). You can't get rid of it. It's just, no, thank you. About the only thing appealing about it is that it counts up instead of down, which is really minor in the end. Now, I'm not saying I don't appreciate the suggestion, just, this is not one for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you can lose temporary atrocity there was a way to bleed it off and if you was using the then optional bane system you could lose some as well by taking a bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T11:11:57-07:00","id":849805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849596#post849596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. It feels kind of silly just typing a post saying I was wrong about one thing, but, I mean, I'm not sure how else to respond. That doesn't suddenly make me like the mechanic, though. I still don't, I just have one less thing to say negatively about it, I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div>The aim to calling your attention at your personal blunder of reading comprehension isn't to make you instantly like something, but to show you how you're miss-representing those (in almost 10 forum pages already).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T13:53:57-07:00","id":852576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=849515#post849515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it has devolved, I don't know. I like banes and breaking points just fine. Frankly, I love the Banes. I just (learned during this thread that I) don't like touchstones. That's it.<br /> <br /> So, I actually enjoy arguing RAW and RAI, but, I don't actually think that was happening here. I think what's going on is that I said I didn't like this particular kind of mechanic (which we are identifying as story-game mechanics, but that's not necessarily the best term), and I listed examples of it that I did not like. In this case, specifically, I mentioned touchstones, Mask/Dirge, Aspirations, beats, and the doors system. I think a lot of people are then extrapolating that I must dislike these other systems they identify as story-game mechanics, but that I don't. So, there's a lot of confusion, I guess.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, its a been a few days since I've been on here. But i think i can help clear this up a bit.<br /> <br /> Let's break down the discussion a bit. You (The Storyteller) have made three definetlive statments that reflect on this:<br /> <br /> 1) You dont like story-mechanics (for the defiention in this thread)<br /> 2) You don't like Mask/Dirge/Anchors/Touchtones/etc.<br /> 3) You DO like Humanity as written.<br /> <br /> Now, this is creating cognitive dissonace in some people, becuase, as Vitalis sort of pointed out, for a lot of us Humanity is a story-mechanic just like the ones you don't like. There are then two obvious possibilites here:<br /> <br /> 1) You are misunderstanding the ones you don't like (Mask/Dirge)<br /> 2) You are misunderstanding the one you DO like (Humanity)<br /> <br /> EDIT: I understand that 'misunderstanding' seems harsh, and you can of course play it the way you want, but as you have said yourself, your play style seems to be atypical for these forums and the stated intent of the writers and devs.<br /> <br /> The two main threads that have been going have been each of these. It is an effort to understand and help, really it is. It is just difficult when there is such a disconnect in understanding about some of the mechanics and their purpose. There are of course other possible reasons for you to like and dislike the above mechanics, just that those two are the most direct and obvious for this group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:05:37-07:00","id":852585,"title":"","content":"I think this thread illustrates very well why the narrativism/gameism/simulationism divide is waffle. Some folks like some mechanics. Some folks don't like other mechanics. Lots of folks want to be able to label and categorize the things they like and don't like, so it feels more objective. But ultimately, it's still totally subjective which mechanics fit into which category, so the categories themselves just end up causing confusion when people say things like &quot;I don't like story game mechanics&quot; and then everyone has a different idea of what &quot;story game mechanics&quot; means, and we end up giving advice on how to fix mechanics that the person never actually had a problem with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-24-2016, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:01:20-07:00","id":852798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=852576#post852576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, this is creating cognitive dissonace in some people, becuase, as Vitalis sort of pointed out, for a lot of us Humanity is a story-mechanic just like the ones you don't like. There are then two obvious possibilites here:<br /> <br /> 1) You are misunderstanding the ones you don't like (Mask/Dirge)<br /> 2) You are misunderstanding the one you DO like (Humanity)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's #3: Humanity is partially a story mechanic and partially something else, and I can very easily ignore the part I don't like and still enjoy it overall. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But really, I'm not sure how this disconnect ever occurred. I mean, look, I do want people to understand what I like. I certainly learned about what I liked in this thread. But, I never asked about Humanity. I never suggested I didn't like it. Was it just mentioned how surprised I was that Humanity was so much more forgiving than it used to be? Because I'm ok with that...I even prefer it, since the moments that call for detachment are so much more impactful without it happening left and right over minor crap, like, picking pockets or something like in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  Added some stuff for clarity 03-25-2016, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T11:08:14-07:00","id":853579,"title":"","content":"So, this thread is basically dead, and that's fine, no need to further respond, but I thought this was the best place to share an awesome experience I had in my game this past week that exemplifies why I like Humanity.<br /> <br /> The group attacked a bunch of drug dealers protecting a stash in their territory. Three of the four who made it to the game had Obfuscate 1, and the fourth had Majesty, so she talked her way close, then everyone attacked. It was brutal. In the end, two thugs were bleeding out dying, two had surrendered and were led into the storage lockup for holding until they sorted out what to do, and the fifth, a ghoul, was being interrogated. Most of the party was hungry at this point, and some tough decisions had to be made. They actually tried to pin and drink the ghoul, but amazing, desperate rolls on his part prevented it, while he successfully pleaded for his life, offering to trade information about the vampires running things if they let him go.<br /> <br /> After that was settled, one character was sitting over the dying men, contemplating whether she wanted to murder them or not, since they were probably going to die anyway. She was basically talking out loud to herself. &quot;It's a mercy, right? They're going to die anyone, so it's ok?&quot; She ended up choosing not to kill them, but as a result, she's going to be imminently hungry and at risk of frenzy (she's sitting at 5 blood).<br /> <br /> Another who had just barely held off a frenzy during the fight since he was actually hungry (he ended up with only 3 blood) asked the group's grappling specialist to hold on to him while he drank one of the conscious guys. In case he frenzied, he wanted the other guy to hold on to him and prevent him from killing him off. He managed to fight it off again and dominated the guy to forget what happened.<br /> <br /> The fourth needed to drink as well, so, he forced the final guy to take some of the hallucinogens they were dealing so he wouldn't remember what happened while he drank.<br /> <br /> Everyone rolled for detachment. Nobody died (the only guy not hungry even moved the bodies and called 911 so they could get help), but there was still impassioned violence all around, and most of them hurt people for blood. But, they all succeeded, and everyone felt awful about it. It was such a great moment when we talked about it and they were like, &quot;I can't believe I just had to debate whether I was going to mercy kill someone or not.&quot; &quot;Yeah, well, I needed someone to hold me as assurance in case I flipped out and murdered someone.&quot; &quot;I just drugged a guy so I could eat him and he wouldn't tell anyone...&quot; It was deep and awesome.<br /> <br /> That's why I love Humanity. Without it, nobody would have cared about what happened. They would just would have killed the guys for expediency and walked away with their information not giving a damn about their condition or, well, anything but themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  Clarity 03-26-2016, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T12:28:08-07:00","id":853614,"title":"","content":"That's definitely an awesome experience, thanks for sharing! Those sort of moments are some of the coolest and most dramatic in Requiem (and CofD in general, but this particular example is pretty vampire-specific).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:28:55-07:00","id":860533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=847989#post847989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no no. Do forgive. I quoted you because I agreed with your statement about what they were for and such.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot; Perhaps your PCs dont care about the touchstones because... ( please do not take this as rude or anything as it's not meant to be.. ) Because you do not care for them? It gives your players mixed signals. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> The words ^ were for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8\" data-vbnamecard=\"8\">Storyteller</a> who posted the question. It seems he does not like them, so perhaps his players might not. I have run into that with other things as a story teller. I say my dislike for something, then suddenly my players are suddenly shying away from druids.. or mages. Or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I was confused for a moment. I, Storyteller, and The Storyteller are two different gents, hehe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have been thinking about requesting permission to change my name. Might look into that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T18:06:49-07:00","id":860680,"title":"","content":"Oh so sorry. Tagged the wrong guy! My apologies. <br /> <br /> probably a good idea for a name change<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T22:03:11-07:00","id":895912,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with the touchstone/anchor system that it simply makes becoming a Draugr much more inevitable than say becoming a wight in Masquerade because eventually your touchstones will die which serves as the ultimate breaking point to descend into draugrhood which makes the 'immortality' of the vampire pretty much pointless.<br /> <br /> However though I'm not really a big fan of the personal horror themes of both games while works in theory but in practice, they're kinda impractical for their own reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-22-2016, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T23:30:17-07:00","id":895945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=895912#post895912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest problem with the touchstone/anchor system that it simply makes becoming a Draugr much more inevitable than say becoming a wight in Masquerade because eventually your touchstones will die which serves as the ultimate breaking point to descend into draugrhood which makes the 'immortality' of the vampire pretty much pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's still nowhere near inevitable.... Just make sure you always have at least two and remember to replace dead ones, and even if your last touchstone dies you can still regain that humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T23:48:55-07:00","id":895952,"title":"","content":"As a note, if you are worried about touchstones dieing though it is less common a place can be a touchstone. Like the church you went to as a boy that you still attend every sunday. Maybe not for morning mass but you still can be found within it each sunday. It is a reminder of who you were, the family you had and through it you are still linked to the community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T23:56:48-07:00","id":895954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=895952#post895952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note, if you are worried about touchstones dieing though it is less common a place can be a touchstone. Like the church you went to as a boy that you still attend every sunday. Maybe not for morning mass but you still can be found within it each sunday. It is a reminder of who you were, the family you had and through it you are still linked to the community.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I don't wish to play as a religious person or anything like you described but however though the biggest problem of all that all those will disappear eventually due to urban planning and other things.<br /> <br /> Which I wonder if it's best to do without touchstones which would be less troubling baggage to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-22-2016, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T00:17:51-07:00","id":895960,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11735\" data-vbnamecard=\"11735\">spaceharrier72</a> the religious tones were just because churches are often some of the oldest buildings in many towns and the center of a community and though they are still at risk of one day being destroyed their life span compared to a standard person is far greater. Touchstones ground you in your humanity and though it may be an added it of baggage I feel it does add some further depth to humanity. Of course, what works for your game works for your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T06:32:36-07:00","id":896053,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11735\" data-vbnamecard=\"11735\">spaceharrier72</a> - your &quot;decent into draugrhood&quot; is only assured if one assumes that no one ever buys up Humanity. There's always been the assumption that vampires spend time and energy remembering what its like to be a human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T07:47:41-07:00","id":896081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=895960#post895960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11735\" data-vbnamecard=\"11735\">spaceharrier72</a> the religious tones were just because churches are often some of the oldest buildings in many towns and the center of a community and though they are still at risk of one day being destroyed their life span compared to a standard person is far greater. Touchstones ground you in your humanity and though it may be an added it of baggage I feel it does add some further depth to humanity. Of course, what works for your game works for your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well what about a character who has never attended a church in their entire lives? Or a character who stopped going to church before they were embraced? Just because a church is a &quot;center of a community&quot; doesn't mean everyone attends one you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-22-2016, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T09:06:51-07:00","id":896107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896081#post896081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well what about a character who has never attended a church in their entire lives? Or a character who stopped going to church before they were embraced? Just because a church is a &quot;center of a community&quot; doesn't mean everyone attends one you know.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't know if you're meaning to, but it seems like you're coming off rather agressive here. The church was suggested simply because they're some of the oldest buildings around. Old buildings that are notoriously resistant to change. That's all. This is merely an example. If you really don't like it, then we can look at the core book's suggestion of a tombstone or obituary as a Touchstone. I can see some vampires taking really old trees as Touchstones as well. <br /> <br /> And it doesn't matter if someone didn't attend the church. Hell, we could have someone raised an fantatical anti-theist and moved to a new city where they were Embraced, and still take the church as a Touchstone because they empathize with certain humanizing features of it, as well as its age. Well, its unlikely to happen, but touchstones are flexible enough for it to work. What is important is the psychological impact on the vampire, reminding them that they are still, in part, human, and to remind them what it means to be human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-22-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T09:18:55-07:00","id":896110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896107#post896107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't know if you're meaning to, but it seems like you're coming off rather agressive here. The church was suggested simply because they're some of the oldest buildings around. Old buildings that are notoriously resistant to change. That's all. This is merely an example. If you really don't like it, then we can look at the core book's suggestion of a tombstone or obituary as a Touchstone. I can see some vampires taking really old trees as Touchstones as well.<br /> <br /> And it doesn't matter if someone didn't attend the church. Hell, we could have someone raised an fantatical anti-theist and moved to a new city where they were Embraced, and still take the church as a Touchstone because they empathize with certain humanizing features of it, as well as its age. Well, its unlikely to happen, but touchstones are flexible enough for it to work. What is important is the psychological impact on the vampire, reminding them that they are still, in part, human, and to remind them what it means to be human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean to sound aggressive, it's just that I think I may have been mistakenly thinking that such things had to be shoehorned in which kinda troubled me especially regarding the character concept I would wish to play whom wouldn't need to bother with them.<br /> <br /> Now it would probably be interesting to use touchtones in a more flexible manner like observing human life especially they change over the centuries and the Vampire adopting to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-22-2016, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T09:44:10-07:00","id":896118,"title":"","content":"Understood. I was just afraid that your feelings on the matter were making you miss that this was just an example, not an absolute. I see that happen a lot.<br /> <br /> Touchstones generally are living people. I suspect that holds true because people make better NPCs, and can lead to better stories, than just an unfeeling material. Touchstones are supposed to bring in conflict for your characters - how you can lose it, how you can protect it, how you react to it being threatened. These are things you go to great lengths to protect. So, in a real way, these should have a measure of fragility to them, but as the result of outside threats rather than simple age. Out of the fifteen example touchstones, two are places rather than people, but they still have troubles associated with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-22-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:01:01-07:00","id":896125,"title":"","content":"To be honest, touchstones sound like one of those &quot;protect the base&quot; missions from video games which is rather troublesome.<br /> <br /> Well let's just say I'm not a big fan of the touchstone system, is there any way to ditch it completely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:36:17-07:00","id":896149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896125#post896125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, touchstones sound like one of those &quot;protect the base&quot; missions from video games which is rather troublesome.<br /> <br /> Well let's just say I'm not a big fan of the touchstone system, is there any way to ditch it completely?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are not &quot; protect the base&quot; missions. Perhaps you are looking at them wrong. This thread went in circles and circles about them. Think about this... Does your vampire have a best friend from the human world you like to call and Just BS with?<br /> A mother? A family member? Perhaps a child you want to look over still? Something that reminds you of what you used to have. Used to be.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's going out with that old co-worker once a month to drink beer at hooters and watch the game...<br /> maybe you have fallen in love with your ghoul and you go to &quot;sleep&quot; every morning listening to their heart beat when they sleep in your arms... You were human.. now you're not, but maybe... just maybe these things can help you from spiraling out of control... slipping into the darkness...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Those things are your touchstones. No you do not have to be with them 24/7. No you do not have to call them every 10 minutes. No you dont have to text them 100 times a night.. Most people who play this game have a touchstone ... they just might not have labeled it so...<br /> <br /> <br /> They are just there...you care about them... You worry when they lose their job. Or get their first car. Or your daughter is going to prom. You worry that your enemy might take your ghoul ... they give you something to care about. Ground you in humanity. If you care, then you could lose it.. and that brings conflict. And conflict is what makes a story. Without it.. it's rather dull... <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 05-22-2016, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:08:34-07:00","id":896168,"title":"","content":"Here's another thing to consider...<br /> <br /> What if you embraced someone who was a drifter (like a homeless person and such) or someone who doesn't have or want anything to do with their family when they were alive nor they have no friends either? What's their touchstones going to be then? I can't see how this is going to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:23:37-07:00","id":896181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896168#post896168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another thing to consider...<br /> <br /> What if you embraced someone who was a drifter (like a homeless person and such) or someone who doesn't have or want anything to do with their family when they were alive nor they have no friends either? What's their touchstones going to be then? I can't see how this is going to work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So you have created someone who doesnt give a shit about anything at all?<br /> <br /> A you spiral out down into the depths of darkness because you have nothing to ground you to humanity. You become the beast. Breaking points get no +2 for touchstones. Drugar here we come.<br /> <br /> B You as a player stop putting up road blocks, because everyone cares about something....<br /> <br /> Perhaps your touchstone becomes your sire. You look at him every day and remember what he took away from you. Your life. Your heart used to beat, now it doesnt because of him. Even hate is caring.. You look at him and say.. I never want to be that monster. If he would do that, then I wont.<br /> <br /> your sire's ghoul... He/she takes care of you and has taught you things that you never new were possible.<br /> <br /> The first person you fed off. You screwed up bad, now you feel guilty. So you check in on them once in a while?<br /> <br /> The place you were turned. You go back there on occasion to remember what you had, what you were..<br /> <br /> ( to pull from the resources thread) You take on a job at Walmart for resources.. You connect to your boss...<br /> <br /> I dont see why even a drifter cant find something to care about .....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 05-22-2016, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:29:01-07:00","id":896184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896181#post896181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So you have created someone who doesnt give a shit about anything at all?<br /> <br /> A you spiral out down into the depths of darkness because you have nothing to ground you to humanity. You become the beast. Breaking points get no +2 for touchstones. Drugar here we come.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is where the biggest problem with Requiem comes in and especially it goes back to my main point that becoming a Draugr is much more inevitable because even if you did cared, your touchstones will eventually die and everything from your mortal life will eventually disappear which your character will eventually stop caring which leads to sooner or later becoming a Dragur eventually and there's no way to stop it. This is why I find the whole touchstone system to be problematic and impractical which is like the Sword of Damascus hanging over you which will eventually drop even if it'll take a thousand years but it's still going to happen no matter how long you keep postponing it which makes the game bleak and pointless.<br /> <br /> So last question, is it possible to completely drop the touchstone system and not use it? Or might as well just ditch humanity system all together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-22-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:35:23-07:00","id":896188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896184#post896184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is where the biggest problem with Requiem comes in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically you just dont get the +2 to keep your humanity. <br /> <br /> It makes perfect sense... If you truly dont care about anything.. Nothing at all. Why is it a problem to become the beast? <br /> <br /> -is confused- <br /> <br /> did you not read the 5 other valid examples of a touchstone for a drifter character?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:46:12-07:00","id":896196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896188#post896188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes perfect sense... If you truly dont care about anything.. Nothing at all. Why is it a problem to become the beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because once you hit humanity 0, your character practically becomes unplayable because they're now a mindless monster and you have to turn in your character sheet as they're now a NPC under control of the ST therefore not only you loose the game but also punishes you for not playing it in a certain way. I have a feeling that is what according to Requiem's logic all Vampires are destined to become eventually as if they never were meant to be playable at all in the first place but rather to be as NPCs all along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-22-2016, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:52:52-07:00","id":896201,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11735\" data-vbnamecard=\"11735\">spaceharrier72</a> the church was just the first thing to come to mind. I'm not religious but I recently made a character who was a priest and tries to maintain thier faith post embrace. Religious aspects of it don't matter, what matters is how it helps them relate to humanity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Touchstones provide built-in conflict for every character.&quot; So I'm going build on your estranged vampire who hasn't seen his family since he'd left home and never was one to make friends. There is a single item he owns but never wears. that like him will never see the light of day. His father's pocket watch, the only thing he has to remember the bastard and he can't manage to get rid of it. He had stolen it to pawn it off once he reached the city but necer could manage to do it. This piece of junk reminds him of everything he'd run from and shows that even now his life or unlife is better than it was. <br /> <br /> Inner conflict. <br /> <br /> Or if you want to draw horror from your example I can easily do that. The pc that embraced the drifter npc thought it'd be wise to embrace someone without connections, someone who wouldn't be missed. Without anything to ground him this drifter embraces the beast and casts of his humanity. He was powerless but now he is powerful. Why should he hide? Why should he care? Humans are cattle and nothing more. A monster like him has nothing to fear from cattle.<br /> <br /> Also as others have said it is possible that your ghoul can be your touchstone. It doesn't have to be something from their time alivery but something that links them to humanity. <br /> <br /> You also sound like you are worried about these touchstones being targeted. On one hand it is part of the struggle. &quot;A rival vampire learns you still care for your little sister and you must stop them before they reach her.&quot; Could be a valid hook that'd lead to possibilities either way it resolves. However on the other hand to worry about these weaknesses as you seem to I assume you have had to deal with sts or dms who were &quot;vs players&quot;. If this is the case I understand. There is a reason why it's a trope that dnd characters are orphans, so their family can't be dragged into the story against them. If you can trust your gm however remember that at its core these game lines of the chronicle of darkness are horror. By having such weaknesses in your character a more dynamic story can unfold.<br /> <br /> Despite all this though, you seem to be trying to convince 'us' of something that may not apply to us as what we are saying may not apply to you. In the end, you'll play what works for you and we will play what works for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:00:18-07:00","id":896205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896125#post896125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, touchstones sound like one of those &quot;protect the base&quot; missions from video games which is rather troublesome.<br /> <br /> Well let's just say I'm not a big fan of the touchstone system, is there any way to ditch it completely?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a rather gross simplification of the matter. Vampire isn't a vide game where violence is always the answer. Or, rather, it is a potential answer, but one that will drive you fruther and further into being an inhuman monster, and thus often undesirable. Vampire is a game about the push and pull of monstrocity and humanity, dark and light, saint and sinner.<br /> <br /> But if you really don't like the touchstones, then... just don't have scenes with them. Or detach the touchstone through humanity loss and don't buy a new one. Its that simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896168#post896168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if you embraced someone who was a drifter (like a homeless person and such) or someone who doesn't have or want anything to do with their family when they were alive nor they have no friends either? What's their touchstones going to be then? I can't see how this is going to work.</div> </div> </div> </div> The game assumes that you have friends, family, relationships you care about, not that you're a wandering sociopath without attachments. Stone faced sociopaths that don't care about others aren't really meant to be played in this genre.<br /> <br /> But, lets say you do make Mr &quot;I am an Island.&quot; Vitalis covered how to make Touchstones without connection to your mortal life. I'm going to say, if you don't want Touchstones... then just take the penalty and play. Losing humanity isn't necessarily a <i>bad </i>thing. So what if you suffer some social penalties - you're Mr Island, you don't care about others. Majesty and Dominate replace the need for social rolls when you need to convince someone to do something anyways, or you can just Obfuscate away from the problems. Vampire is built in a way that using Disciplines allows you to bypass the need to rely on mundane rolls, but at the cost of acting like a monster. If you don't care about human connections, then just embrace the monster. That's a valid way of playing the game too. After a point, you'll stabilize, and you can keep on playing without worry of becoming a Draugr. <br /> <br /> I mean, seriously. Do you have any idea how difficult it is to hit Humanity 0? One decade active without human contact. Heinous, spree, or mass murder. Killing your Touchstone. Diablarie. You don't have a touchstone, so you can't kill it. Going a full decade without human contact is kind of hard to pull off for most beings, considering you need them for food. So, just don't go on a killing spree or diablarize someone. Problem solved.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, where is this idea that Touchstones dying leads to draugrhood? I dont' see it. Sure, <i>killing</i> your touchstone is a humanity breaking point; hunger and anger frenzies happen, thought Touchstones can talk you down from them. But the Touchstone dying of old age or disease isn't a suggested breaking point, and I wouldn't put it at Humanity 1 even if I wanted it to be a breaking point in the first place. So, is this entire thing just a misreading of the rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-22-2016, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:00:47-07:00","id":896207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896201#post896201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;11735&quot;]&quot;Touchstones provide built-in conflict for every character.&quot; So I'm going build on your estranged vampire who hasn't seen his family since he'd left home and never was one to make friends. There is a single item he owns but never wears. that like him will never see the light of day. His father's pocket watch, the only thing he has to remember the bastard and he can't manage to get rid of it. He had stolen it to pawn it off once he reached the city but necer could manage to do it. This piece of junk reminds him of everything he'd run from and shows that even now his life or unlife is better than it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the character I'm thinking of is actually female and this is why you need to be becareful not defaulting to male characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:06:39-07:00","id":896208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896207#post896207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the character I'm thinking of is actually female and this is why you need to be becareful not defaulting to male characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throw an s infront of every he and it fits then. English lacks a truely nutrel pronoun. Sure they, them and it fit but they aren't grammatically correct and it sounds so cluncky to use those repeatability. Gender in this context doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:12:08-07:00","id":896210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896205#post896205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The game assumes that you have friends, family, relationships you care about, not that you're a wandering sociopath without attachments. Stone faced sociopaths that don't care about others aren't really meant to be played in this genre.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first of all I wouldn't use the word &quot;sociopath&quot; which is a ablest term coined in the 1930s to highlight the supposed \u201cdamage\u201d severely mentally ill people caused to society which portrays the mentally ill as menaces to be put away and abused and tortured during hospitalization.<br /> <br /> All that boils down to is simply playing a character with no attachments at all they don't never had anything in their lives since they're drifters and they just happened to be embraced as Vampires and are trying to survive or maintain their immortality the long as they can.<br /> <br /> But let's just say if did you tried to apply such a character you've described though, you're telling me that they 'don't exist' nor is it even possible to have such characters just because the genre says you can't play one or even have one as a NPC? If the game has to assume I have to play as a certain character then it really becomes restricting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-22-2016, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:27:05-07:00","id":896215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896210#post896210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well first of all I wouldn't use the word &amp;quot;sociopath&amp;quot; which is a ablest term coined in the 1930s to highlight the supposed \u201cdamage\u201d severely mentally ill people caused to society which portrays the mentally ill as menaces to be put away and abused and tortured during hospitalization.<br /> <br /> All that boils down to is simply playing a character with no attachments at all they don't never had anything in their lives since they're drifters and they just happened to be embraced as Vampires and are trying to survive or maintain their immortality the long as they can.<br /> <br /> But let's just say if did you tried to apply such a character you've described though, you're telling me that they 'don't exist' nor is it even possible to have such characters just because the genre says you can't play one or even have one as a NPC? If the game has to assume I have to play as a certain character then it really becomes restricting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The inability to feel empathy is a genuine medical problem. Please do not take it so lightly. It is something that some truly struggle with and may be offended by downplaying it's existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:32:42-07:00","id":896216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896215#post896215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The inability to feel empathy is a genuine medical problem. Please do not take it so lightly. It is something that some truly struggle with and may be offended by downplaying it's existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the inability to feel empathy is more of a privilege and entitlement problem than a medical one, since mentally ill people are more likely to harm themselves than others while the so called &quot;perfectly normal&quot; person is perfectly capable showing no empathy and can harm others due to their entitlement over everything (perfect example would be domestic abusers who abuse which eventually kill and murder their girlfriends/spouses in a alarming rate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-22-2016, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:41:23-07:00","id":896224,"title":"","content":"People misuse psychopath and sociopath all the time, and there are modern definitions at play. Irregardless of the semantics of the word choice, however, human beings without any connections are generally implausable without severe mental issues. Humans are social animals, and the game takes place within the framework of a city or town. Its completely implausable that a connectionless drifter somehow ends up Embraced - the transformation into Kindred costs the sire. Why would someone without connections be Embraced in the first place? Why would they want to? Childer are investments.<br /> <br /> The only reason to make such a character is the desire to play a D&amp;D-style murder-hobo that can't be hurt through loved ones. And that is not the mindset that Vampire was intended to be played in. This is called the Social game for a reason - because the challenges are designed to be social challenges. Politics, making friends and allies, living and dealing with the family you were born to. Humans are meant to be both your food and your dates and night outs. These social challenges form the core of Vampire games.<br /> <br /> But if someone tried to play one? Sure, they can exist. And I already told you how they can be played - they'd be a low Humanity monster that relied on Disciplines to get through the night. That's a valid way of playing too, just not one I'm interested in and one that the game isn't designed to support as a PC long term. Not because you can't play it, but because the sheer lack of plot involvement makes them boring. <br /> <br /> Also, as a side effect on how beats and Conditions work, playing this kind of character gains XP slower than someone who fully throws themselves into both human and undead society, which ironically makes them weaker in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:44:38-07:00","id":896228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896216#post896216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the inability to feel empathy is more of a privilege and entitlement problem than a medical one,</div> </div> </div> </div> No, there is a genetic component that leads to the brain underdeveloping the parts that enable empathy. This is a scientific fact. In theory you can have social issues without a genetic component that lead to lack of empathy, but there absolutely are people who are genetically inclined to lack empathy for others.<br /> <br /> Nature and nurture are so intertwined that its very difficult for me to believe that there's a purely social reason for almost anything. Your genetics create a boundry that you can develop into, and your environment creates the direction you grow. Your environment cannot make you grow in a direction your genetics won't allow, however. Not without brain damage or lots of chemicals/drugs to make alterations to your body, but that's beyond the scope of our discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-22-2016, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:54:13-07:00","id":896233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896224#post896224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People misuse psychopath and sociopath all the time, and there are modern definitions at play. Irregardless of the semantics of the word choice, however, human beings without any connections are generally implausable without severe mental issues. Humans are social animals, and the game takes place within the framework of a city or town. Its completely implausable that a connectionless drifter somehow ends up Embraced - the transformation into Kindred costs the sire. Why would someone without connections be Embraced in the first place? Why would they want to? Childer are investments.<br /> <br /> The only reason to make such a character is the desire to play a D&amp;D-style murder-hobo that can't be hurt through loved ones. And that is not the mindset that Vampire was intended to be played in. This is called the Social game for a reason - because the challenges are designed to be social challenges. Politics, making friends and allies, living and dealing with the family you were born to. Humans are meant to be both your food and your dates and night outs. These social challenges form the core of Vampire games.<br /> <br /> But if someone tried to play one? Sure, they can exist. And I already told you how they can be played - they'd be a low Humanity monster that relied on Disciplines to get through the night. That's a valid way of playing too, just not one I'm interested in and one that the game isn't designed to support as a PC long term. Not because you can't play it, but because the sheer lack of plot involvement makes them boring.<br /> <br /> Also, as a side effect on how beats and Conditions work, playing this kind of character gains XP slower than someone who fully throws themselves into both human and undead society, which ironically makes them weaker in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the character I would preferably play defiantly won't fall under the &quot;Family Man&quot; context at all but rather, I think I prefer to play as a hobo/drifter/squatter characters....<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896228#post896228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, there is a genetic component that leads to the brain underdeveloping the parts that enable empathy. This is a scientific fact. In theory you can have social issues without a genetic component that lead to lack of empathy, but there absolutely are people who are genetically inclined to lack empathy for others.<br /> <br /> Nature and nurture are so intertwined that its very difficult for me to believe that there's a purely social reason for almost anything. Your genetics create a boundry that you can develop into, and your environment creates the direction you grow. Your environment cannot make you grow in a direction your genetics won't allow, however. Not without brain damage or lots of chemicals/drugs to make alterations to your body, but that's beyond the scope of our discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any evidence or proof to back up your claims?<br /> <br /> I'm sorry but I often don't accept Hard Sciences because I often find them sketchy at best. After all I have a suspicion that is part of with the media sympathizing with white male murderers saying that they're &quot;mentally ill&quot; as a way of ignoring what actually causes their murder spree in the first place which is their entitlement and privilege that no one wants to acknowledge which meanwhile our society turns around and automatically calls black male murderers &quot;thugs&quot; or arab male murderers &quot;terrorists&quot; because of you know institutionalized racism in our society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-23-2016, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T12:56:47-07:00","id":896236,"title":"","content":"Not sure if you two ( MCN and Mr. Fix ) have noticed. But I dont think there is an actual question here. For every valid point that we make about having a touchstone, it is dismissed with extreme or vague situations.. or with something utterly unimportant like criticizing which pronoun was used. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:02:22-07:00","id":896241,"title":"","content":"Or just ignoring huge portions of replies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:07:04-07:00","id":896246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896236#post896236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if you two ( MCN and Mr. Fix ) have noticed. But I dont think there is an actual question here. For every valid point that we make about having a touchstone, it is dismissed with extreme or vague situations.. or with something utterly unimportant like criticizing which pronoun was used. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am having a hard time deciding if they are trolling or trying to pick apart opinion through usage of straw men arguments or other such tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:10:49-07:00","id":896249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896246#post896246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am having a hard time deciding if they are trolling or trying to pick apart opinion through usage of straw men arguments or other such tactics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the latter might be the most accurate but maybe I am ignorant towards this game and I maybe making up baseless conclusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:18:16-07:00","id":896255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896208#post896208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throw an s infront of every he and it fits then. English lacks a truely nutrel pronoun. Sure they, them and it fit but they aren't grammatically correct and it sounds so cluncky to use those repeatability. Gender in this context doesn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think &quot;he&quot; was a perfectly acceptable pronoun to use in this context, I just had to mention this cause it's a bugbear of mine. They as singular pronoun is not gramatically incorrect in English. It has been used that way as far back as the 14th century, as part of Middle English.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is part of a common trend of people rejecting Morality/Integrity stats as a mechanic. For how often I see people complaining about draugurdum (or whatever gameline-equivalent loss state) being inevitable, I have never actually seen it occur in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:47:04-07:00","id":896280,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> hu, I've always been told that it was improper grammar. I've had people argue that they can not be singular even. Could you possibility pass on your sources? Though I doubt it'd help itd be nice to provide proof for my stance which yes is counter the post in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:52:00-07:00","id":896284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896280#post896280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> hu, I've always been told that it was improper grammar. I've had people argue that they can not be singular even. Could you possibility pass on your sources? Though I doubt it'd help itd be nice to provide proof for my stance which yes is counter the post in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singular_they\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/My_pronoun_is_THEY_-_International_Design_in_Government_Day_at_Code_for_America_Summit_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-My_pronoun_is_THEY_-_International_Design_in_Government_Day_at_Code_for_America_Summit_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singular_they\" target=\"_blank\"> Singular they - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singular_they\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singular_they </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wikipedia itself is not the most reliable source, but the article is replete with sources from credible authors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T14:42:54-07:00","id":896313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896249#post896249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the latter might be the most accurate but maybe I am ignorant towards this game and I maybe making up baseless conclusions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> some what related.... Somewhat not at all... I hope some get the analogy.<br /> <br /> When the Twilight craze was happening. I was teaching 9th grade English. So many people loved that movie. so many people hated it. I would hear so many things like &quot; I hate it because vampires sparkle&quot; So they judged it all on the fact that they sparkle. So everything else written was just stupid. Or the other way people loved it simply because it had a vampire who was in love with a human. I my class would get into huge literary debates over Team Jacob or Team Edward. Who was better.. ect.. Do you know how many of them actually READ the book? or WATCHED the movie? maybe 50% for watching and perhaps 10% for actually reading it... So they would base their entire opinion on what someone else who had heard something from someone else had said...<br /> <br /> So I actually read through everything... all 4 of those dreadful books and I hated almost every moment of it, but now.. Now I know. I have solid first had knowledge of what it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T15:56:49-07:00","id":896362,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm going to take a leap into this on something because I was Internetless for most of it:<br /> <br /> The idea that the homeless, or drifters, in society don't have social connections is horribly inaccurate. It strikes me as silly to complain about ableist language, while perpetuating rather pernicious stereotypes about people that don't have a roofs over their heads on a reliable basis.<br /> <br /> &quot;Drifters&quot; require social interactions for their mental health as much as any other human. Which means they have Touchstones like any other human beings; even if in different circumstances. If you like to play &quot;drifters&quot; do it right for the genre.<br /> <br /> As well, losing Touchstones from time happens. Fun fact: You can replace Touchstones. We do this in real life. We lose things that we care deeply about. It leaves holes in us emotionally. We find new things to love to take that place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T19:28:48-07:00","id":896463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>spaceharrier72</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896168#post896168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another thing to consider...<br /> <br /> What if you embraced someone who was a drifter (like a homeless person and such) or someone who doesn't have or want anything to do with their family when they were alive nor they have no friends either? What's their touchstones going to be then? I can't see how this is going to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>IE, what if you went and embraced a murder hobo? Why would you do this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:04:41-07:00","id":896819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896362#post896362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I'm going to take a leap into this on something because I was Internetless for most of it:<br /> <br /> The idea that the homeless, or drifters, in society don't have social connections is horribly inaccurate. It strikes me as silly to complain about ableist language, while perpetuating rather pernicious stereotypes about people that don't have a roofs over their heads on a reliable basis.<br /> <br /> &quot;Drifters&quot; require social interactions for their mental health as much as any other human. Which means they have Touchstones like any other human beings; even if in different circumstances. If you like to play &quot;drifters&quot; do it right for the genre.<br /> <br /> As well, losing Touchstones from time happens. Fun fact: You can replace Touchstones. We do this in real life. We lose things that we care deeply about. It leaves holes in us emotionally. We find new things to love to take that place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you (not sarcastic) for pointing out that blaring obvious point. Touchstones can grow old and die. Or perhaps an illness takes them too soon. That is life. That pain or loss or hole they feel is life. The touchstone is doing what it is intended to do. Perhaps after death the touchstone becomes that person's grave. You tend to it, visit it. all that... When your loved one dies, it doesnt mean you automatically turn into this raving beast.. (drugar) <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896463#post896463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IE, what if you went and embraced a murder hobo? Why would you do this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I already answered what could be touchstones for this &quot;what if&quot; hobo. As far as why the Sire is doing it. There could be a hundred reasons. Here are two: 1 he didnt know the hobo was a murderer (assuming you meant that) and 2 The Sire is also a murderer and he was hoping to murder together.<br /> <br /> Buuuuut Even Murderers have touchstones. example: Dexter. &gt; His sister or his wife or the imaginary father he talked to all the time. Or hell... All of the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T11:54:32-07:00","id":897033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/847552-removing-touchstones-or-at-least-downplaying-them-tremendously?p=896819#post896819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I already answered what could be touchstones for this &quot;what if&quot; hobo. As far as why the Sire is doing it. There could be a hundred reasons. Here are two: 1 he didnt know the hobo was a murderer (assuming you meant that) and 2 The Sire is also a murderer and he was hoping to murder together.<br /> <br /> Buuuuut Even Murderers have touchstones. example: Dexter. &gt; His sister or his wife or the imaginary father he talked to all the time. Or hell... All of the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a rhetoric post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}